window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 86","paragraphs":["The Sea (1)","The sea.","The father of all nature and the starting point of all life.","It was because the sea existed that countless forms of life could emerge, and it could be called the source of water itself.","Any living creature would wither and die without water, which was why the sea was so important.","But as the \"father\" of nature, the sea was also harsh.","Not only was it harsh, but its depths were unknowable.","Someone once said that even if humanity came to understand the entire universe, it would take even longer to fully understand the ocean.","And depending on the rise and fall of sea level, entire regions could become either habitable or uninhabitable.","That was how closely intertwined the sea was with life—and how complex and dangerous it could be.","Whoooosh—","A thought suddenly occurred to me.","It looked like the color you’d get if you melted down a blue sapphire crystal.","There was a smooth sandy beach without any muddy tidal flats, with waves gently washing over the sand.","At first glance, it was an ordinary yet beautiful sea.","The salty breeze and seagulls soaring freely through the sky made everything seem utterly peaceful.","But I absolutely could not let appearances fool me.","Whoooosh!","I turned my head and saw the river connected to the sea.","Strangely enough, the colors were sharply divided, almost as if someone had drawn a boundary separating the river from the ocean.","It was another incredibly beautiful sight.","But the reality was something else entirely.","’...The sea is flowing into the river?’","The sea was where rivers ended.","You could safely say that almost every river eventually flowed into the sea.","At least, that was what I knew as common sense .","I had never heard of the reverse happening.","And now, with my own two eyes, I was watching that common sense get completely shattered.","’This makes no sense...’","Surprisingly, I hadn’t felt all that hopeless when I first encountered the ocean.","Along the way, I had discovered another branch of the river flowing in a different direction, as well as some areas that seemed suitable for exploration.","But the moment I saw seawater flowing backward into the river, my head began to spin.","It felt as though every law of common sense was collapsing.","I even began to wonder whether this could truly be called an environment as I understood the word.","’I should... make sure this is actually seawater...’","My mind had taken enough of a beating that I decided to verify whether this really was the ocean.","The wind carried salt, but maybe it had picked that up somewhere else.","I felt like I wouldn’t be satisfied until I took a sip and confirmed it myself.","\"Blech! Ptooey! Ptoo! Ptooey!\"","It tasted incredibly salty.","And sandy.","Judging from that, this was definitely the ocean.","The occasional waves only reinforced that conclusion.","Title) Guess What I Found After Following the River?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the vast ocean)","(Photo of seawater surging backward into the river)","It was the ocean!","And amazingly enough, instead of the river flowing into the ocean, the ocean flows backward into the river!","Fantasy worlds are so fascinating!","How the hell does nothing but fucked-up shit keep happening to me?!","Do I have to swim across that ocean to escape? Somebody please tell me!","└ Heavenly Demon) What a beautiful sea. But art thou all right? Even through thy words, this Lady can sense thy despair.","└ SwordMaster) Of course he’s not all right. Please learn to read the room;;","└ Heavenly Demon) Was this Lady at fault?","└ SwordMaster) Yes. At times like this, just keep quiet and cheer him on.","└ You can really tell Heavenly Demon has zero social experience;;","└ If she’s actually an old-timer, that makes it even worse. Otherwise, she’s basically just a kid.","└ Surprisingly, there are a lot of nobles like that. They get spoiled rotten growing up and end up completely clueless.","└ Especially if they’re the youngest child born way later than their siblings. They tend to be even worse.","└ Starlight Princess) I’ve never seen an ocean flow into a river before... You’re sure that really is the ocean, right?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. I took a sip just to make sure. It was insanely salty.","└ Starlight Princess) Hmm... Hang in there. I don’t even know what to say.","└ Wild Grylls) There’s no situation where the ocean flows into a river, right?","└ Starlight Princess) Situation or otherwise, something like that is impossible in a world fashioned by the gods. Just what kind of place is the Forest of Four Seasons...?","└ Wild Grylls) Maybe the gods are incompetent?","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero) Don’t blaspheme! The Goddess is absolutely perfect!","└ Wild Grylls) Perfect, my ass lol. The fact that a forest like this even exists already makes no sense.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero) Even so, you shouldn’t insult Her! There must be a reason!","└ Wild Grylls) As soon as I hear that reason, I’ll curse Her the fuck out. Or maybe I’ll just curse Her out anyway.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero) Just stop insulting Her!!!","└ Allfather) An ocean flowing into a river... Could you show me more footage?","└ Wild Grylls) (Video 2 of seawater flowing backward into the river) Want to see more?","└ Allfather) No. That is sufficient. This... Even I cannot explain this. It completely violates the laws of nature, so I have no idea what to make of it.","└ What if the lake and ocean have switched roles?","└ Wait, Grylls. Was the river water salty?","└ Wild Grylls) Nope. Not salty at all. It tasted completely normal.","└ That’s weird in its own way. Why isn’t it salty?","└ This place seriously won’t even let you get close to escaping;;","The gallery erupted into chaos.","Naturally so.","A phenomenon that completely defied the laws of the world had just appeared.","Apparently, even in a world where fantasy and murim coexisted, the laws of nature were still roughly the same.","Well, a world where space randomly twisted around and oceans routinely flowed backward would be completely insane.","There was no way humans could live in a place like that.","Normal really was best.","Title) Just Asking to Make Sure","Wild Grylls","Things like space getting distorted or oceans flowing backward don’t normally happen here, right?","It’s this place that’s weird, right?","└ Nope. If shit like that happened every day, this world would’ve been destroyed already.","└ There are occasionally monsters powerful enough to slice through space itself, but those are exceptions.","└ We have common sense too, Grylls;;","└ Wild Grylls) Thank god.","I had asked just in case.","Everyone agreed that this was abnormal.","Apparently, there were rare occasions when the collision of tremendously powerful forces could distort space, but those were extreme exceptions.","Moreover, most such cases were caused by artificial forces.","For something like this to occur naturally was impossible.","’Putting that aside, this fucking ocean is ridiculously huge.’","All I could see beyond the horizon was more ocean.","Unlike the wide-open horizon before me, my chest felt completely constricted.","What was I supposed to do now?","The ocean was so damn vast that I couldn’t even begin to formulate a plan.","’For now, let’s look around. I need to find some kind of trace.’","Thanks to the river flowing backward, I didn’t have to worry about losing my way.","And since the beach was covered in clean sand, walking wasn’t difficult either.","’I need to be careful. There could be something else weird living here.’","That didn’t mean I was letting my guard down.","For starters, there were far too many suspicious things about this place.","The first was that it was too quiet .","Back at the lakeshore, creatures had constantly been busy fighting among themselves.","The river had been the same.","Right before I arrived here, hadn’t some spotted predator been sent flying through the air?","But this place was unusually quiet, even for an ocean.","’And it’s too clean.’","That was the second strange thing.","The beach was far too clean.","There wasn’t a single trace of any animal anywhere.","At least the lakeshore had small crabs crawling around.","Here, there wasn’t even that.","That could only mean one thing.","Some powerful beast definitely lived here.","Every step I took made me uneasy.","Whoooosh!","’So there’s more than one river.’","Before long, I discovered another river.","Just like the first one, seawater was flowing backward into it.","I followed the river with my eyes and spotted a dense forest far thicker than the one I lived in.","The trees grew tightly packed together, and everything was covered in green.","Calling it a jungle wouldn’t be an exaggeration.","Someday, I might have to go there.","’And it’s not just the jungle.’","The snowy mountains, desert, swamp, volcano, and everything else I had seen across the river.","To find a clue that could lead to my escape, I might eventually have to explore places like those too.","But if I ever reached the point where I actually went into those places, wouldn’t that mean I had already lost most of my hope of escaping?","No matter how much stronger I became by adapting to this forest, those were environments where simply surviving would be difficult.","’I’d basically be going there to die—’","Rrrrrumble!","Just as I was staring at the entrance to the jungle, lost in thought, the ground began to shake.","Nothing good had ever happened whenever the ground started shaking.","I immediately went on high alert.","’Where is it? Where’s it coming from...?’","FWUMP!","As I hurriedly searched for the source of the tremors, something burst out of the ground.","It was mostly red and stretched well above my height.","And then there were the suckers scattered along its surface.","Anyone could tell what it looked like.","An octopus tentacle.","Whip!","\"Aaagh!\"","The octopus tentacle that had erupted from the sand wrapped around my leg and yanked me away.","It happened so suddenly that I nearly dropped both my sword and shield.","Just as the tentacle was about to drag me beneath the sand, I barely managed to slash through it with my sword.","Slash!","The tentacle was severed with ease.","The detached limb trembled violently, perhaps from pain.","In the meantime, I sprang to my feet and readied my equipment.","I could remove the severed tentacle wrapped around my leg later.","FWUMP! FWUMP!","Apparently, losing one limb had seriously pissed the thing off.","Several more tentacles erupted from beneath the sand.","Octopus tentacles writhed in the air like a mass of feelers.","I briefly considered what to do before deciding to break straight through.","Getting out of here came first.","Whoosh!","One of the countless tentacles shot toward me.","This time, rather than trying to grab my leg, it came stabbing down from above.","And it wasn’t like the other tentacles were sitting around doing nothing.","Some stabbed downward from above.","Some swung like whips.","Others tried to wrap around my legs.","The sheer variety of attacks nearly overwhelmed me, but I forced myself to remain as calm as possible.","’Deal with the closest ones first!’","I dodged the tentacle stabbing down from above and barely blocked the one swinging like a whip with my shield.","Finally, I cut down the tentacle trying to bind my feet before it could grab me.","Slash!","A huge chunk of the octopus tentacle was sliced clean off.","The other tentacles flinched, as though the creature could feel the pain.","I seized the opportunity and immediately made a run for it.","If I kept fighting like this, I would eventually be at a disadvantage.","Swoosh!","The tentacles pursued me as I fled.","The severed ones stopped midway because they couldn’t reach any farther, but the others kept coming.","In the end, I had no choice but to fight.","Still, this was much better than being attacked from every direction.","’Dodge, block with the shield, cut with the sword.’","Anything I couldn’t dodge, I blocked with my shield.","Even blocking required quick reactions.","And blocking alone wasn’t enough.","If I couldn’t properly counterattack, I would be trapped in an endless cycle of defending myself.","Every single strike mattered.","But I had the Heavenly Demon Sword.","And I had aura.","Aura in particular allowed me to cut through an area far beyond the sword’s normal reach.","Slash! Slash!","\"Guuuuuuuh!\"","As I repeatedly cut through its tentacles, a strange sound emerged from beneath the sand.","It was probably the creature’s main body screaming in pain.","Served it right.","Swoosh! Swoosh!","Eventually, the creature must have decided it couldn’t win and retreated.","Its tentacles disappeared back beneath the sand.","I panted heavily for a moment before gradually steadying my breathing.","That ambush had nearly gotten me killed in the most anticlimactic way possible.","Fortunately, I had already sensed that something was suspicious and had been prepared.","’But is that thing really an octopus?’","The suckers made it resemble one.","But an octopus living in sand—","’No. Stop thinking in terms of common sense.’","I shook my head.","There was no point.","How many times had common sense already been proven wrong in this place?","I couldn’t rely on it anymore.","An octopus living beneath the sand wasn’t strange at all by this forest’s standards.","’If the land is already like this, what the hell lives in the ocean?’","I turned and stared out at the sea.","The ocean.","The birthplace of all life.","What kinds of monsters could possibly be living beneath those waters?","The thought alone was already terrifying.","But I still had something to do.","’There’s an octopus on this side, so I’ll head the other way.’","Finding a clue that would lead to my escape.","That was my highest priority.","’I’m getting out of here.’","No matter what."]},{"title":"Chapter 87","paragraphs":["The Sea (2)","Every time I looked at the sea, I could think of nothing except how beautiful it was.","If I had come here on vacation, I would have enjoyed myself while taking in the beauty of the ocean.","But just like the forest, the sea was crawling with dangerous things.","It looks like a pristine sandy beach? If anything, that was what warned me of the danger.","Thanks to that, I hadn’t been dragged away by that enormous octopus tentacle.","Even if something looked beautiful on the surface, I could never let my guard down.","There was no telling what might attack me, or when or where. I couldn’t relax my vigilance for even a moment.","The beach is pretty wide.","The sandy beach was fairly expansive. No matter how long I walked, I couldn’t seem to reach the end of it.","What was even more surprising was the location itself. From what I could tell, I was on the other side of the river—in other words, the place where the surroundings constantly changed.","Yet now that I had actually entered this area, there was nothing but sandy beach everywhere, and nothing changed at all.","I even went back just to make sure, but it was the same.","It felt strange.","Is it only the other side of the river that’s weird?","It was strange that space only seemed to distort across the river, and it was equally strange that this place remained perfectly normal.","Everything was so bizarre that I couldn’t make sense of it.","At least I didn’t have to worry about getting lost.","I doubted I’d gain much from wandering around like this. It would probably be better to head back.","\"Hm?\"","I was just about to give up exploring the beach and return when something suspicious caught my eye.","The beach was mostly flat, but there was one spot that had been hollowed out into a depression.","Extremely suspicious.","I wanted to dig around and satisfy my curiosity, but I hesitated.","What if that’s a trap too?","I’d been burned so many times already that I couldn’t bring myself to approach it casually.","What if I got close and something suddenly jumped out at me?","I was worried, but ignoring it didn’t sit right with me either.","Because I was desperately lacking information.","Something even more dangerous might emerge from there later, right?","Gathering information like this little by little would increase my chances of survival.","I made my decision.","It’s just a pit, so I’ll only take a quick peek.","I approached cautiously.","Whatever was in there might be able to sense vibrations like the octopus.","Eventually, while maintaining a safe distance, I craned my neck forward.","It was close, but I managed to see what was inside the pit.","... Eggs?","They were eggs.","Oval-shaped, and absolutely enormous.","Forget comparing them to chicken eggs. They were big enough to rival ostrich eggs.","And there wasn’t just one. Several of them were nestled together.","What kind of eggs are these?","Laying eggs right in the middle of a sandy beach?","What kind of animal would do that in such a dangerous place?","Since I didn’t know enough about this sort of thing, I had no choice but to ask the gallery.","Title) Anyone know what laid these eggs?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of eggs as large as ostrich eggs)","I was walking around when I found this random pit, and there are eggs inside. Anyone know what these are?","└ Heavenly Demon) This one has never seen eggs so large before.","└ SwordMaster) Why are there so many things you’ve never seen?","└ They’re from the Central Plains.","└ People from the Central Plains might know plenty about people, but there are lots of animals they don’t know.","└ There are so many people around there that they don’t know much about stuff like this lol","└ Are you some kind of racist?","└ SwordMaster) Calling me a racist just because I asked one question is a bit much ;;","└ Allfather) The only marine animals I know of that lay eggs on beaches are turtles. I believe those are turtle eggs.","└ Wild Grylls) Turtles?","└ Allfather) Yes. Sea turtles usually lay their eggs like that.","└ Wild Grylls) It should be fine if I take one, right?","└ Allfather) Wouldn’t asking me that be rather pointless?","└ True. Who’s gonna stop you? lol","└ Think of it like when you killed Wonmo’s mother.","└ Wild Grylls) That’s not what I mean. What if I steal one and the mother suddenly pops out? I already went through hell because of an octopus earlier ;;","└ What happened with the octopus? Where’d you find an octopus?","└ Wild Grylls) It came out of the ground. Only its tentacles came out, but it was definitely an octopus.","└ Why the hell would octopus tentacles come out of the ground? lololol","└ There was a monster like that?","└ Of course not lololol. I’m telling you, that place itself is weird.","└ Allfather) Taking an ordinary sea turtle egg shouldn’t cause any major problems. Still, be careful.","Apparently, taking one would be fine.","The moment I saw that comment, I examined the eggs closely.","There were chicken eggs in the auction house too, but I’d never gone out of my way to buy any.","I had no particular reason to, and they weren’t especially appealing.","But for some reason, one I’d found in the wild looked delicious.","I’ll just take one.","Couldn’t one of these eggs cover an entire meal?","I carefully picked up the enormous turtle egg, which was as large as an ostrich egg.","Fortunately, neither a trap nor the mother turtle appeared.","Given its size, it was heavy and cumbersome, but that was fine.","I had a subspace bag, after all.","Should I take one more?","Just as I was about to get a little greedier—","SPLASH!","Suddenly, I heard a violent rush of water behind me.","It wasn’t the sound of waves.","It was the sound of something bursting out of the water.","The instant I heard it, I hurriedly spun around.","\"....\"","... A turtle?","What emerged from the sea was none other than a turtle.","Unlike a tortoise, this sea turtle had limbs that were closer to flippers.","Whether it had seen me steal its egg or not, the sea turtle slowly crawled toward me.","Does it not know?","Just in case, I slowly backed away.","But the sea turtle abruptly stopped, apparently having noticed my presence.","Then it stretched out its long neck and stared directly at me.","Considering the situation, it could probably figure out that I was an \"egg thief.\"","It’s fine. It’s just a turtle.","I didn’t know about tortoises, but sea turtles were extremely slow on land.","If things went wrong, I could just run away.","Or so I thought.","\"Woooooo.\"","The sea turtle made a bizarre sound before pulling its feet into its shell.","Its head remained sticking out, making it look rather ridiculous.","Shhk! Shhk!","What happened next, however, wasn’t ridiculous in the slightest.","Instead of flipper-like limbs, blunt, thick legs like those of a tortoise emerged from inside its shell.","It wasn’t some transforming robot, yet here was a turtle doing something like that. It should have been shocking...","That’s awesome...","It was so absurd that all I could do was stare in admiration.","Now that was evolution in the truest sense of the word.","While the shark giant had looked more like a grotesque monstrosity, the turtle’s evolution actually seemed practical.","Wooooong!","A round sphere of energy began gathering inside the mouth of the turtle, which had transformed from a sea turtle into a tortoise.","I knew all too well what that sphere was.","Hadn’t I already gotten a preview of it from the Guardian?","FWOAAAAASH!","A powerful laser blasted from the turtle’s mouth.","Since I was standing near the eggs, it aimed straight for my head.","Thankfully, I managed to dodge it by twisting my body aside.","KABOOOOM!!","The laser was insanely powerful.","It was definitely stronger than the Guardian’s.","How did I know?","Because the laser had punched a massive hole straight through the cliff.","The sheer destructive power was enough to leave my jaw hanging open.","I’d die even if that thing just hit the ground next to me.","What the hell, was it firing a cannon out of its mouth?","Even the blast radius was huge.","But perhaps a turtle was still a turtle, because its movements were slow and sluggish—","DADADADADA!","Correction.","It was unbelievably fast.","The turtle charged toward me in an instant and leaped high into the air.","Let me repeat that.","It jumped.","Then it pulled all four legs and its head back into its shell.","The end result was a gigantic shell flying straight at me.","As the turtle turned itself into a living boulder and hurtled toward me, I hurriedly raised my shield.","KWA-BOOOOM!!","\"Urgh!\"","Running speed, incredible jumping power, and finally, a rock-hard shell.","Those three excellent qualities combined into one attack, and even though I blocked it with my shield, I was still sent tumbling backward.","And that was despite taking a proper defensive stance.","The impact was terrifying.","\"Ugh...\"","Wooooong!","I was still dazed from the impact transmitted through my shield when I sensed energy gathering in front of me and hurriedly raised my head.","I had no idea when it had stuck its head back out, but the turtle was already gathering energy in its mouth.","Now that it had knocked me far away from the eggs, it apparently intended to finish me off.","Considering the power of the laser I’d just witnessed, my shield wouldn’t stand a chance.","W-What do I do...? Ah!","There was a way.","I rummaged through my subspace bag faster than I ever had before.","The crossbow got in the way for a moment, but I still managed to pull out what I wanted.","\"L-Look at this!\"","I shouted and held up the turtle egg, which was as large as an ostrich egg.","My hands were fairly large, so I could hold it in one hand.","The turtle visibly flinched when I pulled out the egg, clearly taken aback.","The same went for the energy gathered in its mouth. I could see it gradually diminishing.","Soon, the turtle completely dispersed the energy.","Its expression, however, remained murderous.","It glared fiercely at me as though it wanted to tear me limb from limb.","Seeing such an expression on an ordinarily docile-looking turtle...","This whole situation was making me feel like the bad guy.","No. I really am the bad guy.","Not only had I tried to steal a turtle egg, I was now brazenly holding it hostage.","Even objectively speaking, there was no denying that I was the bad guy here.","But I had to survive, didn’t I?","Unlike that turtle, I wasn’t exactly capable of shooting lasers out of my mouth.","I’d do whatever it took to stay alive.","Step. Step.","I slowly backed away while keeping the egg where the turtle could see it.","Every time I took a step backward, the turtle followed me a little farther.","It looked ready to chase me to the ends of hell unless I gave the egg back.","No other choice.","I’d walk all the way to the lower reaches of the river like this, then give it back the egg.","After that, I’d run for my life.","Why not take the opportunity to kill the turtle instead?","Too inefficient.","For one thing, it was nearly as large as a bear.","On top of that, it possessed agility completely unbecoming of something called a turtle.","It’s about time I headed back anyway.","I needed to leave now if I wanted to make it back by dinner.","Once darkness fell, I’d be the one at a disadvantage.","Worst-case scenario, I might never find the cave again.","My top priority was returning safely without getting hurt.","SHWAAAAAA!","As I continued backing away, I eventually reached the mouth of the river where the water flowed backward.","The turtle hadn’t taken its eyes off me once.","As a bonus, its expression was growing angrier by the second.","Now all I had to do was roll the egg back to it and this would be over.","Though if it showed even the slightest sign of attacking, I’d chuck the egg away immediately.","\"... Huh?\"","Right in the middle of our suffocating standoff, something astonishing began happening behind the turtle.","The distance from the mouth of the river to the pit was considerable.","But my eyesight had improved so much that I could see everything clearly.","A flock of birds had appeared from somewhere and was descending toward the pit.","\"Hey! Hey! Look! Look behind you!\"","\"Uwoong?\"","When I frantically pointed behind it, the turtle turned around as well.","In the meantime, the birds began trying to gulp down the eggs like pelicans.","The eggs were so huge, however, that they seemed to be having trouble swallowing them.","\"UWOOOOOOOOOO!!!\"","Naturally, the turtle exploded with rage.","Calling it an explosion wasn’t even enough.","It was more like a volcano erupting.","Then, just as it had done with me, it charged toward the pit at a tremendous speed.","The birds were startled and hurriedly flapped their wings before taking off.","Now’s my chance!","While the turtle rushed back toward the pit, I turned and fled without looking back.","Just in case it decided to fire a mana cannon at me, I even circulated my mana as I ran.","Thanks to that, the surrounding forest flashed past me in an instant, and even the violently rushing river seemed to be flowing slowly.","\"Hehehe.\"","Once I reached a reasonably safe place, I couldn’t help but laugh.","An unexpected find.","An unexpected attack.","And unexpected luck.","The result of it all was the ostrich—","No, the turtle egg sitting inside my subspace bag.","Between the eel and this, it looked like I’d finally get to enjoy some delicacies for a change.","And I’m never going near the sea again.","There was no way in hell I was ever returning to that place."]},{"title":"Chapter 88","paragraphs":["Diary (1)","Title) Got an egg.","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an enormous egg)","Stole an egg. A turtle showed up halfway through and scared the hell out of me, but I somehow managed to bring it back.","I’m having eel for dinner tonight and eating this tomorrow morning.","└ Heavenly Demon) Did you not catch the turtle?","└ Wild Grylls) I didn’t have time, and it was strong, so I gave up.","└ Heavenly Demon) I recommend catching the turtle. I hear turtle is quite delicious.","└ SwordMaster) Have you ever eaten it?","└ Heavenly Demon) There is a dish called yongbongtang . I have eaten one made with turtle before.","└ SwordMaster) Yongbongtang uses softshell turtle, not sea turtle, for crying out loud ;;","└ That’s ridiculous lolololol","└ But don’t quite a few people get those mixed up?","└ A lot do, but the differences are pretty obvious when you actually look at them.","└ Every time I see Heavenly Demon, her ignorance just oozes out of her, seriously ;;","└ Smart Demon) Can’t be helped. She’s spent her whole life focused solely on martial arts. They say you achieve greatness by devoting yourself to one thing, after all.","└ Even so, that’s a bit much ;;","└ Passing Dwarf) You gonna eat that?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. Of course I’m eating it. It’s food I went through hell to get.","└ Passing Dwarf) I wanna try it. Can’t you trade me some for good equipment?","└ Wild Grylls) Sorry. That shark giant stole my fish today, so I don’t have any to spare.","└ Passing Dwarf) Then can you get me one later?","└ Wild Grylls) Hell no ;; That wasn’t a sea. It was a living hell. I barely escaped with my life.","└ Passing Dwarf) Tsk. That’s too bad. Still, give me one if you ever get the chance.","└ Wild Grylls) Do eggs even go well with alcohol?","└ Passing Dwarf) Egg soup for a hangover.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;;","└ Didn’t even think about hangovers lololol","└ Do dwarves even need hangover cures?","└ Of course. Otherwise they can’t work.","I returned after exploring the seaside beach that had been practically indistinguishable from hell.","An octopus tentacle burst out of the sand and wrapped itself around my leg, a turtle transformed, and then it started shooting lasers out of its mouth.","The forest alone was enough of a headache, but knowing the sea was just as insane made me shudder merely thinking about it.","I probably wouldn’t ever go back.","It wasn’t like I needed to cross the sea, so there was no reason to.","The sea itself is full of things even more dangerous than what’s on land....","Just how bizarre was the sea around the Forest of Four Seasons?","Even the shark that had followed the river upstream was a humanoid creature with arms and legs.","The turtle could swap out its legs depending on the terrain too.","I couldn’t even begin to imagine what else might be out there.","For starters, most of them seem pretty intelligent.","Was it because they had evolved, like Allfather said?","It felt as though their intelligence had increased to some degree.","The Sloth and Wonmo were both remarkably good at understanding what I said.","Then there was the turtle, whose expression had instantly turned murderous the moment I showed it the egg.","Overall, they displayed intelligent behavior far removed from that of ordinary animals.","... Then what happens to animals like monkeys or gorillas?","Surely they hadn’t become as intelligent as humans, right?","Something I’d heard on my way to the sea made me even more worried.","That was definitely the sound of monkeys.","A leopard-like animal had suddenly come flying out of the forest and fallen into the river.","It had been a pretty large creature, yet something had sent it flying as if it were nothing.","And from that forest, I’d heard noises that sounded like the cries of monkeys.","\"Haah....\"","I let out a deep sigh.","I suppose this was exactly what people meant when they said there was always another mountain beyond the mountain.","How was I supposed to escape this hellhole?","None of the common sense I’d known before applied in this forest, leaving me completely at a loss.","And since this is another world, even basic common knowledge is meaningless.","I was essentially starting from zero.","The fact that I was only realizing that now meant I’d probably been far too optimistic until this point.","So was I going to give up?","As I’ve emphasized countless times, absolutely not.","Even if it was only out of sheer spite, I was getting out of here no matter what.","And once I did, I’d point a finger straight at God and demand an answer.","Why, out of all the countless places I could have been sent, had He dropped me into this godforsaken hellhole?","What possible reason did He have for sending someone who’d been living a perfectly decent life despite his hardships to a place like this?","Looks like I’ll have to revise my plans.","Now that I’d realized this place was even crazier than I’d imagined, my plans needed to change as well.","Could I hope for someone to come help me?","The gallery was my only option there.","The more I posted about the Forest of Four Seasons, the more everyone wanted nothing to do with it.","Even powerhouses like Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster were asking what kind of insane forest this was.","That said everything.","In other words, I had no choice but to escape entirely through my own efforts, and to do that, I needed to become stronger.","At first glance, that might not sound any different from my original plan.","But one thing had changed.","Not a base, but a shelter. Not merely adapting and surviving, but actually living here. And finally...","A deadline that had become practically unlimited.","Originally, I’d intended to escape this forest as quickly as possible.","But I’d changed my mind.","The Forest of Four Seasons had repeatedly taught me that the more I rushed, the more it forced me backward.","So even if it took a year—or even longer—I would endure.","I would become strong enough that, at the very least, nothing here could threaten me anymore.","And to make that possible, I’ll have to manage things carefully so the gallery never cuts off its support.","My relationship with the head mod, Don’t Abandon the Hero, was especially important.","If I got on their bad side and ended up permanently banned, I’d be completely screwed.","But that didn’t mean I was willing to worship God.","I’d rather die than do that.","I can’t bring myself to lie about it either, so I’ll just have to dodge the subject somehow.","If the head mod ever brought up anything related to faith, it would probably be best to avoid the topic as much as possible.","As I gradually organized my revised plans in my head, I turned to look to the side.","My gaze fell on the barricade, where a gap had been left after the saber-toothed tiger smashed through it.","I should probably ask the dwarf to fix that first.","Come to think of it, I need to be careful that my body doesn’t start changing in some weird direction.","If my body really was gradually evolving to adapt to the Forest of Four Seasons, as Allfather hypothesized, then I needed to steer that evolution in a beneficial direction.","For example, I could greatly increase the amount of time I spent practicing the internal energy cultivation method, guiding my body toward becoming more attuned to mana.","Or I could exercise hard and encourage it to become a body that built muscle more easily.","Maybe a hundred sit-ups, a hundred push-ups, and a hundred squats every day?","It was a workout that reminded me of a certain bald-headed character, except there was no running involved.","Getting cardio around here was simple.","All I had to do was wander around without a care in the world until something attacked me.","Then I’d have no choice but to run for my life, gasping for breath.","I’d rather not do cardio at all if that was the alternative.","Come to think of it, Starlight Princess said she exercises.","I should ask her about it later.","I wanted to know what kind of exercises she did.","If she used equipment, I could ask whether she could help me out.","Simple exercise equipment was sold in the auction house too.","With that thought, I immediately sent Starlight Princess a message.","Now that the trading restriction had been lifted, one-on-one conversations were available again.","She must have been browsing the gallery at the time because she replied immediately.","I smiled with satisfaction at how much livelier she’d become, but only for a moment before getting straight to the point.","[ Wild Grylls: Hello, Starlight Princess. Are you there?]","[ Starlight Princess: Hello! What can I do for you?]","[ Wild Grylls: I was thinking about starting to exercise. What kind of exercises do you usually do?]","[ Starlight Princess: Didn’t you say you didn’t have time to exercise?]","[ Wild Grylls: The Forest of Four Seasons is more terrifying than I expected. I think I need to assume it’ll take at least a year to escape.]","[ Starlight Princess: A year... It sounds like you’ve had a change of heart. I thought you wanted to get out as quickly as possible.]","[ Wild Grylls: I don’t think I can keep myself from breaking otherwise.]","That wasn’t an empty remark. It was the truth.","Hard things were prone to breaking.","So I was making myself flexible enough that I wouldn’t snap.","In my case, I’d extended my deadline to rid myself of impatience.","[ Starlight Princess: I see. I understand how you feel. You haven’t given up hope, have you?]","[ Wild Grylls: If I’d lost hope, I would’ve hanged myself a long time ago.]","[ Starlight Princess: That’s good. No matter what happens, never give up hope. Just as I met you and was completely cured, you might meet someone who changes your fate too.]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you for saying that. By the way, how much exercise do you usually do?]","[ Starlight Princess: It hasn’t been long since I fully recovered, so I’m only doing simple bodyweight exercises. Sit-ups, push-ups, squats, and finally, running.]","...Surely Starlight Princess wasn’t going to turn into that bald guy too, right?","The thought briefly crossed my mind, but I immediately discarded it.","Let’s not waste time thinking about pointless things.","[ Wild Grylls: I see. So you don’t use any equipment?]","[ Starlight Princess: This is my first time exercising, after all. It’s your first time too, isn’t it?]","[ Wild Grylls: Not exactly. I did some in the military.]","The military was an organization where you had to exercise just to properly carry out your training.","Combine that with a regimented lifestyle, and it was practically inevitable that you’d end up in good shape.","Of course, I’d gone back to my old self after leaving the military.","Still, I retained the memories of it.","[ Starlight Princess: Then let’s start with bodyweight exercises together. I’ll even give you some protein supplements.]","[ Wild Grylls: You really don’t need to go that far ;;]","[ Starlight Princess: You don’t need an elixir? All right.]","[ Wild Grylls: Ma’am?]","[ Starlight Princess: I’m not joking. An elixir is a potion that accelerates regeneration. And muscles are...]","Starlight Princess launched into a lengthy explanation.","She even explained the principle behind how muscles became stronger.","Apparently, exercise damaged the muscles, and the body took advantage of the recovery process to rebuild them stronger than before.","[ Starlight Princess: Therefore, my specially made protein supplement drastically speeds up that recovery process. What do you think? Isn’t it amazing? You won’t even get sore muscles!]","[ Wild Grylls: That’s really impressive.]","I had no idea what she was talking about, so I decided to just sit there and applaud.","Apparently, she’d taken the regenerative power of an elixir and focused all of it solely on muscle recovery, so I supposed it really was impressive.","[ Starlight Princess: So drink this after exercising or doing any other kind of training. I’m sure it’ll make you stronger.]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you. I feel like I’m always the one receiving help from you.]","[ Starlight Princess: It’s still nowhere near enough compared to you saving my life. And, Mr. Grylls.]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes?]","[ Starlight Princess: Like I said earlier, never give up hope.]","She had noticed the change in my state of mind from nothing more than our conversation.","She must have sensed something.","[ Starlight Princess: Preparing yourself isn’t a bad choice compared to simply waiting endlessly. But even so, never give up hope. Please.]","[ Wild Grylls: I’ll take that to heart.]","[ Starlight Princess: Ah. While we’re at it, why don’t you start keeping a diary? Writing one helped comfort me too.]","[ Wild Grylls: A diary?]","[ Starlight Princess: Yes. A diary is a way of leaving something behind. It also gives you time to reflect on yourself.]","[ Wild Grylls: Couldn’t I just write in the gallery?]","[ Starlight Princess: But that’s your desires, not who you are as a person, right? I think a diary is what truly reveals a person.]","I quietly stared at Starlight Princess’s message.","A diary.","I fell into thought.","It wasn’t a bad suggestion, but there was something that made me hesitate.","A little while later, I bought a notebook from the auction house and wrote my name in it.","[ Wild Grylls: (Photo of a notebook with the name \"Park Jong-hyeok\" written in it) Do you recognize these letters?]","[ Starlight Princess: I’ve never seen that writing before. I know most languages, but... what country’s script is it?]","[ Wild Grylls: It’s the writing system from the country where I used to live. So it doesn’t exist in this world, right?]","[ Starlight Princess: At least as far as I know, it doesn’t.]","[ Wild Grylls: Tsk. Is that so? That’s a shame.]","As expected, she didn’t know Hangul.","It would have been stranger if she did.","That was why I’d hesitated to keep a diary.","Still, it might not be a bad idea.","I expected to be staying here for a long time.","A diary would undoubtedly become a record proving, I’ve survived this long.","More importantly, I might even be able to use the records in it to predict future events.","Accumulating data one entry at a time and using it to improve my chances of survival.","Not a bad idea.","It didn’t matter if no one else ever knew about it.","I had good people around me, after all.","I could simply think of it as... a hobby to ease my loneliness.","[ Starlight Princess: Um... Mr. Grylls.]","[ Wild Grylls: Yes? Go ahead.]","[ Starlight Princess: Don’t be too heartbroken. I’ll remember you.]","[ Wild Grylls: Huh?]","Wait, what exactly was this woman misunderstanding?"]},{"title":"Chapter 89","paragraphs":["Diary (2)","A tiger leaves behind its hide when it dies, while a person leaves behind their name.","It was a proverb expressing a defining trait of humanity: one should accomplish great things in life and leave behind a name that will shine for generations to come.","Humans possessed the highest intelligence of all animals, but they still retained their instincts as living creatures.","One of those was the desire to leave something behind.","Whether that something was children, a name, or achievements didn’t matter.","There was a reason so many people lived and died for \"honor.\"","After all, one’s honor determined just how great a name one would leave to future generations.","That was how strong the human desire to leave behind a legacy was.","Keeping a diary fulfilled that desire as well.","It might seem childish, but it was actually quite a profound hobby.","People kept diaries for all sorts of reasons, but ultimately, it was an act of \"leaving\" a record behind.","The diaries left by great historical figures, in particular, could possess immense academic value and frequently even reshape our understanding of history.","Even the diary of an ordinary person could hardly be called worthless.","An ordinary person’s diary might seem unimpressive at first glance, but their life was embedded within its pages.","Others could gain wisdom from it or learn from their mistakes.","It had more than enough value.","Did I... say something I shouldn’t have?","Snow-white hair and skin.","A beautiful face and a cold-looking demeanor.","Selena, a woman who had suffered from an extraordinarily difficult-to-treat disease before regaining her vitality with Grylls’s help, was anxious.","Her expression was as cold as ever, but the trembling in her eyes betrayed how she truly felt.","What if I hurt Mr. Grylls by saying that?","Selena understood Grylls’s situation well.","Certain death, and death that could strike at any moment.","There was a subtle difference between the two, but both had one thing in common.","They were intimately close to death.","Thanks to Grylls, she had now been completely freed from the fear of imminent death, but that didn’t mean she had forgotten the terror.","If anything, she knew all too well just how frightening death was.","That feeling that had once seemed capable of driving her insane at any moment.","Although her fear had gradually faded once she entered the stage of \"resignation,\" she still remembered the feeling vividly.","For someone in Mr. Grylls’s situation, keeping a diary is something you’d usually do once you’ve reached the stage of resignation....","Keeping a diary itself was a good thing.","The mere act of leaving something behind had meaning.","But when people close to \"death\" began keeping diaries, it was usually because they had reached the stage of resignation.","Either they were quietly waiting for death, or preparing for a death that might come at any moment.","It was fairly common and, from one perspective, almost like a final desperate struggle.","Did he really come from another world?","The problem was Grylls himself.","Selena carefully studied the photograph he had sent her.","It showed a notebook filled with unfamiliar characters.","Even she, who had mastered numerous foreign languages, had never seen the script before.","Even languages from remote frontier nations often shared similarities.","It was easiest to think of them as dialects of one another.","But the writing in Grylls’s photograph wasn’t a dialect.","It was an entirely new writing system.","If Mr. Grylls really came from another world, then even if he leaves a diary behind... there won’t be a single person who can understand it.","A diary was something people were embarrassed to show others.","Yet, ironically, it was also born from the desire for someone to understand who they were.","If someone truly wanted to keep their secrets completely hidden, they wouldn’t write them down anywhere.","They would simply keep them buried in their heart.","Selena had once written a diary with that same feeling.","Even after her illness had been cured, she occasionally went back and read it.","How sad and miserable must that be?","A legacy that no one would recognize—","No.","A legacy that no one could recognize.","The only legacy he would leave behind would be the posts he had made in the gallery.","If his diary had been written in a language she knew, perhaps she could have inherited it someday.","But because he had crossed over from another world, even if she received his diary, she wouldn’t be able to decipher it.","The best solution would be for Mr. Grylls to teach me his writing system, but...","Would someone struggling just to survive have the leisure for that?","Of course not.","Death was closing in on Grylls every hour of every day.","Hadn’t he told the gallery just today that he’d narrowly escaped death again?","Mr. Grylls helped me out of pure goodwill. I need to repay him in kind.","Selena thought carefully.","How could she ensure that his legacy could be preserved?","Regardless of the maxim about never losing hope, one still had to prepare for every possibility.","She occasionally gave him elixirs or delicious snacks, but that was nowhere near enough.","... All right. I’ll do this.","After a deliberation that felt both long and short, Selena made her decision.","I’ll transcribe everything Mr. Grylls has posted in the gallery and record everything he’s done.","The gallery’s records weren’t eternal.","Just as the dead could no longer speak, the gallery deleted the records of those who died.","If every post belonging to a particular registered user suddenly disappeared, it meant that person had died.","In other words, if Grylls’s posts vanished, it would effectively confirm his death.","If I can’t help him directly, then at the very least, I’ll make sure his death doesn’t go unrecorded.","It was the least she could do.","Selena once again blamed her own lack of ability.","She had desperately tried to analyze the Forest of Four Seasons mathematically, but there was only one conclusion she could reach.","Impossible.","She had realized that the moment she saw the video of the sea flowing backward into the river.","So that anyone else who becomes stranded in the Forest of Four Seasons won’t die for nothing.","Grylls’s survival records could someday become an invaluable resource for anyone else who found themselves stranded in the Forest of Four Seasons.","With that in mind, Selena began retracing Grylls’s journey.","She started with the very first post he had written.","The post Grylls had made while confused and disoriented after suddenly finding himself in the Forest of Four Seasons.","He’s been suffering ever since the beginning.","How he’d been chased by a pack of Mad Dogs immediately after helping Heavenly Demon.","How the Guardian had appeared afterward.","How a Mad Dog had bitten one of his arms, nearly putting his life in danger, only for SwordMaster’s help to save him from the brink.","And how he’d discovered a mature Mandrake, which ultimately led to her own complete recovery.","Only ten days had passed, yet so many incidents had already occurred.","There had been so much that merely organizing everything he’d done took a considerable amount of time.","I should write about the registered users too....","Since it was a gallery, there were far too many... colorful personalities.","Pieces of trash—","No, idiots—","No, morons.","For now, she excluded the anonymous users masquerading as human beings as much as possible.","Occasionally, they said something important or taught Grylls useful things, such as how to clean and prepare fish.","But aside from a few important contributions like those, most anonymous users did nothing but leave bizarre comments.","His life-and-death struggle with the saber-toothed tiger, and the heart he obtained from it that had the same structure as a Dragon Heart....","The more she looked back over everything, the stronger one thought became.","Just how has Grylls managed to survive in this hellish forest?","He had the gallery’s help, but the Forest of Four Seasons was a place where even most powerful individuals wouldn’t be able to survive.","Just looking through the gallery records showed that all sorts of dangerous animals had appeared.","He must have exceptionally good instincts in combat.","There was a reason Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster had taken an interest in him. His talent, at least, was extraordinary.","What was even more surprising was the intelligence he displayed in the gallery.","When dealing with Passing Dwarf or anonymous users, he spoke like some uncouth thug, while he was extremely polite toward the registered users.","Even in a gallery where anonymity was the norm, his kindness and courtesy couldn’t be hidden.","That was something Selena couldn’t help but notice.","Just what did Mr. Grylls do before coming here?","He had displayed an astonishing ability to adapt.","He had already established a base for himself.","Even more interesting was his resentment toward God.","In truth, it would have been stranger for someone in Grylls’s situation not to resent God.","But his resentment went beyond mere grumbling. There was such sincerity behind it that it bordered on blasphemy.","And yet he keeps pushing forward.","The deeper she looked, the stranger a person he seemed to be.","His exploits were equally full of peculiarities.","As Selena recorded Grylls’s actions in her book, she slowly reflected on them.","From what I’ve learned so far...","The kindness to repay goodwill with goodwill.","The decisiveness to immediately cut ties with anyone who betrayed that goodwill.","The friendliness of being polite by default, yet speaking roughly with those he was close to.","The fairness to respect order even in desperate circumstances.","And the cleverness to subtly steer that order in a different direction when there was a legitimate reason to do so.","Those were the aspects of Grylls’s personality that could be gleaned solely from his activity in the gallery.","He definitely said he was an orphan... What could he have gone through to develop a personality like this?","Orphans inevitably lacked certain things.","That wasn’t discrimination. It was simply an unavoidable reality.","Everything they should ordinarily have received from their parents was absent, leaving them more heavily influenced by their environment than most.","As a result, orphans tended to become defensive by nature, and their personalities often became prickly as well.","Grylls bickered with the dwarf from time to time, but there was nothing prickly about him.","He seemed perfectly ordinary.","Maybe it’s only because this is the gallery...","It was possible that everything he did was calculated.","But that seemed unlikely.","If that were the case, there would have been signs.","If he were that calculating, he wouldn’t have helped Heavenly Demon in the first place.","Selena gradually continued compiling her records about Grylls.","She didn’t know what would become of these records in the future, but they were bound to have a considerable impact.","In particular, they would have an enormous influence on research related to the Forest of Four Seasons.","Knock, knock, knock.","\"Princess, it’s Mary. May I come in?\"","Selena was going through the gallery and organizing her records when Mary knocked from outside.","Selena closed the book for the moment.","She had no intention of showing it to anyone yet.","\"Come in.\"","Creak—","Once Selena gave permission, the door slowly opened.","The person who appeared behind it was Mary, the maid who had remained by Selena’s side until the very end.","Mary politely bowed in greeting.","\"So, what is it?\"","\"Well, the Duchess...\"","\"She’s someone you’ll soon have to call Mother. Aren’t you being a little too formal?\"","\"Y-Yes?\"","Startled by Selena’s words, Mary abruptly straightened from her bow.","Selena’s expression hadn’t changed in the slightest.","If anything, she looked downright cold.","\"You’ll soon be adopted as her daughter. You need to practice.\"","\"H-How could someone like me possibly...!\"","\"You need to.\"","\"Y-Yes!\"","Unlike her gentle demeanor in the gallery, Selena maintained a cold manner of speaking in real life.","It couldn’t be helped.","As her incurable illness had progressed, even her emotions had gradually faded.","At least she had been improving lately.","Selena rose from her seat.","The Duchess—or rather, her mother—had summoned her, so she needed to go.","In the past, she had used a wheelchair.","Now, she could walk proudly on her own two legs.","\"Mary.\"","\"Yes?\"","\"Hold my hand. Let’s go together.\"","\"B-But...!\"","\"It’s a request from your older sister.\"","\"Y-Yes!\"","Well, she still had a long way to go before truly growing close to Mary.","Selena affectionately took Mary’s hand and began walking with her.","The warmth of another person had once felt unusually hot to her.","Now, Mary’s hand merely felt soft and warm.","It didn’t feel hot at all.","I sincerely hope Mr. Grylls doesn’t lose hope.","Selena whispered the wish silently to herself.","Around the same time, Grylls, who had decided to start keeping a diary—","\"Wow.\"","He exclaimed in admiration as he looked at the test entry he’d written.","It must have been an incredible piece of writing, considering even his expression was filled with admiration.","It didn’t matter that no one else would ever appreciate it.","He could simply use it as a collection of big data and a field guide.","But then an unexpected problem emerged.","\"My writing skills haven’t improved since elementary school.\"","He was terrible at writing.","No, \"terrible\" didn’t even begin to describe it.","His writing was so awful that even he was impressed after reading what he’d written.","[I tried to steal a turtle egg and met the mother turtle. The mother turtle transformed into a tortoise and shot a laser at me. I was scared.]","That was more or less the style.","It was, in every sense of the word, a truly \"objective\" diary.","Grylls carefully picked apart the diary entry he’d written, then shrugged.","It’s not like anyone’s going to read it.","Contrary to someone’s worries, he was remarkably optimistic."]},{"title":"Chapter 90","paragraphs":["Eel (1)","After briefly coming to terms with the fact that my writing skills had remained stuck at an elementary-school level, I started browsing through the gallery.","I wanted to look through everything I’d posted there so far.","After all, I’d realized that the gallery had essentially served as my diary until now.","But the gallery had plenty of shortcomings if I wanted to use it as a database or field guide.","It’d be too much work to write down everything that’s already happened, so I’ll just add brief descriptions of Wonmo and the Sloth.","My writing skills might have been atrocious, but everyone had at least one thing they were good at.","For me, it was drawing.","I was actually decent enough that even a rough sketch of Wonmo was immediately recognizable as Wonmo.","Wonmo might look easy to draw because he was so round, but he was surprisingly difficult. So I focused on capturing his most distinctive features.","As for the Sloth, he was basically just a sloth, so I drew him roughly.","Still, I made sure to include the features unique to him.","The Sloth possessed all the usual characteristics of a sloth.","Long arms compared to his short legs.","A subtly hunched posture.","A face that somehow looked both laid-back and stupid at the same time.","His claws, however, were vicious.","They looked even sharper now that I’d been taking care of them.","And underneath, I’ll add a simple description.","For Wonmo, I wrote that he was an Owlbear cub who had started living with me after I killed the adult Owlbear.","The Sloth, meanwhile, I described as a little thug who stole my food.","If the Sloth ever found out, he’d probably smack me, but that was impossible.","At least in this world, I was the only person who knew Hangul.","And there’s no reason for anyone to go out of their way to learn writing from another world.","I didn’t want to go through that much trouble just to leave something behind.","It was enough for someone to know that a person like me had once existed.","The dead lived on in the memories of the living.","That alone had value.","At least, that’s what I think.","Even after my parents passed away, my memories of them remained vivid.","I missed them, so every year on the anniversary of their deaths, I held memorial rites for them.","Even when I was short on money, I did my best to remember the foods they’d liked and somehow managed to prepare them.","Otherwise, it would’ve been hard to endure.","At least until I was finally able to let them go, I’d intended to continue holding those rites.","I don’t even know if I should keep doing the memorial rites now that I’m here.","But now that survival rather than money was the issue, I wasn’t sure.","Forget remembering my parents—I might end up joining them myself.","Their death anniversary was still a long way off, but you never knew.","Come to think of it, how do they even count dates here?","A different world might have a completely different way of measuring dates.","I could simply number the days in my diary, but I was curious.","Ah, forget it. I’ll just use the year I’m familiar with as my standard.","My parents’ death anniversary had been one week before the date I’d fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","During that week, I’d gone drinking with friends and met up with people I knew.","I remembered having a harder time than usual.","It had been especially difficult to meet my friends.","With everyone busy finding jobs, it had become difficult to see one another.","I wonder if they’re doing all right.","Those bastards were probably struggling in their own ways too.","Though I was the one suffering like crazy over here.","I chuckled and began jotting down what had happened today.","The octopus tentacles that had burst out of the sand.","The transforming turtle.","I’d gone through a lot today after encountering one bizarre animal after another.","Still, I got something for all that trouble.","I’d even obtained a turtle egg as large as an ostrich egg, so I’d received more than enough compensation for the day.","I quietly closed the diary, now filled with various drawings, and stepped outside the cave.","It was almost evening, so it was about time to start preparing dinner.","Before that, I should check whether anything got caught in the fish trap.","Wonmo happened to be awake too, so we all headed up together.","Splash! Splash!","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuu!\"","\"You happy? Me too.\"","There were no fewer than three fish caught in the trap.","I returned with Wonmo, who was practically bouncing with excitement.","Having plenty of food put me in an incredibly good mood.","Maybe this was my reward for everything I’d gone through today.","But how am I supposed to clean this thing?","I looked not at the container holding the ordinary fish, but at the other one.","Inside was an eel as huge as a python.","I was gradually getting used to cleaning ordinary fish, but an eel was different.","Its entire body structure was different, so I had no idea where to even begin.","Should I knock it out like a normal fish?","I’d probably get knocked unconscious by its tail before that happened.","Its body wasn’t especially bulky, but it was so long that I needed to be careful.","I crossed my arms and stared at the eel for quite a while before opening the gallery.","Times like this, asking the gallery was definitely the best option.","Title) Need some tips on cleaning an eel","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an eel inside a metal container)","I’m planning to eat this guy. Can anyone give me some tips on how to clean it?","└ Eels are harder to clean than ordinary fish, so be careful.","└ Don’t you need to nail its head down first to keep it in place?","└ Wild Grylls) I have to put a nail through it? ;;","└ Eels are slippery and thrash around like crazy, so they’re hard to handle.","└ Wild Grylls) What if I just smack it on the head and knock it out?","└ You’ll end up hitting your own hand. Better to pin it to a cutting board with a nail.","└ If that doesn’t work, sever the spinal cord. That should make things easier.","└ Passing Dwarf) Hey. Once you’re done with that, give me one bite. I’m curious what eel tastes like.","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, sure.","└ Praise the Sun) Think I could get some too?","└ Wild Grylls) Yes.","└ Allfather) Might I have a bite as well?","└ Wild Grylls) Sure, I guess... I don’t mind.","└ King Leor) I know it’s shameless of me, but could I have some too...?","└ Wild Grylls) Sir?","└ Smart Demon) I’ve prepared a storage container. But would it be possible for me to have just one bite as well...?","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;;","└ SwordMaster) Why is everyone begging for one bite like a bunch of paupers? I don’t get it.","└ Probably because it’s eel.","└ They’re definitely all men lol. Look how shamelessly they’re begging.","└ SwordMaster) What’s so special about eel?","└ It’s good for stamina.","└ Yeah, very good for men lol.","└ And it was caught in the Forest of Four Seasons? No man could resist that lololol.","└ SwordMaster) ;;","Right.","As a man, I could understand.","But this is supposed to be my dinner , you people.","I might share once I’d eaten enough to fill myself up, but I needed to put a stop to this before it got out of hand.","└ Heavenly Demon) I shall wield the ban hammer against anyone who becomes too forceful, so keep that in mind.","└ Booo. Tyrant!","└ Heavenly Demon’s really throwing her weight around now that she’s a sub-mod lololol.","└ Heavenly Demon) What did you say?","└ I said you’re the most exalted person in the entire world.","└ Heavenly Demon) A lie. Face the wall and reflect on your actions for one gak .","└ Fucking bitch.","└ Heavenly Demon) Half a sijin .","└ LOLLLLL","└ What’s one gak , and what’s half a sijin ?","└ It’s a Central Plains way of measuring time. One gak is fifteen minutes, and half a sijin is one hour.","└ Isn’t that way of measuring time becoming pretty uncommon these days?","└ Older people still use it pretty often.","Fortunately, Heavenly Demon immediately stepped in to keep everyone under control.","Still, I intended to share with the people who had asked politely if possible.","The eel was so huge that I doubted I could finish it all by myself anyway.","Let’s get everything ready first.","Since the eel was so long, I bought an extra-long cutting board.","Just as the gallery had advised, I drove a nail into the edge of the board to secure the eel.","Naturally, I hammered it in from the other side so that the pointed end stuck upward.","Even nails are kind of expensive.","All that remained was getting the eel out.","Wearing the World Tree Gloves, I pulled the eel from the metal container.","Maybe the World Tree Gloves had some kind of anti-slip effect, because I couldn’t feel its usual sliminess at all.","SMACK!","\"Urgh!\"","Instead, it slapped me with its tail.","The thing was much stronger than an ordinary fish, so even getting it onto the cutting board was a chore.","But before a knife, all fish were sashimi.","I used my dagger to sever the spinal cord behind its head.","The thing was as thick as my forearm, so even cutting through it was work.","Twitch! Twitch!","Once I’d cut almost halfway through its neck, its thrashing noticeably weakened.","Without wasting any time, I pinned its head down with the nail.","That should stop it from going berserk again.","God, this was exhausting.","I wonder if this thing has an inner core too.","Judging by its size, there was a good chance.","Every fish I’d eaten so far had contained one.","I slowly began cleaning the eel, which had almost completely stopped moving.","First I neatly split the body open, then removed the bones.","My dagger was already sharp, but I even used aura to make the process more efficient.","Done. Now I just need to rinse it and cut it into pieces.","Once I’d roughly finished preparing the eel, I thoroughly washed it with water.","Twitch!","\"Eek!\"","Every now and then, it twitched as if it were still alive and scared the hell out of me, but it really was only occasional.","Finally, I poured a little vegetable oil into a large pan and placed the eel, cut into appropriately sized pieces, on top.","Oh, and for the record, there was no inner core.","Apparently, not every fish contained one.","Sssssizzle!","The grilled eel gradually turned golden brown.","I gulped.","This was a delicacy I’d never even tried back on Earth.","Even the friend who had treated me to beef had found eel too expensive.","They say this stuff is really good for men, right?","But I don’t even have anyone to use it with.","I suddenly felt depressed.","The gallery was a place where people indulged all sorts of desires, so pleasant-to-look-at pictures were posted fairly often.","And when it came to particularly exotic races like elves or demons, sometimes I’d find myself hitting save before I even realized it.","Of course, if something was too explicit, the head mod deleted it without hesitation.","Still, for me, those posts were like rain after a drought, so I made good use of them.","Though sometimes I get hit with a bomb.","I still remembered it vividly.","The time I’d entered the gallery only to immediately get hit with one of those \"bombs.\"","The head mod and sub-mods had to personally look at that stuff before banning whoever posted it.","No wonder they said it’d give them inner demons.","While I was distracted by those thoughts, the eel had turned beautifully golden brown.","Oil practically poured from the meat.","There hadn’t been any need to add cooking oil in the first place.","This must be high in calories.","The amount of oil made that obvious.","Out of all the pieces of meat, I picked up a piece from the tail.","I’d heard that the tail was the best part of an eel.","Now it was time to find out.","Crunch—crisp.","Crispy on the outside and moist on the inside.","It had cooked astonishingly well.","The oil from the meat was especially rich, almost sweet in flavor.","There wasn’t any fishy smell either.","I’d only sprinkled on a little salt, yet there wasn’t even a hint of it.","Even the bones are all soft.","I’d heard that the tiny bones were one of the biggest annoyances when eating eel.","But this one didn’t even have that problem.","With a blissful smile, I began devouring the eel.","There was so much that I occasionally gave pieces to Wonmo and the Sloth as well.","It was naturally very fatty, so they both loved it.","Wonmo especially.","[ Passing Dwarf: Damn. This is fucking delicious lol]","[ Wild Grylls: If it’s that good, give me a barricade lol]","[ Passing Dwarf: lol sure. I’ll make one when I wake up tomorrow morning, so wait.]","I wonder where that eel came from.","After finishing my internal energy cultivation method, I started cleaning up.","By the time I was done, pitch-black darkness had settled over the area.","I wrote a diary entry to wrap up the day, then made a post in the gallery.","There had been so much eel that I’d been able to share it with the others too.","Besides, it was greasy food, so overeating could easily give me indigestion.","And so, after finishing my feast of one of the finest delicacies I’d had in ages, I immediately began practicing the internal energy cultivation method.","Maybe it’s because it was eel, but I feel like I have more energy than usual.","It could’ve just been a placebo effect, but it genuinely felt that way.","When people said eel was good for virility, that ultimately meant it was good for your basic \"vitality.\"","At worst, it couldn’t hurt.","Title) Good night, everyone!","Wild Grylls","(Video of a blazing campfire)","See you tomorrow!","Anyone I promised a trade to earlier, let’s do it tomorrow!","After posting, I exchanged a few words with some of the registered users and the anonymous users tossing around their usual jokes.","Seeing the gallery as lively as ever made me chuckle.","Don’t rush.","Starting today, I’d decided to take the long view.","It was time to follow the saying that the more hurried you were, the more you needed to slow down.","Well, technically, the Forest of Four Seasons had forced me to slow down, but that didn’t matter.","As long as even the faintest thread of hope and possibility remained, nothing in the world was truly impossible.","I slowly planned out what I’d do tomorrow, then quietly closed my eyes.","I’ll survive until the very end.","Until the very end.","And so, time passed.","The next morning—","\"Ah, seriously. Is this some kind of joke?\"","The moment I opened my eyes and saw the situation I was in, I couldn’t help but get irritated.","What I saw was a tent.","A tent standing tall and proud, as though it feared neither heaven nor earth.","It was proof that I was an extremely healthy man.","The problem was that it had been going on for far too long.","Seriously, nothing in this place knows the meaning of moderation.","The eel I’d eaten yesterday was definitely to blame."]},{"title":"Chapter 91","paragraphs":["Eel (2)","I may not have any use for it anymore, but my manhood is still extremely precious to me.","And I’m sure every man feels the same way.","Even those asshole buddies who’d laugh their asses off if you broke a leg—if something happened down there ?","That’s the one place they’d sincerely console you about. Anyone who makes fun of that is just a bastard.","And right now, I was facing the greatest crisis a man could ever face.","Maybe it was because I ate eel yesterday, but my tent showed absolutely no signs of going down.","I wondered if eating a single eel could really do this to me, but things were different when the Forest of Four Seasons was involved.","Hadn’t I spent an entire day burning with fever just from eating a single fish before?","’Ah, please. I really don’t want to ask people about this.’","I desperately searched the gallery for anyone who had experienced symptoms similar to mine.","But I guess all guys were the same, because all I found were posts bragging about themselves.","Occasionally, there were stories from guys bawling their eyes out over kidney stones, but that was about it.","It was hard to find anything related to a problem as serious as mine.","’Should I post about it on the gallery...?’","I couldn’t help but seriously consider it.","It was a little—no, extremely embarrassing.","The gallery guaranteed anonymity, so normally I could just shamelessly go for it, but this was different.","Some of my friends were the type to stay polite even in games.","They simply couldn’t bring themselves to act shamelessly because it wasn’t in their nature. I hadn’t understood them back then.","But now that I was actually in an emergency, I couldn’t help hesitating over all sorts of things.","’No. I’ll ask Allfather first.’","Allfather was extremely knowledgeable, so he should be able to help to some extent.","Besides, he was a fellow man, so he’d probably take this seriously.","Hoping that Allfather was well versed in medicine too, I sent him a message.","[Wild Grylls: Allfather, are you there by any chance?]","[Allfather: What is it?]","Fortunately, it seemed Allfather had been hanging around the gallery.","I was relieved.","But being relieved meant nothing if I couldn’t get a solution.","Hoping for the best, I told him about my current symptoms.","[Wild Grylls: I think I’m in a somewhat dangerous... situation. Especially as a man.]","[Allfather: Don’t tell me your penis or testicles ruptured?]","Allfather casually brought up something horrifying.","If that had happened, I would’ve already departed this mortal coil.","Still, it didn’t change the fact that I felt like I was on the verge of bursting.","[Wild Grylls: It’s not that bad yet. But ever since I woke up this morning, it just won’t calm down ;;]","[Allfather: Hmm. It must be because you ate eel yesterday. And since it was an eel from the Forest of Four Seasons, that would explain it.]","[Wild Grylls: You’re sure about that, right?]","[Allfather: Yes. I woke up this morning and mine was quite... Hahaha.]","No wonder even an elixir hadn’t worked.","I’d even applied it directly there, but it hadn’t helped at all.","If anything, it had only made it sturdier.","I wouldn’t even have an excuse if someone called me a fucking idiot.","I’m being fucking serious here, goddammit.","That hollow laugh of his seemed to contain a whole lot of meaning.","Just what the hell was in that eel for it to have an effect comparable to a potent tonic?","But none of that mattered right now.","Treatment came first.","[Wild Grylls: Please tell me the explanation is going to be simple.]","[Allfather: Yes. According to my research, each sex possesses its own unique energy. In the Central Plains, they call it yin and yang, though it can also be described in medical terms.]","[Wild Grylls: This can be cured, right?]","[Allfather: Yes. But I need to explain the theory first, if that’s all right with you. It’ll make the treatment easier.]","[Wild Grylls: Is medicine not enough?]","[Allfather: Since this concerns the energy within your body, your own efforts are the most important part, Mr. Grylls.]","Was he talking about hormones?","I listened carefully to Allfather’s explanation.","[Allfather: Yang energy, in particular, tends to govern physical traits such as muscle mass, body hair, stamina, and so on. Some claim it also affects hair loss, but that has yet to be confirmed.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you saying the eel contained yang energy?]","[Allfather: Not exactly. It merely has the effect of amplifying that energy. The problem is that the place where a man’s energy gathers most easily is the groin.]","From the sound of it, this was going to be pretty difficult.","The internal energy cultivation method was training that demanded an extreme degree of concentration.","It was already starting to hurt down there, and now I had to practice the internal energy cultivation method in this condition?","This was daunting.","Allfather’s explanation was simple.","Eating the eel had caused my yang energy—in other words, my male hormones—to skyrocket.","And there was a high probability that those surging hormones had gathered in my crotch and caused this whole disaster.","It might sound completely ridiculous, but this was a fantasy world.","This was a place where things that made absolutely no sense by my standards were treated as common sense.","[Wild Grylls: So how do I cure it?]","[Allfather: Since you’ve learned an internal energy cultivation method, it should be easy. Imagine the energy gathered in your groin spreading throughout your entire body.]","[Wild Grylls: That sounds incredibly easy when you put it like that.]","[Allfather: The real question is whether you can concentrate on your internal energy cultivation method while keeping that thing erect.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah.]","[Allfather: If it proves too difficult, there are easier methods.]","[Wild Grylls: What are they?]","[Allfather: Either cut it off or relieve yourself manually. Those are your two options.]","[Wild Grylls: ;:;]","Cutting it off was absolutely out of the question.","I thanked Allfather and began practicing my internal energy cultivation method.","I had to resolve this situation somehow if I wanted to get through this crisis.","’Focus on the energy gathered in my groin, not my lower abdomen.’","Anyone who saw me right now would probably think I was a pervert.","But I was serious.","I had to prevent my pride and joy from bursting, no matter what.","Doing my best to ignore the part of me that was making its presence painfully obvious, I gathered and regulated my energy.","\"Phew...\"","As expected, it wasn’t easy. I could clearly feel the energy gathered in my dantian, but sensing it down there was much harder.","Still, I had to do it. I focused with everything I had.","Shaaah—","Fortunately, maybe my concentration had worked. I could feel the tightly concentrated energy gradually thinning out.","I had only just begun rejoicing when something strange happened.","\"Huh? Huhhh?\"","The concentrated energy began spreading throughout my body.","It was pretty alarming at first, but before long, the clump-like energy dispersed like powder.","If it had ended there, I wouldn’t have been so startled.","But a change immediately followed.","The mana flowing through my body.","Its flow hadn’t merely accelerated—it had become far more powerful.","And it wasn’t just my mana. It felt as though my overall physical abilities had been forcibly pumped up.","My heart pounded violently, and I could hold my breath far longer than before.","The sudden change left me completely bewildered.","’F-For now, just keep everything circulating.’","I had no idea what might happen if I stopped here. I maintained my concentration until the very end.","I barely managed to synchronize my long breathing cycles with the torrent of mana raging through me like a storm, gradually calming my pounding heart.","’Heaven is the supreme height to which all creation looks up...’","Just in case, I even recited the chant the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","Rather than trying to calm the storm, I imagined myself adjusting to it.","Instead of trying to \"control\" the energy, I managed it by \"adapting\" to it.","Otherwise, I felt as though the storm itself would sweep me away.","Thump! Thump! Thump—","After a while, my heart gradually settled down, and the flow of mana stabilized as well.","I regulated my breathing a few more times before ending the cultivation method and opening my eyes.","\"Phew.\"","I shook my head.","It felt like I had become one with the storm.","What would have happened if I had chosen to control it rather than adapt?","Given my already low proficiency, there was a good chance I would have failed.","’That chant the Heavenly Demon taught me is surprisingly useful.’","Reciting it whenever I encountered a crisis had helped me tremendously.","For a moment, I wondered what the next part of the chant would be, but I decided to wait patiently.","’...It didn’t burst, did it?’","With a sense of dread, I checked inside my pants.","Fortunately, everything was still intact.","Sorry for being such a lousy owner.","Something incredibly bizarre had happened first thing in the morning, but I had gotten through it safely.","’I’m definitely not posting this on the gallery.’","It was too embarrassing.","I’d rather write it in my diary.","Now that I had also discovered the eel’s effects, it seemed worth recording.","’Whenever possible, share the eel with others. Eating too much by yourself will cause problems.’","A perfect diary entry.","Illustrations, effects, precautions—it lacked nothing.","And thus began the eventful twelfth day of my survival.","The first thing I did was post on the gallery to let everyone know I was alive.","Title) Wild Grylls Is Awake","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a completely burned-out campfire with nothing but charcoal remaining)","Day 12 starts today.","└ Heavenly Demon) You woke unusually late today.","└ Wild Grylls) Something happened this morning.","└ Heavenly Demon) Was it dangerous?","└ Wild Grylls) Personally, I’d call it the greatest crisis of my life.","└ Heavenly Demon) Still, I am glad to hear you resolved it.","└ Allfather) It seems everything worked out well.","└ Wild Grylls) Thanks to you haha ;;","└ Passing Dwarf) Hey. That eel you gave me yesterday definitely worked, kekeke.","└ Praise the Sun) Same here, kek. Been a while since I felt this confident.","└ King Leor) My wife wrung me dry first thing this morning.","└ Smart Mine) I thought it was some kind of drug, not an eel.","└ Everyone only got one piece and it affected all of you like that?","└ I guess that’s the Forest of Four Seasons for you.","└ Then what about Grylls? Grylls ate way more of it all by himself.","└ Was that \"something happened this morning\" because you couldn’t get it to go down?","└ LMAO, if that’s what happened, it really was a crisis, kekeke.","Apparently, I was the only victim(?).","Too much of anything was bad, and this was the result of hogging more of it for myself.","From now on, I’d share any eel I caught.","Assuming I managed to catch another one, that was.","\"Do I have to start being careful about what I eat too...?\"","I could ask Allfather, but ultimately, I was the one who had to deal with whatever symptoms appeared.","I sighed and got to my feet.","Time to start the day.","The first thing I needed to do was maintenance.","I had decided on it yesterday.","I wanted to turn this place into a proper shelter rather than merely a base, so I needed to work on it thoroughly.","’He said he’d give me the barricade around lunchtime, so...’","First, I needed to adjust the positions of the existing barricades.","Since I had converted the moat into a drainage ditch, the ditch now ran beneath the barricades in many places.","It would probably be better to position the barricades outside the drainage ditch altogether.","’I’m going to have to put some muscle into this.’","The barricade stood slightly taller than my eye level.","There was no way I could move it without using mana—","Scrrrape—","\"Huh?\"","Why was it moving?","I had only given it a light experimental push, yet the barricade slid across the ground.","Thinking the ground might be slippery, I checked, but that wasn’t it at all.","Even if it was dirt, something this heavy shouldn’t slide so easily.","’What the hell? Am I imagining things?’","Thinking it might have been my imagination, I pushed harder.","I didn’t use any mana whatsoever.","Scrrrraape!","To my surprise, the barricade moved easily.","That didn’t mean the barricade itself was light.","The marks it left scraping across the ground made that obvious.","In other words, I had become much stronger than before.","’But I was completely normal yesterday.’","Could eating a single eel really have made me this much stronger?","The eel was the only explanation that immediately came to mind.","It seemed ridiculous that eating eel could make someone this much stronger, but where was I?","The Forest of Four Seasons.","A place where I had to shrug and accept it no matter what bizarre thing happened.","I dragged the barricade around for a bit before, on a whim, grabbing its bottom edge and trying to lift it.","The barricade came up effortlessly.","’This is nice.’","I think I understand why athletes take performance-enhancing drugs."]},{"title":"Chapter 92","paragraphs":["Traces (1)","I think I need to revise what I said about the eel.","A natural strength-enhancing drug. That description fit it perfectly.","Of course, the downside was that the side effects weren’t just a little severe—they were extremely severe—but they were manageable.","More importantly, unlike actual drugs, the effects didn’t seem temporary. There was a high chance they were permanent.","’Forget virility and all that. It boosts stamina itself.’","There were all sorts of folk beliefs surrounding eel, but in reality, eel was good for everyone regardless of age or sex.","It would be strange if something that was good for men was somehow bad for women.","It was easier to think of it as an energy booster.","And eel from the Forest of Four Seasons boosted not only energy but overall physical ability.","’Things could’ve gone really badly if I hadn’t learned the internal energy cultivation method.’","But no matter what it was, if your body couldn’t process it, you were bound to suffer for it.","If the Heavenly Demon hadn’t taught me the internal energy cultivation method—if she hadn’t taught me the chant—my manhood probably would’ve exploded.","’There’s absolutely no downside to training the internal energy cultivation method.’","It relieved fatigue. It increased my mana. Whenever something went wrong with my body, it helped restore it.","It was perfect in every way.","I should train even harder from now on.","\"Hrngh.\"","I repositioned the barricades one by one.","Since I had become stronger, I managed to save far more time than I originally expected.","’I can install the barricades the dwarf gives me here.’","After finishing the rearrangement, I went back into the cave and moved on to other tasks.","The first thing I did was update the map.","I marked the location of the sea.","There wasn’t just the sea itself. There were also quite a few rivers where seawater flowed upstream.","Since I currently had no idea where those rivers led, I left as much blank space around them as possible.","’Even that river split into two branches farther upstream.’","The problem was that one of those branches flowed toward another rather terrifying place.","Maybe a troop of monkeys lived there, because I had heard cries like, \"Oooh! Oooh!\"","I would rather avoid the place if possible, but there was a good chance I would eventually have no choice but to go there.","’How did the monkeys evolve?’","The most basic change in this place seemed to be animals growing larger.","Most of the animals I had encountered so far had been huge.","So how had monkeys, animals famous for their high intelligence, changed?","I had wondered about this once before, but I sincerely hoped they hadn’t transformed into anything as bizarre as that shark-man from before.","’For now, I’ll head upstream and come back.’","Now that I had finished repositioning the barricades, I checked how many fish had been caught.","Three fish had been caught overnight.","A plentiful haul.","Since I occasionally obtained unexpected food supplies like the turtle eggs, my stockpile seemed to be gradually growing.","’I’ll have the turtle egg for breakfast.’","If I left it sitting around for no reason, it could end up going bad.","Things like this were best eaten quickly.","The egg was about the size of an ostrich egg, so one should be enough to fill me up.","’Guess I’ll have to make it sunny-side up.’","Even with a spatula, there was no way I could flip it.","Like I said, it was just too big.","After thinking about it, I decided to simply cook it sunny-side up.","Sunny-side up eggs were delicious too.","So I poured a little oil into the large cast-iron pan, and once it seemed sufficiently heated over the campfire, I tried cracking the egg.","Tap! Tap-tap! Thunk!","\"Huh?\"","Surprisingly, it wouldn’t crack easily.","It was pretty tough.","Considering how large the egg was, its shell was apparently thick as well.","Worried that the oil in the pan would start splattering everywhere, I hurriedly fetched my hammer.","Clang! Clang! Clang!","\"What the hell?\"","Even the hammer struggled to break it.","The shell was as hard as iron.","Thinking I might simply be holding back too much, I put a little more strength into my blows, but the result was the same.","It showed absolutely no signs of breaking.","Apparently, it had evolved so that even if a beast stole the egg while its parents were away, it wouldn’t be able to crack it open.","’Wouldn’t that make it hard for the hatchling to get out too?’","Was it survival of the strongest?","What a brutal race from the moment they were born.","In the end, I had to use aura before I finally managed to crack the egg.","Sssssizzle!","At least my efforts weren’t wasted, because the egg began cooking beautifully.","There was so much of it that it filled the entire large pan.","I sprinkled salt over the top.","That should bring out the flavor even more.","Salt was godly.","’Maybe I should’ve brought another one while I was there?’","Of course, if I had, it would’ve been so heavy that I probably wouldn’t have been able to move properly.","I chuckled, and once the egg was cooked, I removed the pan from the campfire.","Unlike fish, it was difficult to transfer this onto a plate.","I had no choice but to cut it up and eat it like a steak.","I grabbed a knife and fork and cut into the edge.","Even with a sunny-side up egg, the trick was to fry the edges until they became slightly crispy.","Crunch—","The crispy fried edge combined with the mild flavor characteristic of egg whites.","Finally, the salt added a savory touch that brought everything together.","Objectively speaking, the fish tasted better, but there was something special about this egg.","Especially because I had obtained it from the wild rather than through the auction house.","Pop!","I broke the neatly centered yolk.","Using it like a sauce, I ate it together with the egg white.","The yolk wasn’t fishy either. It had a peculiar, subtle flavor that seemed like it could become addictive.","\"Wow. This is delicious.\"","I finished the entire pan of egg.","I even wiped my mouth with a tissue afterward.","It wasn’t quite like steak, but it tasted somewhat like eating bacon.","What an incredible flavor.","The eel was the same way. Most of the food from the Forest of Four Seasons tasted fantastic.","’Though having salt probably makes the biggest difference.’","Honestly, salt was practically a cheat item among cheat items.","Without salt, I probably wouldn’t have been able to enjoy food like this.","Moments like these really made me appreciate the existence of the gallery.","Without the gallery, even finding salt would have required an enormous amount of effort.","’Or I might’ve died long ago.’","After cleaning everything up, I checked the time.","Probably because I had repositioned the barricades first, it was already 9 a.m.","I usually considered 8 a.m. the start of my day.","’I’ve still got plenty of time, and I have some things to receive, so I’ll spend the morning training.’","First, there was something I hadn’t managed to receive yesterday.","The container that Smart Mine had promised me, which supposedly made it easier to store inner cores.","I had wondered whether something like that even existed, but since he had offered it, I intended to accept it.","’If he scams me, I just won’t trade with him again.’","Inner cores were everywhere.","I found one practically every time I cut open a fish’s belly.","I had already collected close to ten of them.","Giving away one shouldn’t be a problem.","Title) Smart Mine, I’d Like to Trade","Wild Grylls","If you see this post, please trade with me. I was too busy to do it yesterday.","It was only about five minutes after I posted that message that I received a reply.","I had been waiting for Smart Mine as well, so I accepted without hesitation.","[Smart Mine: Greetings, Mr. Grylls. First, allow me to express my gratitude for agreeing to this trade.]","[Wild Grylls: You sound completely different from how you do in the comments.]","[Smart Mine: It is my personal rule to always show proper respect to a patron.]","[Wild Grylls: I have no intention of becoming your patron, though.]","[Smart Mine: Considering the value of inner cores, you are more than qualified to be one.]","What a weird persona.","Or maybe he really was just being polite.","The gallery was full of all kinds of people, so this was nothing compared to some of them. Just look at the Heavenly Demon.","If anything, having him act this politely might be more comfortable.","At least he’d made a good impression on me.","[Wild Grylls: By the way, what exactly is this container for storing inner cores?]","[Smart Mine: It is a bottle that emits cold when you channel qi into it. You can think of it as a miniature refrigerator.]","[Wild Grylls: If it runs on mana, wouldn’t it be better to just buy an actual refrigerator...?]","[Smart Mine: The amount of qi it requires is significantly lower. It is also difficult to make, so it is generally used only for storing valuable items.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you sure you’re okay with giving me something like that?]","[Smart Mine: This item can be bought with money. Inner cores, on the other hand, are difficult to obtain even with money.]","I roughly understood.","It was because of their rarity.","King Leor had once given me a crystal orb imbued with Light magic.","So there was nothing particularly strange about a container that generated cold.","It was fantasy. I just had to accept it for what it was.","Thinking too deeply about it would only give me a headache.","[Wild Grylls: All right. But it’s not going to break or anything, right?]","[Smart Mine: The chances are extremely low, but if it does malfunction, please tell me immediately. I will repair it myself.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’ll give you the inner core I got today, so I hope this turns out to be a good trade for both of us.]","[Smart Mine: The honor is mine.]","Calling it an honor was a bit much.","I finished the trade with the impeccably polite Smart Mine.","Soon afterward, I received the bottle he had mentioned.","’What kind of writing is this?’","There were unfamiliar characters inscribed on the bottle.","It was much smaller than an elixir bottle, only about as long as my pinky finger.","It was fairly thick, so an inner core looked like it would fit inside, but I couldn’t feel any cold coming from the outside of the bottle.","’Did I get scammed?’","Feeling slightly uneasy, I tested it first.","The moment I pulled out the stopper sealing the glass bottle, cold air slowly seeped out.","There was a chance he had simply trapped cold air inside it, so I waited for thirty seconds.","Even after thirty seconds had passed, the container continued emitting cold air.","’That’s fascinating.’","They didn’t have mini refrigerators, yet they had something like this.","Maybe it really was because of how much mana each one consumed, but I didn’t know enough to say.","As long as it worked, that was all that mattered.","I put all the inner cores I had collected so far into the bottle.","As soon as I did, the surface of the bottle turned white as though it had frosted over.","’Did the cold intensify because the mana inside the inner cores is leaking out?’","Let’s just say that was the reason.","As long as it preserved them properly, I didn’t care.","Now that I had extended the inner cores’ storage life, I got to my feet and began training.","As always, my training consisted of swordsmanship and shield practice.","From now on, I intended to do it once every day.","’More precisely, whenever Wonmo is asleep.’","Right now, Wonmo was sprawled on his back with his belly exposed, sleeping soundly.","I didn’t know whether it was because I was nearby or because he still didn’t understand how frightening the wild could be.","’Still, he’s cute.’","Wonmo was a baby.","Babies needed to be protected.","Besides, hadn’t I killed Wonmo’s mother?","Granted, his mother had tried to kill me first... but now that I had decided to raise him, I needed to take responsibility.","’Training aside, how do I improve my reaction speed?’","In the middle of training, I glanced to one side.","Toward Namu-Ppareumbo.","I wasn’t asking for agility, dynamic visual acuity, or reaction speed on Namu-Ppareumbo’s level.","I just wanted to improve my reactions enough that I could respond to sudden attacks.","’Snakes are the biggest problem.’","Snakes were quick.","And stealthy.","They might be slower than Namu-Ppareumbo, but I still needed to prepare for them.","Besides, there was absolutely no downside to improving my reaction speed.","It meant I would have more opportunities to counterattack.","With that in mind, I decided to ask the gallery.","How exactly could I improve my reaction speed?","Title) Any Exercises for Improving Reaction Speed?","Wild Grylls","I want to improve my reaction speed. Are there any good exercises for that?","└ Heavenly Demon) Do you not have Namu-Ppareumbo?","└ Wild Grylls) What about him?","└ Heavenly Demon) I thought your reactions would naturally improve if you sparred with him.","└ Wild Grylls) I could literally die if something goes wrong ;;","└ SwordMaster) Exercises for improving reaction speed are simple. You just need to focus on exercises that stimulate your nerves.","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t know what kind of exercises those are.","└ SwordMaster) Throw a highly bouncy ball hard against a wall. Keep trying to catch it, and your reactions will naturally improve.","└ Wild Grylls) What if the ball hits me?","└ SwordMaster) Then it hits you. What else?","└ Wild Grylls) Teacher? ;;","└ SwordMaster) But seriously, I’m not joking. That really is one of the best methods.","└ Starlight Princess) Nothing in particular comes to mind for me. From your perspective, Mr. Grylls, I think that method would probably be best.","└ Cheonggu Princess) I can give you a ball.","└ Passing Dwarf) You’ve got elixirs anyway, so isn’t it fine even if it hits you in the face?","└ Wild Grylls) Why don’t you try getting hit yourself?","└ Passing Dwarf) Ever been hit by a falling rock?","└ Wild Grylls) Fuc—","In the end, I decided to follow SwordMaster’s advice and throw a ball against a wall.","I got the ball from Cheonggu Princess.","It was slightly smaller than a baseball.","’Wait. Wouldn’t it be better to have Ppareumbo throw it at me?’","If I bounced it around randomly, it might end up hitting Wonmo while he was sleeping peacefully.","With that thought, I handed the ball to Namu-Ppareumbo.","\"Here, Ppareumbo. I’ve got a job for you.\"","\"Throw this at me without warning. Make it a little fast, though. Got it?\"","Why do I have to do that?","Namu-Ppareumbo asked with his expression.","So I gave him a fairly convincing reason.","\"It’ll make the tree that grows your food a little tougher. Wouldn’t that be good for you too?\"","At that, he nodded.","I had no idea how I was somehow capable of communicating with this guy.","Questions aside, we went outside the cave and started training.","Namu-Ppareumbo was so ridiculously slow even when going outside that I had to carry him myself.","\"All right. Throw it.\"","\"...\"","At my words, Namu-Ppareumbo slowly pulled his arm backward.","Slowly.","Very, very slowly.","So slowly that merely watching him was frustrating.","I endured it patiently.","After all, I had no idea when the ball would come flying at me.","\"You little shi—\"","But even the motion of extending his arm forward was so painfully slow that I couldn’t help swearing.","I became so irritated that I shifted my feet.","Whoosh!","At that exact moment, Ppareumbo snapped his arm forward so quickly that it happened in what felt like an instant.","Smack!","\"Gah!\"","The ball slammed straight into my face.","A disaster born from letting my guard down and having comparatively slower reactions.","My temper flared for a moment, but it had partly been my own fault, so I didn’t get angry.","\"O-One more time...\"","\"Let’s do it one more time. Just throw it a little softer this time.\"","If it was for survival, if it was for escaping this place, there was nothing I wouldn’t do.","Sometimes, a man had to grit his teeth and endure.","Thwack!","\"Urgh!\"","And this was one of those times."]},{"title":"Chapter 93","paragraphs":["Traces (2)","The reaction-speed training I started with Namu-Ppareumbo.","Though calling it \"training\" was generous. It was closer to one-sided abuse, but I endured it stubbornly.","Namu-Ppareumbo was holding back in his own way, and my reaction speed was gradually improving as well.","At the very least, as long as I stayed focused until the end, I wouldn’t get hit completely defenseless.","I could at least react fast enough to try to catch the ball, so it was good enough as training.","\"Wonmo, Daddy’s having a really hard time.\"","\"Kyuu?\"","\"So come here.\"","At lunchtime, I hugged Wonmo, who had just woken from his nap, and soothed my gloomy mood.","Wonmo had no idea what was going on, but he made a pleased, rumbling sound as if he liked it.","After calming down from the misery of training, I prepared lunch.","Lunch was one of the fish I had caught this morning.","For reference, two more fish had been caught since then.","Having plenty of food made me happy.","For the time being, I could feast on fish.","’I’ll explore in the afternoon.’","I had said I planned to stay here for a while, but that didn’t mean I was going to stop exploring entirely.","From now on, rather than blindly traveling farther and farther away, I planned to examine the surrounding area in much greater detail.","If I was lucky, I might discover medicinal herbs comparable to a fully grown mandrake.","Or perhaps I could find valuable minerals like the orichalcum cave.","’Sometimes I can’t tell whether I’m lucky or unlucky...’","After finishing lunch, I got ready with my animal companions.","The subspace bag hung at my left hip.","At my right hip were the elixir and various other bottles.","Everything was ready.","But before leaving, there was one thing I wanted to check.","’Should I try drawing the bow?’","The bow had been given to me by Grow the Trees, a fixed-nickname user I suspected was an elf.","Previously, even drawing the string had been difficult.","What about now?","Since my strength had visibly increased, there should be some meaningful improvement.","Creeeeak—","As expected, the string was far easier to draw than before.","That still didn’t mean I could use it effectively in actual combat.","Before, I had needed every ounce of my strength just to draw it.","Now, it was more like I merely had to strain a little.","Still, I would need considerably greater strength before I could draw it comfortably.","\"And the dwarf isn’t answering. Is he drinking or something?\"","Originally, I was supposed to receive the barricades from Passing Dwarf.","But whether he was busy or drinking, he wasn’t responding.","It would probably be better to get the barricades after I returned from exploring.","’Today, I’ll head deeper into the forest instead of following the river.’","Yesterday had taught me that simply walking along the river wasn’t particularly useful.","It would be better to explore different parts of the forest as though I were expanding the map.","Along the way, I could search for rare medicinal herbs or discover animal territories.","Just like the animals did, I would turn this general area into my own \"territory.\"","’Though I’m not going to mark it.’","If I started marking territory like an animal, I might get ambushed while doing it.","I also had no intention of throwing away what remained of my human dignity.","I already suffered enough every time I needed to relieve myself.","I had no desire to take things that far too.","\"Whoa. What the hell is this?\"","I was exploring while imagining that I might discover some mysterious medicinal herb when I found something else instead.","Not an herb.","A mushroom.","To someone unfamiliar with mushrooms, it might not even have looked like one.","It resembled a set of blue deer antlers.","’Is it some kind of relative?’","There was a mushroom known as the \"king\" of poisonous mushrooms—the fire coral mushroom.","True to its name, it looked like red deer antlers.","Its poison was said to be so potent that severe exposure could cause damage comparable to radiation poisoning.","There was even a common claim that merely touching it could cause dermatitis.","’It’s interesting, so I should record it.’","I pulled out the book I had prepared in advance and sketched the mushroom’s appearance.","Drawing it like deer antlers should be good enough.","Then I looked around to see whether there was anything unusual nearby.","It could have been a case similar to the golden mushroom.","’Looks like it just grows normally.’","Nothing in particular stood out.","I closed my notebook and posted it on the gallery.","Title) Found a Blue Mushroom","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a blue mushroom shaped like deer antlers)","Anyone know what kind of mushroom this is?","It looks obviously poisonous, so I didn’t touch it, but I’m curious.","└ Heavenly Demon) It seems to be openly announcing that you should not eat it.","└ SwordMaster) Seriously. It looks unpleasant enough that I wouldn’t even want to touch it. Though maybe it resembles the Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon) Are you mocking this lady’s face by comparing it to a mushroom?","└ SwordMaster) It’s blue, kek.","└ Heavenly Demon) I find myself wanting to turn you blue as well. Perhaps I should make a suggestion to the moderator.","└ SwordMaster) I’m sorry ;;","└ Guess he really doesn’t want to turn blue, kekeke.","└ How much must he hate it, kekeke.","└ Is the Heavenly Demon actually doing her sub-mod duties??","└ Yeah lol. Maybe because she’s unemployed, a lot of the disgusting posts have disappeared.","└ Starlight Princess) There’s a similar mushroom in the Central Plains called the fire coral mushroom, but I’ve never seen one like that. Could it be a mutation?","└ Wild Grylls) You have that kind of mushroom there too? There were some where I used to live as well.","└ Starlight Princess) Yes. It’s extremely famous for being highly poisonous. But this is my first time seeing a blue one.","└ Allfather) This is my first time seeing such a mushroom as well. If it isn’t too much trouble, could I ask you to obtain one for research?","└ Starlight Princess) If possible, I’d like one too.","└ Wild Grylls) Sure. Understood.","Just in case, I put on my gloves before harvesting the mushrooms.","I wasn’t planning to eat them anyway, so there was no reason I couldn’t trade them freely.","’There are so many strange mutations here that there must be plenty of things that would be new even by outside-world standards.’","I continued exploring.","Wonmo led the way, using the excellent sense of smell characteristic of animals to detect anything unusual ahead of us.","He might still be a cub, but an owlbear was still an owlbear.","His sense of smell was remarkably sharp.","Sometimes I failed to notice animal droppings along the way, but Wonmo alerted me whenever that happened.","’This is owlbear poop. And it’s old...’","I had seen it before.","Owlbear droppings.","A lot of time had passed, and there had even been rain in between, so most of it had already washed away.","Still, enough of its shape remained that identifying it wasn’t difficult.","’So this used to be an owlbear’s territory.’","I had never realized because all my previous exploration had been centered around the river.","Then, now that the owlbear was gone, who had taken over its territory?","Judging by the lack of any visible traces, no other animal seemed to have moved in yet.","’Then again, that owlbear had its territory stolen by the saber-toothed tiger in the first place.’","No matter how strong an owlbear was, there was no way it could defeat the saber-toothed tiger.","The saber-toothed tiger even regenerated quickly, making it impossible for the owlbear to compete in a battle of endurance.","\"Kyuu. Kyuu.\"","Around the time I was looking around for any other traces, Wonmo began urging me to hurry.","The sight of him pointing ahead with his tiny forepaw was adorable.","I chuckled and followed after him.","Wonmo was better at finding traces than I was, so I could probably leave that part to him.","I just needed to keep an eye out for any unusual plants or mushrooms along the way.","And if a snake showed up, I’d kill it immediately.","\"Kyuuuu!\"","Then Wonmo apparently found something, because he suddenly began jumping up and down in excitement.","Curious, I pushed my way through the thick trees.","Once I passed through them, a surprisingly wide clearing greeted me.","\"A cave?\"","There was also a cave with an enormous entrance.","The entrance to the cave I lived in was fairly large too.","But this one was even bigger, and I could even feel a cool breeze coming from it.","’The wind is blowing inward.’","Just in case, I readied my weapons.","I had no idea what might be inside.","I didn’t bother turning on the Light crystal orb.","Light was already entering the cave, probably because part of the ceiling was open.","\"All right. Let’s go.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","Once I was ready, we entered the cave.","Wonmo seemed excited, bouncing around before suddenly dashing ahead.","I wanted to tell him not to run and to go slowly, but it was already too late.","If there was something else inside, he’d probably scream.","\"Kyaaaaaak!!!\"","Just like that.","Wonmo disappeared behind a boulder and immediately let out a terrified shriek.","I jumped in alarm and rushed over.","What came into view was an animal.","I barely paid attention to the countless bones scattered around it.","The only thing that made my mind go blank was the animal strangling Wonmo.","An unusually long pair of legs, a body slightly hunched forward, and a strangely melancholic expression.","Above all, even from a distance, I could clearly see the bulging muscles covering its upper body.","’A-A kangaroo?’","A kangaroo was holding Wonmo in a headlock with its thick arms.","Calling it a headlock was generous. Judging by the way Wonmo was struggling, it was practically strangling him.","I had no idea why there was a kangaroo in a forest, much less inside a cave, but rescuing Wonmo came first.","I rushed toward it and swung my sword.","It was threatening Wonmo, so I fully intended to kill it.","Swish!","But true to the animals of the Forest of Four Seasons, the kangaroo dodged easily.","It released the arm around Wonmo’s neck, but I couldn’t let my guard down.","Wonmo whimpered as he ran toward me.","’What the hell? Why is its body better than mine?’","I was dumbfounded by the kangaroo’s blatantly muscular physique.","The muscle mushroom had looked grotesque because of its bizarre limbs, so it hadn’t exactly struck me as impressively built.","But the kangaroo’s muscles bulged visibly beneath its skin, making me even more wary.","\"...\"","Grrrk—","The kangaroo stared at me for a while before slowly lowering its upper body.","Judging by the sound of force gathering in its powerful hind legs, it looked ready to charge.","I raised my shield in preparation.","Boom!","The kangaroo kicked off the ground and leaped high into the air.","It jumped so high that it cleared my head entirely.","I kept my eyes locked on it until the very moment it passed overhead.","Thud! Thud! Thud!","The kangaroo landed behind me and fled toward the cave entrance.","Fortunately, it seemed it had no intention of fighting.","To think I’d live long enough to encounter a kangaroo in the middle of a forest.","I supposed only the Forest of Four Seasons could make something like this happen.","’There really are a lot of animals that crossed over from the other side of the river.’","Namu-Ppareumbo, who normally lived in the jungle.","That kangaroo just now.","And probably plenty of others.","They had likely crossed through one of those distorted spaces and ended up unable to return.","I let out a long breath and checked Wonmo’s condition.","\"Kyuu... Kyuu...\"","Apparently the chokehold had hurt quite a bit, because he clung tightly to my leg.","Maybe this was the first time in his life he had ever truly been hurt.","Even during the battle against the orichalcum Protector, he probably hadn’t felt this threatened.","\"It’s okay. I’m here.\"","\"Kyuu...\"","I stroked Wonmo and reassured him.","Thanks to that, he gradually recovered his spirits.","Now that the kangaroo was gone, all that remained was to investigate the cave thoroughly.","Judging by the countless animal bones scattered everywhere, some kind of beast had once lived here.","’I don’t think that kangaroo was responsible for all this.’","Kangaroos were herbivores.","They might strangle animals with those massive arms, but they were still herbivores.","Of course, the Forest of Four Seasons might have changed it into a carnivore.","But the kangaroo had fled the cave as soon as I threatened it.","At the very least, that meant it didn’t recognize this place as its own \"territory.\"","’Is that a nest?’","The bones weren’t the only thing worth noticing.","There was also a huge bird-like nest.","What made it even more interesting was that Wonmo walked over to it and lay down comfortably as if it were his own bed.","Every now and then, he made a sad little sound.","That gave me a pretty good idea of what this place was.","’So this was an owlbear cave.’","Even the nest itself was much larger than an oversized bed.","It was exactly the right size for an owlbear to lie in.","’Come to think of it, do owlbears normally build nests?’","I didn’t know, so I searched the gallery for information about owlbears.","Owlbears were apparently famous creatures, because there were plenty of posts about them.","And from those posts, I learned that owlbears did indeed have a habit of building nests inside caves.","I briefly thought about how many strange things existed in the world before continuing to inspect the cave.","Trickle, trickle—","A shallow stream flowed through the cave.","There were even tiny fish swimming in it, so the water seemed clean.","’I kind of want to move here.’","With sufficient defenses, this place could probably serve as a natural fortress.","But since part of the ceiling was open, rain would become a problem.","And the sheer size of the cave could also be a disadvantage.","Even large animals would be able to enter and move around easily.","\"...Huh?\"","I was looking around the nest when one particular bone among the many scattered around caught my eye.","Compared to all the animal bones, this one stood out immediately.","\"...\"","It was a human bone.","’Is that... a skull?’"]},{"title":"Chapter 94","paragraphs":["Traces (3)","Human bones are relatively easy to distinguish from those of other animals.","You can even tell them apart from those of apes, which resemble humans. They’re simply easy to distinguish.","The back of the skull is rounded, while the jaw is squared.","This is definitely a human skull. I was certain of it.","Title) Found human bones","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a human skull)","Found a skull in what I think used to be an owlbear’s cave. This is a human skull, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: It does appear to be a human skull. Are there no other bones?","└ Wild Grylls: There are too many bones around here, so it’s hard to find them.","└ SwordMaster: Looks like one to me.","└ Yeah, definitely.","└ If that’s not a human skull, what the hell is it?","└ Judging by how it’s been reduced to bare bones, it must have been there for a long time.","└ There were humans in the Forest of Four Seasons??","└ There probably were. They’re all dead like that guy, that’s all.","└ Don’t tell me that’s Grylls’s future?","└ The odds are fuuuuucking high lol.","└ That’s your great senior right there. What are you doing? Hurry up and pay your respects.","└ Are you fucking insane? Lmaoooo.","└ Fuck. Is that really something you should say to the guy? Lmaoooo.","└ Man, way to completely kill his motivation lol.","└ Starlight Princess: You people are truly awful. How can you call yourselves human beings and say something like that?","└ Be honest. You snickered too, didn’t you?","└ Starlight Princess: My emotions have dried up, so I didn’t even laugh.","└ Come on. It was just a joke. Why are you taking it so seriously?","└ For real, what a boring way to live.","I asked the gallery just in case, and they agreed that it was indeed a human skull.","And an old one at that. The fact that nothing but bare bone remained made that obvious.","’It’s not like they suffered a head injury.’","The skull was remarkably clean. It was intact, without a single broken spot.","I began searching to see if there were any other human bones.","But I soon had no choice but to give up.","I wasn’t an archaeologist. How was I supposed to distinguish human bones buried among countless others?","Just confirming that a human had once been here was enough.","’Was this person dragged here by the owlbear?’","I needed to explore the surroundings a little more. I put down the skull and began looking around the cave.","The cave itself was enormous, so there were plenty of places to investigate.","\"Here...\"","Eventually, I found a place I couldn’t simply pass by.","It was a space right beside the nest.","\"...\"","Two tall walls rose up, with a fairly large space beyond the gap between them.","I poked my head through and cautiously looked inside.","\"...\"","Bones.","Human bones lay quietly against the wall.","Unlike the bones that had been eaten by the owlbear, this skeleton had retained its complete form.","I slipped through the gap and thoroughly examined the interior.","\"Oh...\"","The space beyond the walls was larger than I’d expected.","And cozy.","A great deal of time seemed to have passed, judging by the thick cobwebs and accumulated dust, but even taking that into account, the place still felt cozy.","More than anything else, what caught my eye were the pieces of furniture and equipment scattered around.","Most had been made of wood and had largely rotted away, but a few had barely managed to retain their original shapes.","’Is this a stone axe?’","It was a tool made by binding together a piece of wood that was on the verge of crumbling and a stone.","The front of the stone seemed to have been ground down as much as possible to form a sharp edge.","Judging by how it had been secured to the wooden handle, the person must have made the cordage from fibers themselves.","Unlike me, who had access to the gallery, traces of someone who had started with absolutely nothing were everywhere.","’But these marks...’","I brushed my hand over the marks carved into the ground.","They were extremely familiar.","Because they were identical to the marks I carved into the wall every time another day passed.","Marks recording the number of days survived.","But normally, you’d make marks like these on a wall, not the floor.","Puzzled, I looked around.","’That wall’s full too... and that one...’","The space was enclosed by walls on every side.","And all of them were covered in marks.","It seemed the person had run out of room on the walls and had started carving them into the floor instead.","It was enough to tell me just how long this person had survived.","\"...\"","An indescribable emotion crashed over me like a tidal wave.","Even after surviving for so long, this person had eventually been reduced to a skeleton.","I had the gallery, but...","Could I really hold out as long as this person had?","They had survived far longer than I had. Judging by that alone, they must have been far stronger than me.","And yet they died.","Alone, with no one even knowing what had happened to them, leaving behind nothing but countless marks recording the days they’d survived.","This person could be my future.","That thought crossed my mind.","\"Haa...\"","I couldn’t put the feeling into words.","Was it despair?","Or resignation?","If I’d never known any of this, I might have clung to hope until the very end...","But seeing this left me feeling lost.","Could I really get out of here?","No.","Before that, could I even survive?","’...I just have to keep trying.’","The survival marks covered not only the walls but even the floor.","It looked like they had survived for well over two or three years at the very least.","I didn’t know why this person had died.","I searched around, wondering if I could find the cause of their death.","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place that had made even someone as clueless as me stronger.","There was no way someone who had survived here for two or three years had died for no reason.","\"Hm?\"","As I searched every corner of the space, something suddenly caught my eye.","A chest sitting off to one side.","Despite the passage of time, it had retained its shape.","Judging by the thick layer of dust covering it, there weren’t even any signs of spiders or other insects having gone inside.","’Still, just in case...’","I gently prodded it with the tip of my sword.","Something could leap out of there for all I knew.","Fortunately, my worries proved unfounded. The chest merely rattled a few times, with no sign of anything happening.","’What’s inside? Did this person store bottles in it like I do?’","With a faint sense of anticipation, I slowly opened the chest.","Dust billowed into the air, making me cough, but it wasn’t long before I could see what was inside.","\"...Books?\"","There wasn’t much inside.","Just a few books.","Surprisingly, they seemed to have been stored well, because they were in fairly good condition.","Careful not to make the cover fall apart, I picked up one of the books.","There was some kind of writing on its worn-out cover.","’As expected, I can’t read it.’","I don’t know a single language from this world. Judging by the script, though, it looked vaguely similar to a European language.","In situations like this, the gallery was the best option.","I carefully took pictures of everything inside the space.","Title) Found a place where a survivor used to live","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a space between the walls)","(Photo of a skeleton leaning against the wall)","(Photo of survival-day marks carved all over the place)","(Stones and pieces of wood presumed to have belonged to the survivor)","(Photo of a book with writing in it)","(Photo of the chest where the books were stored)","Found a secluded spot next to the owlbear’s nest and went inside.","There was a skeleton in here, along with survival-day marks carved all over the place.","But the strangest thing is the book. What country’s script is this?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is not from the Central Plains.","└ SwordMaster: It’s not the script of the Messiah Empire either. I’ve never seen it before.","└ Cheonggu Princess: It’s not from our country either.","└ Praise the Sun: It’s not Setan’s either. Nor is it from Alvenheim.","└ That looks like some ancient language.","└ That’s not enough to tell. Upload more.","Everyone’s reaction was the same—they didn’t recognize it.","Given how few countries there were, there should also be relatively few languages, so this was strange.","For now, it seemed best to follow the anon’s suggestion.","I flipped through the pages.","The distinctive musty smell of an old book wafted out, but the pages were still easy enough to turn.","’They’re yellowed with age, but they’re still perfectly readable.’","Now I just had to upload them to the gallery.","Hopefully someone would recognize the writing.","└ Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ve never learned writing like that!","└ Suspiciously: It’s not a language used by beastfolk either.","└ If nobody recognizes it, couldn’t it be the script of a country that was destroyed a long time ago?","└ That’s pretty likely, isn’t it? At the very least, it’s definitely from a country that existed more than fifty years ago. No countries have fallen in the past fifty years.","└ Grylls, you seriously found something incredible.","└ Wild Grylls: What good does that do me if nobody can translate it? This is important to me too.","└ Why is it important?","└ Because it’s a survival journal?","└ Wild Grylls: Yeah. Since it’s a survival journal, it could be a huge help to me. I absolutely need it.","Title) Showing more of the book","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a page densely covered in writing)","This should be enough, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: This makes it even clearer that it is not from the Central Plains.","└ SwordMaster: Not from the Messiah Empire either. Could it be the script of the Iris Kingdom?","└ Allfather: It is not the script of the Iris Kingdom either. However, I feel as though I have seen it somewhere before. Please wait a moment.","└ Starlight Princess: Could it be the script of the Holy Kingdom?","Books can serve as bridges connecting the past to the present.","If that bridge collapses somewhere along the way, countless records and technologies can be lost.","There’s a reason people who want to erase records start by burning books.","’If it’s an ancient script, I guess it’ll be even harder to identify.’","No matter the country, many things change as time passes.","Language is no exception.","Languages of the past can differ greatly from their modern forms.","That’s only natural. No one knows what kind of history might unfold in the intervening years.","Even the Republic of Korea had some of its language altered under the influence of the Japanese colonial period.","And if you compared the Hunminjeongeum created by King Sejong the Great to the Korean language of today, the differences were obvious.","’There are quite a few books here.’","As I flipped through the pages, I checked the other books.","They were similarly well preserved and packed with writing I couldn’t understand.","If only I could decipher all of them.","They could be an enormous help to me.","’I’ll just upload all of them.’","The gallery was my only option for translation anyway.","In that case, it would be better to upload the whole thing.","Careful not to damage the books, I placed them back inside the chest.","Then I put the entire chest into my subspace bag.","Afterward, I searched around for anything else useful, but there wasn’t much.","’I guess the only other thing is the necklace on the skeleton.’","A necklace hung around the skeleton’s neck.","More precisely, it was a pendant.","A pendant set with a red gemstone that looked quite expensive.","But I doubted it would be useful even if I took it.","So I left it where it was, letting the skeleton continue wearing it.","’This person must’ve missed other people too.’","I looked at the skeleton leaning forlornly against the wall.","It went beyond loneliness. There was something downright pitiful about the sight, and I couldn’t help feeling sorry for them.","This person must have wanted to escape too, but they’d never managed to fulfill that wish.","’They say prisoners arrive with both eyes gouged out, but this person could write.’","They must have been stranded here, or there had been some other circumstance.","I stared silently at the skeleton for a moment before entering the gallery.","Then I bought a suitable sack and carefully gathered the skeleton’s bones into it.","’Bear with me until I move you.’","Maybe it was because I’d always faithfully observed the anniversaries of my parents’ deaths.","Or maybe it was simply my personality.","Either way, leaving the dead like this didn’t feel respectful.","There was nothing I could do about the scattered bones that appeared to have belonged to people eaten by the owlbear, but this skeleton had been preserved intact.","After placing all the bones into the sack, I left the hidden space.","When I came out, Wonmo was playing with a butterfly near the nest.","\"Wonmo. Let’s go.\"","\"Kyuu!\"","That was enough exploring for today.","I’d return to the cave and start photographing the books.","The sooner I figured out what they contained, the sooner I’d be able to obtain all kinds of information.","’And I should hold a memorial rite while I’m at it.’","I didn’t know whether this world even had the concept of ancestral rites, but I was going to do it anyway.","This person might be a glimpse of my own future, but as someone in the gallery had said, they were also my great senior.","The legacy my senior had left behind could become an invaluable resource for me.","Some time later, after returning to the cave, I unpacked everything and began looking around the surrounding area.","I needed to find a suitable place for a grave.","’I’ll bury them over there.’","Of course, I wasn’t going to do it immediately.","Uploading the books to the gallery came first.","I took out the chest containing the books and pushed it off to one side.","’Did the gallery figure anything out?’","Some time had passed since I’d uploaded the picture of the book’s pages.","By now, maybe they’d managed to identify the writing to some extent.","With that hope, I logged into the gallery.","└ Allfather: Could you please hurry and photograph the next page for me? This old man’s lower half refuses to calm down from all the excitement.","└ Sir...;;","└ This guy gets vulgar as hell whenever he finds something interesting;;","└ What the hell is that thing to get him so worked up?","└ Apparently they think it was written by the Immortal King’s brother? He was probably from the Balkan Kingdom?","└ What the hell is that doing there?","└ Fuck, if that’s genuine, scholars all over the world are going to lose their minds.","└ Historians are getting excited while academy students are crying lmaooo.","It seemed Allfather had successfully deciphered it."]},{"title":"Chapter 95","paragraphs":["Foreshadowing (1)","Nothing in this world lasts forever.","The same goes for countries that seem as though they could never fall.","Countless nations have been founded and destroyed throughout history, and it is common for later generations either to inherit their legacies or erase them entirely.","As long as people exist, conflicts large and small are inevitable, and once those cracks begin to widen, collapse will eventually follow.","This world was no different.","Countless kingdoms and empires had existed here before disappearing.","I’d never been particularly interested in history, but since this was another world, I couldn’t help developing at least a little curiosity about it.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m here. What does the writing say?","└ Allfather: Oh! You’re here! Mr. Grylls, you’ve discovered an extraordinary record!","└ Wild Grylls: Is it really that significant?","└ Allfather: I’ve only managed to decipher half of that page so far, but this is a record from the Balkan Kingdom! Do you have any idea how incredible that is?","└ Wild Grylls: No.","└ Hey. You said you can do arithmetic, right? Doesn’t that mean you’ve had a basic education?","└ You received a basic education and don’t know about the Balkan Kingdom?","└ Wild Grylls: I keep telling you, I’m from another world.","Even if I’d received an education, the only countries from the past I knew much about were Joseon, Goryeo, Goguryeo, Silla, and Baekje.","If I broadened the scope a little, there were the Mongol Empire, Nazi Germany, Britain, and so on.","Going even further back, I suppose there was Rome, but that was about it.","I’d never been particularly interested in history.","Even the things I did know were mostly things I’d stumbled across while browsing the internet.","Some countries had an unusual number of memes associated with them.","Britain was a prime example.","There was a meme that whenever something happened somewhere in the world, you could blame Britain and you’d probably be right—the \"Perfidious Albion\" meme.","Britain really had committed all sorts of atrocities, but there was one country that made even the title of \"Perfidious Albion\" look trivial.","Nazi Germany.","A country that turned massacre into an industry.","The absolute pinnacle of madness.","That was about the extent of my knowledge.","I knew absolutely nothing about this world’s history.","└ Wild Grylls: So I guess the Balkan Kingdom was some insanely awesome kingdom?","└ Allfather: Hoho. I suddenly feel like dropping a Meteor on you.","└ Wild Grylls: Huh?","└ Allfather: It wasn’t merely some \"insanely awesome kingdom.\" It was a kingdom that had reached the pinnacle of magic—particularly necromancy.","└ And it was the kingdom where the Immortal King was born.","└ All the related records disappeared when the kingdom fell, and now one just happens to be sitting in the Forest of Four Seasons. Lmaooo.","└ But why did he go to the Forest of Four Seasons? I’m curious.","People who loved history began leaving comments one after another.","As someone who knew absolutely nothing about it, I couldn’t make heads or tails of what they were saying.","I considered searching for the information myself, but I couldn’t do that without risking missing the conversation.","’I don’t even know who the Immortal King is.’","As far as I remembered, the only thing I knew was that the Wizard King, Kadir, had defeated him.","Other than that, I knew nothing.","I’d never felt any particular need to know, either.","└ Wild Grylls: I have no idea what any of you are talking about. So basically, there was a powerful country a long time ago, and it was destroyed because of the Immortal King, right?","└ Allfather: More or less.","└ Wild Grylls: And the Wizard King defeated the Immortal King.","└ Allfather: That’s also correct.","└ Wild Grylls: Then when did the Balkan Kingdom fall?","└ Allfather: Chronologically speaking, it fell about thirty years ago.","└ Things were absolute chaos back then. People were evacuating everywhere.","└ My dad was a paladin. We received notice that he’d been killed in action.","└ Stay strong.","└ Wasn’t the previous Hero involved too?","└ As far as I know, the previous Hero died a heroic death, which allowed Kadir to defeat him.","Thirty years ago wasn’t all that long ago.","The effects of something like that were bound to linger.","Even World War II had only ended about a hundred years ago.","And the Korean War, the worst war in Korean history, had been even more recent—less than eighty years ago.","In other words, people of the current generation had personally suffered because of the Immortal King.","To them, the Immortal King must still represent an enormous source of fear.","└ Allfather: He turned every citizen of his kingdom into an undead. It was one of the worst incidents in history, one that nearly swallowed the entire world.","└ That one incident made the Holy Kingdom strictly prohibit necromancy.","└ Didn’t they go beyond banning it and classify it outright as heresy?","└ Rather than heresy, they basically classified necromancers as evildoers. It’s kind of a shame, though. Necromancy was genuinely useful as a substitute for manual labor.","└ It was controversial from the beginning. The Central Plains banned necromancy from the start because they considered it disrespectful to the dead.","└ Who gives a damn about the dead? The living still have to live;;","└ Fuck, you try farming with nothing but your bare hands. You have any idea how convenient it was whenever a village had a necromancer?","└ Necromancers are creepy as hell, so who knows what they might do.","└ That’s prejudice. Using magic on a corpse to determine the cause of death was also a form of necromancy.","└ Wild Grylls: W-Wait, that’s possible?","└ Allfather: It remains an unsolved problem even today. However, we may be able to find the answer in the books you’ve discovered, Mr. Grylls.","└ Wild Grylls: Did the Immortal King destroy me or something?","I still didn’t really get it.","It sounded like a story about some completely unrelated country.","Maybe being stuck in the Forest of Four Seasons for so long had dulled my sense of reality.","Or perhaps it was because I was hearing all of this through the gallery.","Either way, none of it really hit home.","The Balkan Kingdom, the Immortal King, or whatever else—they meant nothing to me.","└ Wild Grylls: I’ll photograph every page of the books and upload them. Can you translate them? Rather than the historical stuff, please focus on how this person survived in the forest.","└ Allfather: Good heavens! Thank you so much! I don’t know how I could possibly repay you for this honor...!","└ Wild Grylls: Just tell me the parts related to survival. That’s all I need.","As I’d said before, survival was the most important thing.","I turned the pages and photographed them one by one.","Uploading all of this to the gallery would take time.","That was precisely why I’d hurried back.","’Should I just give them to Allfather?’","I wondered how long it would take to upload everything, but ultimately decided to post all of it.","Even if Allfather was intelligent, he might still have trouble deciphering parts of the text.","If I made everything public like this, I’d have a better chance of getting objective information.","If someone provided significant help, I was even willing to give them a fully grown mandrake.","’I’ll ignore what the anons say.’","Of course, since all kinds of people gathered in the gallery, I planned to ignore the anons’ interpretations whenever possible.","Someone might deliberately mistranslate something and confuse everyone.","’Still, I’ll give the books to Allfather.’","Regardless of uploading them to the gallery, I intended to give the physical books to Allfather.","They were useless in my hands, and Allfather was the person I trusted most with them.","Whatever their academic value might be, information related to survival took priority for me.","’This person was pretty incredible too. They somehow kept surviving and even managed to keep a journal.’","While photographing the pages, I turned my head toward the sack containing the bones.","What kind of person had managed to keep surviving in this hellish forest and even write a journal while doing it?","Hoping the journal contained some useful survival tips, I carefully photographed every single page.","Considering how old the books were, they had been preserved remarkably well, so there were almost no illegible characters.","’Oh. What kind of plant is this?’","At first, most of the pages had been filled entirely with writing, but as I moved on to the other books, illustrations began appearing as well.","Some of them looked like they could be useful for my survival.","There were drawings of various plants and animals, as well as illustrations of specific locations.","These were exactly the kinds of things I needed right now, so I took extra care when photographing them.","\"Ugh. My neck.\"","I spent most of the afternoon doing nothing but photographing the books.","Even so, it took comparatively little time because I didn’t have to hold something in one hand and take pictures like I would with a camera.","All I had to do was turn the pages and take pictures with my eyes.","The image quality was excellent too, so there was no risk of the writing becoming blurry.","My eyesight determined the image quality.","And I had good eyes.","Therefore, high resolution.","\"Now I just have to upload all of these to the gallery.\"","I uploaded everything I’d photographed from the books to the gallery.","Why go through all this trouble? Wouldn’t it be easier just to leave everything to Allfather?","I could say it was for the sake of getting objective interpretations, but people who didn’t understand probably still wouldn’t understand.","I simply had a strange feeling that this was what I should do.","’I’ll upload each book separately so they’re easier to distinguish.’","There was no limit to the number of photos that could be uploaded to the gallery.","However, the gallery wasn’t completely free to use in terms of mana, so there was a practical limit.","Every upload consumed a tiny amount of mana.","The more photos there were, and the longer a video was, the more mana it consumed.","Title) First book I found","Wild Grylls","(Photos of the book’s contents)","(Photos of the book’s contents)","(Photos of the book’s contents)","(Photo of the final page)","I’m just uploading the entire book.","I’ll give one fully grown mandrake to whoever deciphers information related to survival.","For the record, I’m only going to trust registered users. I’ll upload the rest of the books later.","I posted exactly that and then uploaded all the other books as well.","It was nothing but repetitive manual work, yet after finishing it all, I felt oddly accomplished.","Once I’d gone through everything, I initiated a trade with Allfather.","Less than three seconds after I sent the request, he accepted.","[ Wild Grylls: Hello, Allfather. Did you see the posts I uploaded?]","[ Allfather: I’m reading them right now with my lower half standing at full attention.]","[ Wild Grylls: ;;]","He was always like this, so I decided to ignore it.","If I got awkward about it, I’d probably end up being the weird one.","[ Wild Grylls: Anyway, I was thinking of donating the books I found? Well, giving them to you, at least.]","[ Allfather: What! Those precious books...! Are you truly sure you want to give them to me?]","[ Wild Grylls: I can’t properly preserve them, and I can’t decipher them either. In return, if you find anything related to survival, tell me immediately.]","[ Allfather: That much is easy. Aren’t you curious about the Balkan Kingdom or the Immortal King?]","[ Wild Grylls: He was basically a king who raised an army of skeletons and started a war, right?]","[ Allfather: Hoho. That summary is so perfect that you’ve left me with nothing to say. You’re simply not interested, are you?]","[ Wild Grylls: I’ve got enough problems of my own.]","[ Allfather: I see. Very well. I’ll tell you how this man managed to survive.]","[ Wild Grylls: Thank you. Ah, before that, may I ask you one more thing?]","[ Allfather: Go ahead.]","[ Wild Grylls: I’d like to know this man’s name.]","At least I wanted to know his name.","There was a big difference between burying someone whose name you knew and someone whose name you didn’t.","Fortunately, his name must have been written on the first page, because Allfather answered immediately.","[ Allfather: The last scribe of the Balkan Kingdom, Rice Kraone. His name was Rice Kraone.]","[ Wild Grylls: Rice Kraone. Understood.]","Now that I’d handed the books over to Allfather, there was only one thing left to do.","Bury the skeleton from the sack somewhere sunny.","I took a shovel, a hammer, and the sack containing the skeleton and headed outside.","’A cross... no. Better not. I’ll just use a stone.’","Mixing a cross with a Korean-style memorial rite would be one bizarre combination.","It would be better to find a reasonably flat stone and use that instead.","Thud! Thud!","I began digging with the shovel.","I made the grave long enough for the entire skeleton to fit.","All that remained was to place the skeleton inside and cover it up.","’Strangely enough, all the bones are still connected.’","The skeleton had continued to hold its shape like one of those models you’d see in a science classroom.","Normally the bones should have separated, but instead they remained connected and retained their form.","I didn’t know enough about the subject to tell whether that was normal, but it wasn’t a problem.","I gently laid the skeleton in the grave and covered it with soil.","Thud! Clack! Clack! Clack!","Then I planted a broad, flat stone at the head of the grave.","I hammered it into place so it wouldn’t move.","Everything was ready.","I bought a reasonably priced bottle of liquor from the auction house.","For reference, it was liquor from the Central Plains.","At least it had an East Asian feel to it, so it was familiar to me.","Pouring beer over a grave just didn’t feel right.","Glug, glug, glug—","I poured the liquor over the grave and stone marker, soothing the spirit as best I could.","Then I bowed twice.","It was a little crude, but it should be enough to show respect.","What mattered wasn’t formality.","It was sincerity.","At least, that was what I believed.","’Ah. Right. His name.’","I’d forgotten to put his name on the stone.","That had almost been a serious mistake.","I laid the stone marker flat again.","Then I bought some ink and a brush from the auction house and carefully wrote on it.","Naturally, I wrote in Hangul.","It was the only script I knew.","[Rice Kraone, the last scribe of the Balkan Kingdom, rests here.]","That should be enough.","I waited until the ink dried, then fixed the stone back into place over the grave.","I’d finished paying my respects to the dead.","Normally, the last thing to add would be a keepsake or personal belonging... but there was no need.","I hadn’t touched the pendant the skeleton had worn around its neck until the very end.","I’d buried it together with him.","In other words, the somewhat peculiar funeral was finally over.","Just as I turned around to head back toward the cave—","[Grazaas.]","A voice, eerily sinister, sounded from behind me.","At the same time, an icy chill swept over me, enough to make every hair on my body stand on end.","I flinched violently and spun back toward the grave.","And then—","\"...\"","There was nothing there.","So little, in fact, that I almost wondered whether I’d imagined the voice.","Only the silent surroundings and the grave where I’d just performed the memorial rite remained.","’Am I seriously starting to hear things now?’","I rubbed my face and headed back to the cave.","I’d even eaten eel, but somehow it felt as though my energy had already been drained again.","’I’ll take a nap.’","For some reason, exhaustion had suddenly piled up throughout my entire body.","While Grylls was taking his nap—","└ Hey. If I deciphered that correctly, this is going to cause a massive uproar.","└ What’s in it?","└ It says the Holy Kingdom massacred the citizens of the Balkan Kingdom in an attempt to create the Immortal King;;","└ ???","└ What the fuck are you talking about??","└ The Holy Kingdom did? Why the hell would they do that?","An unexpected revelation was beginning to unfold."]},{"title":"Chapter 96","paragraphs":["Foreshadowing (2)","The Immortal King.","The being who plunged the world into terror by turning every citizen of the Balkan Kingdom into undead—an immortal army.","Undead fundamentally had no need for supplies , which made them an overwhelmingly powerful military force.","On top of that, they could raise the enemy’s corpses as undead, making their opponents experience firsthand what it meant to be hopelessly outnumbered.","But did that mean necromancy, the foundation of all undead magic, had always been evil?","No.","It had only been strictly prohibited by the Holy Kingdom after the incident involving the Immortal King. Before that, it had been a form of magic anyone could use.","Title) It’s a shame about necromancy","Necromancy was genuinely useful if you used it properly.","You didn’t even need human corpses. You could use monster or animal corpses and replace manual labor with them.","I don’t think necromancy itself is bad. The people who misuse it are the problem.","└ You want to legalize necromancy and end up with another Immortal King? Absolutely not.","└ Then what about other kinds of magic? Isn’t misuse the real problem? Other offensive magic is evil if you abuse it too.","└ That’s true, but the Central Plains never viewed necromancy favorably to begin with. If only the Holy Kingdom had banned it, maybe things would be different, but the Central Plains joining in made a huge difference.","└ Even so, banning it outright is a bit much;;","└ Exactly. What about people who died before they could even leave a final message?","└ It’s basically like an entire promising profession disappeared overnight. A lot of things became much more troublesome because of that.","Title) If only the Immortal King had never existed","Then my father probably wouldn’t have been executed.","└ That’s rough. A lot of people resent the Holy Kingdom because of things like that.","└ My father was the greatest merchant there was.","└ ?? Why would a merchant fall because of this?","└ Fuck, don’t tell me this bastard’s dad was a grave robber??","└ Sounds more like he was involved in human trafficking than grave robbing;;","└ What kind of fucking lunatic was he;;","└ He should’ve had his head chopped off ages ago lmaoooo.","└ Is it because of people like that that necromancy’s reputation got even worse?","└ That’s an extreme case. Normally they used corpses of unidentified people.","└ It’s basically the same logic as condemning all pharmacists because one of them made illegal drugs.","└ And human trafficking isn’t even something unique to necromancy. He’s just forcing a connection.","Necromancy was an unsettling form of magic, not an inherently evil one.","In fact, it had provided the world with numerous benefits, both large and small.","The most representative example was replacing simple manual labor.","It had contributed greatly to agriculture in particular—the starting point and foundation of human civilization.","An ox died?","Use necromancy to raise it again.","Not enough workers?","Ask a necromancer to provide labor.","Human corpses could also be used, though doing so required going through rather strict procedures.","Most people especially despised the use of necromancy in war, so there was an unspoken rule prohibiting it.","If a country used necromancy in warfare, it could hardly complain if the rest of the world treated it as an international pariah.","Title) Necromancy really is creepy, though","Honestly, bringing dead bodies back to life is ominous by itself.","It gives off an evil vibe, and there’s just something disturbing about corpses.","└ (Photo of a Death Knight riding a horse) A skeleton horse looks fucking badass though.","└ Damn. After seeing that, I’ve decided I’m resurrecting a horse with necromancy.","└ You’re gonna get arrested by the Holy Kingdom;;","└ Then I’ll just ride away on the horse.","Title) Just laying out the facts","Was the Immortal King evil? Yes.","Did the Holy Kingdom overreact? Yes.","Is necromancy creepy magic? Yes.","If they’d only banned using it on humans, that would’ve been one thing, but people are pissed because they banned necromancy itself.","They also claim it summons the souls of the dead, but even that’s uncertain.","Have you ever seen a basic labor skeleton with a sense of self? I haven’t.","I think it’s less that they have egos and more that some spirit-like entity inhabits them, like with a Protector.","The corpses simply carry out the orders they’re given.","└ Then what about people who claim they summoned their ancestors through necromancy?","└ That’s only possible when you have a definite medium or one of the deceased’s personal belongings.","└ Then what about liches and Death Knights?","They’re both closer to monsters, so that comparison doesn’t really mean much. Think of goblin shamans, orc shamans, or gnoll magicians.","└ What’s your job? Are you a professor or something?","└ I’m just a gallery loser sitting at home.","└ Get the fuck out lmaooo.","└ Everything sounded convincing until I saw that. My trust just plummeted lmaooo.","└ What kind of analysis is a gallery shut-in doing? Lmaooo.","After the Immortal King incident nearly covered the world in corpses, necromancy came to be regarded as evil magic.","Several highly respected mages and scholars argued that it was unwise to simply abandon necromancy altogether, but their voices meant little.","Too many people had been harmed by the Immortal King’s actions or had lost someone they loved.","At least for the current generation, necromancy would never be seen again.","That was what everyone believed.","Title) I deciphered what Grylls uploaded","The language of the Balkan Kingdom has almost completely disappeared, and this version was used by the upper classes, so it was difficult to translate.","But everything in here is shocking as hell. If this is genuine, the Holy Kingdom is going to be in serious trouble.","└ What’s it say? Earlier someone said the Holy Kingdom carried out a massacre.","└ The established story is that the Immortal King appeared first and then the Holy Kingdom intervened, right? But according to this, the order is reversed. The Holy Kingdom massacred the people of the Balkan Kingdom first, and that is what caused the Immortal King to emerge;;","└ How does that make any sense? That shouldn’t even be possible;;","└ The Balkan Kingdom had a relatively small population, and the Holy Kingdom was overwhelmingly powerful, so maybe that’s how.","└ No. What I’m asking is why the Holy Kingdom would massacre the people of the Balkan Kingdom in the first place. There has to be a reason.","└ It says they asked the Balkan Kingdom to lend them its power so they could defeat the Demon King. When the Balkan Kingdom refused, the Holy Kingdom wiped them out as an example;;","└ Fucking hell;;","└ If that’s true, \"serious trouble\" doesn’t even begin to describe it.","Title) There were actually a lot of suspicious points","According to people who were close to the Balkan Kingdom, the Immortal King had originally been closer to a benevolent ruler.","It’s true that the Immortal King was highly skilled in necromancy, but he strictly prohibited necromancy involving the dead.","If there was a special reason, however, he would allow it through proper procedures.","The Balkan Kingdom may have been small, but its people had no trouble making a living.","Its national power was weak compared to other countries, but considering the size of its territory, its people were actually fairly prosperous.","So why would a man who knew how to be satisfied suddenly become the Immortal King and try to devour the world?","And why would he go so far as to turn every single one of his own people into undead?","They said it was to conquer the world, but unless someone was completely insane, they wouldn’t do something like that.","Being alive was what made conquest meaningful in the first place, so why would he do something like this?","└ So you’re saying you think the Holy Kingdom has something shady going on behind the scenes too?","└ Yeah, but only here in the gallery lol.","└ Well, if they get rattled by rumors that started in the gallery, that’d basically prove they have something to hide lol.","└ I don’t understand why records like that would even be in the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ People are just making a big fuss over nothing lol.","When the shocking revelation first began spreading through the gallery, the users didn’t believe it.","The contents were difficult enough to accept on their own, and more importantly, they had been discovered in the Forest of Four Seasons.","The truth suddenly emerges from a book found while exploring the most remote place imaginable?","└ So you’re saying Grylls deliberately went looking for it? In the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ That doesn’t make sense either. You just have to chalk it up to ridiculous luck.","└ Look at how fast you accepted that explanation lmaooo.","Title) If anything, the Forest of Four Seasons makes it more believable","If the Holy Kingdom really tried to kill everyone in the Balkan Kingdom, it makes sense that someone would flee to the Forest of Four Seasons.","The Immortal King probably sent his scribe there as a last resort too. If he was going to die either way, there was nothing to lose.","└ That actually sounds plausible.","└ Even if he left records behind, there would’ve been no one to read them anyway.","└ Except the person who found them was Wild Grylls lmaooo. The one bastard who can use the gallery from inside the Forest of Four Seasons.","└ What kind of coincidence is this? Lmaooo.","Paradoxically, that was precisely what made the story more credible.","Grylls had even uploaded the related books to the gallery in their entirety .","If he’d only posted selected excerpts, people might have accused him of manipulating the narrative.","But since he’d gone to the trouble of uploading everything, that accusation couldn’t easily be made.","And as had been mentioned many times before, the gallery was a form of technology accessible to anyone, regardless of age or gender, so long as they met the necessary conditions.","That was more than enough for scholars scattered across the world to gather beneath Grylls’s posts and debate the contents.","Title) The more I think about it, the more random this feels","(Photo of an elf tilting their head)","Grylls finds records related to the Immortal King while exploring?","Doesn’t this feel way too sudden?","And Asella—the gallery’s head moderator, Don’t Abandon the Hero —was also watching the situation unfold.","She stared at the gallery with confusion in her eyes.","As both a devout believer and the current Hero, she had just been confronted with a truth that was almost impossible for her to accept.","’W-What is this...?’","The truth surrounding the Immortal King, the worst necromancer and tyrant in recorded history.","History stated that the Immortal King, consumed by excessive ambition, had turned every citizen of his kingdom into undead.","To stop him, the previous Hero and her partner, the mage Kadir, had personally taken action to thwart his ambitions.","During that battle, the Hero had sacrificed herself heroically, and Kadir had ultimately defeated the Immortal King.","...That was the history known to the world.","’N-No way! The Holy Kingdom would never do something like that...!’","The material Grylls had uploaded contained events so vile that they sounded like a conspiracy theory.","Grylls himself had only posted them because he wanted the records left behind by his great senior deciphered, but their impact was far beyond anything he could have imagined.","A truth that could never be revealed to the world.","The dark underside of the Holy Kingdom, a nation devoted to worshipping the gods.","Only the beginning had been deciphered so far, but it could be summarized like this:","The organization formed to defeat the Demon King had instead created the Demon King.","There wasn’t even a trace of justice to be found in the story.","The revelation struck Asella deeply.","’Y-Yes. It has to be a lie. If something like this really happened, the Goddess would never have forgiven it...’","The Holy Kingdom was a nation that worshipped the gods.","There was no way such a country could have created a Demon King.","Asella tried to rationalize it and calm her pounding heart.","For now, her priority was settling the gallery, which had gone beyond chaos and was on the verge of overflowing entirely.","’Should I... delete Mr. Grylls’s posts?’","The third rule of the gallery:","Posts that create tension between nations are prohibited.","Grylls’s posts were a perfect violation of that rule.","The prohibition against excessive fraternization only applied to relationships formed in the real world, so that wasn’t an issue.","’But Mr. Grylls himself posted them without thinking anything of it...’","She couldn’t help hesitating.","More importantly, there was an even larger problem.","If she deleted Grylls’s posts, people would become even more convinced that the contents were true.","It might actually be better to leave them untouched.","Asella had her foolish side, but she was by no means stupid.","’For now, it would be better not to delete these posts.’","The information had probably already spread as far as it could.","She’d been physically occupied until moments ago and hadn’t had the chance to check the gallery.","’If the Holy Kingdom really did this...’","Shake! Shake!","Asella violently shook her head, trying to drive away the thoughts creeping into her mind.","The real world was still quiet.","Even if controversy broke out, the Holy Kingdom could simply deny everything.","’This chaos might remain confined to the gallery.’","Problems that erupted inside the gallery rarely spilled over into the real world.","It was essentially a tempest in a teacup.","Of course, things would be different if concrete evidence existed.","For example, the books Grylls claimed to have found.","If those books ended up in someone else’s hands, that would change things.","’Even then, it would be difficult unless that person had considerable prestige.’","There was still time.","Asella decided to wait and see how the Holy Kingdom responded.","She desperately hoped none of it was true, but...","’The Goddess hasn’t said anything at all, so it must be false.’","Given the circumstances she herself was currently facing, dark emotions began creeping into her heart.","’It has to be.’","***","While the gallery was in complete uproar—","\"Ahh. That was a good nap.\"","Grylls woke from an exceptionally satisfying afternoon nap.","The first thing he did after waking was check the gallery.","He wanted to see whether anything had been deciphered.","After seeing the chaos filling the gallery, only one thought crossed his mind.","\"Looks like they still haven’t translated the part I actually wanted.\"","He was disappointed."]},{"title":"Chapter 97","paragraphs":["Foreshadowing (3)","Title) Immortal King Summary","Wild Grylls","Once upon a time, there was a certain kingdom.","The kingdom was poor, but it had a kind king and happy subjects.","The kind king devoted himself to his people, and his people understood how hard he worked for them, so they always smiled.","But one day, some bad guys invaded and began tormenting the people.","Because the king loved peace, he tried talking to the bad guys, but what do you think happened?","The bad guys ignored the king’s pleas and tormented his people even more!","Enraged, the king asked his remaining subjects to help him defeat the bad guys.","The people knew how kind their king was, so they gladly joined forces with him.","Thanks to that, the king and his people worked together and defeated the bad guys, but oh no!","An even worse guy appeared from among the bad guys!","The even worse guy was so powerful that even the kind king had difficulty defeating him.","But the king refused to give up and continued fighting to protect his people.","His people also fought without regard for their own lives for the sake of their benevolent king.","In the end, the king and his people defeated the even worse guy.","Having defeated all the bad guys, the king and his people dreamed of a happy future as they all departed together for dreamland.","...","└ From the undead’s perspective, he really was a kind king lmaooo.","└ For real lol. He was a wise and benevolent ruler of the undead.","Thinking of the day when everyone could smile together...","That’s basically it, right?","└ Heavenly Demon: You have a talent for fairy tales.","└ SwordMaster: Seriously. Weren’t old gruesome fairy tales all like that?","└ Allfather: Hohoho. If the Immortal King had seen this post, he would have coughed up blood.","└ Wild Grylls: He’s already dead, so I don’t think he’ll be coughing up any blood lol.","└ Damn. But when you compare it to what actually happened, it’s kind of chilling lol.","└ The part about \"fighting without regard for their own lives\" and the line about \"departing for dreamland\" are creepy as hell;;","That was what was happening while the gallery descended into chaos over the contents of the books I’d uploaded.","The Immortal King, the Balkan Kingdom, the Holy Kingdom, whatever.","None of it mattered.","What mattered to me was the information related to survival.","I didn’t care about some hidden historical truth.","’Talking about it in the gallery isn’t going to change anything anyway.’","Even if this whole mess spilled over into the real world, I didn’t care.","There was only one situation in which I’d need to care.","If I escaped the Forest of Four Seasons.","No matter how much trouble the Holy Kingdom caused over this, they couldn’t affect me at all while I was stuck here.","’The head moderator might be a little uncomfortable, though.’","The Holy Kingdom was a nation that worshipped the gods, and the head moderator was a deeply devout believer.","Now information that could shake the very foundations of that country had suddenly appeared.","Naturally, she’d probably be somewhat uncomfortable.","If she asked me to delete the posts, I’d happily do so.","The information had already spread everywhere anyway, and I’d already given the books to Allfather.","All I had to do was quietly watch.","I had no interest in anything involving the Immortal King.","’I’m not even sure people will believe it.’","Unless Allfather publicly revealed the physical books, it would be difficult for people to trust information that originated from the gallery.","It would also depend on the Holy Kingdom’s existing reputation.","If the Holy Kingdom already had a bad image, this could become a serious problem.","If it had a good reputation, people would probably dismiss the whole thing with, What kind of bullshit is that?","’Most organizations made up of people have something shady going on behind the scenes anyway.’","Just as stagnant water inevitably rots, groups of people eventually become corrupt as well.","Even if they started with good intentions, given enough time, corruption was inevitable.","Unless the people were periodically replaced, it would be difficult for any organization to remain clean forever.","’Well, that’s true everywhere, isn’t it?’","That was something for the people of that country to deal with.","As someone stuck inside the Forest of Four Seasons, I had even less reason to get involved.","I watched as criticism and condemnation of the Holy Kingdom began appearing throughout the gallery, then silently logged out.","It seemed like it would take a while before they deciphered the survival-related parts I actually wanted.","’Anyway, this means there’s at least some chance there are other survivors...’","The corpses I’d found this time had taught me something.","There was a good chance that more human remains existed somewhere in this forest.","Unlike the bodies that had presumably been eaten by the owlbear, there could also be remains like the book’s owner, preserved relatively intact.","’If there were people much stronger than me, they probably survived even longer.’","The owner of the books had been the last scribe of the Balkan Kingdom.","A scribe was someone associated more with letters than martial arts.","There was a chance he’d become stronger by surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons, just as I had.","Unfortunately, though, he probably hadn’t been able to use the gallery.","Even I couldn’t guarantee that I would’ve survived without the gallery.","That was a huge difference.","’From now on, I’ll have to search places like caves thoroughly.’","There wouldn’t have been much opportunity to build cabins in the Forest of Four Seasons, so most survivors had probably used caves as shelters.","’And it probably wasn’t just humans who came here, right?’","If I was incredibly lucky, I might even encounter someone.","Demons and elves in particular had a much higher baseline than other races.","They could easily manifest magic that humans had to rack their brains to learn.","Even without the gallery, having magic would provide an enormous advantage when it came to survival.","\"Though by this world’s standards, I’m a fucking idiot, so magic isn’t even worth dreaming about.\"","I’d given up on magic ages ago.","Apparently, they described fire using some kind of physics.","The moment I heard magic was particularly intertwined with mathematics, I’d abandoned the idea without hesitation.","I’d rather use \"magic\" through brute physical force.","’If there really is another survivor...’","Just knowing another person was out there would be comforting.","Until now, I’d thought I was completely alone.","Would I be able to find more traces of people?","It felt as though I’d gained a small new objective.","If escaping was my ultimate goal, then searching for traces of other survivors could be a smaller goal along the way.","’Didn’t they say most people who entered the Forest of Four Seasons were criminals?’","Criminals sentenced to the severe punishment of having their eyes gouged out before being sent inside.","Or criminals who had committed such horrific offenses that there was no longer any place for them in society.","Or, failing that, explorers who entered simply to prove their courage.","Of course, the chances of actually encountering any of them would be extremely low.","After all, they said the Forest of Four Seasons was about the size of a small country.","’Still, I can’t give up.’","It felt like I’d found another source of hope.","The hope that, if I was lucky, I might actually meet another person.","I let out a long breath and stood up.","’I should spend this time training instead.’","There was still some time left before dinner.","Rather than sitting around feeling sorry for myself, it would be better to practice my swordsmanship.","I picked up my sword and shield and began gradually working on the areas where I was lacking.","’I don’t care who it is. I just hope someone’s still alive.’","It was a very small wish.","***","Kadir was a man who wanted to know everything in the world.","Whether it concerned magic, people, or history made no difference.","Few things interested him more than truths hidden in darkness.","Such a thirst for knowledge could sometimes lead to ruin, but who was Kadir?","The Wizard King.","The master of the Magic Tower.","The man who had mastered every form of magic.","No matter how enormous it might be, a mere truth was nothing more than another curiosity to him.","\"Rice Kraone.\"","[...]","Kadir calmly spoke someone’s name.","The skull sitting by itself in front of him reacted.","A green glow appeared inside its empty eye sockets.","It was almost as though it had opened its eyes.","\"Do you know who that is?\"","The skull speaking with Kadir had originally been kept inside a freezer.","But considering that it had asked him to kill it, there was no doubt that it was anything but ordinary.","[How do you know that name?]","An eerie yet dignified voice flowed from the skull.","It didn’t sound like a voice produced by vocal cords. It felt more as though the words were being transmitted directly through thought.","Kadir—or rather, Allfather —was unfazed by the spine-chilling voice.","\"So what was written in the book really is true.\"","[I asked how you know that name.]","When Allfather failed to give him the answer he wanted, the skull—","No.","The Immortal King let out a sound of irritation.","At the same time, green energy enveloped the skull and blazed like flames.","It was deathly energy itself, surging and billowing around him.","Even with nothing but his head remaining, the Immortal King’s power had not disappeared.","\"I learned of it by coincidence. From the looks of things, your scribe fled to the Forest of Four Seasons.\"","[...]","\"If you answer my questions sincerely, I’ll tell you where and how I obtained this information.\"","The deathly energy surrounding the Immortal King gradually faded.","It was a silent permission to continue.","Allfather smiled broadly for a moment before his expression turned serious.","\"Why did you hide this truth?\"","[Because our kingdom was weak, and we lost. Is that enough of an answer?]","It was a cynical answer, yet one that cut straight to the nature of the world.","The weak inevitably had many things taken from them by the strong.","Truth was no exception.","More importantly, history was written by the victors.","The records of the defeated could only be distorted and erased.","Allfather stroked his beard as though he finally understood.","\"I’ve known for a long time that the Holy Kingdom was rotten, but I never imagined it was this bad. Thanks to you, they underwent a purge once already. Does that mean what we have now is actually the improved version?\"","[...]","\"No, I suppose not. They still went and exiled the Hero... Tsk, tsk. I suppose they still haven’t learned their lesson.\"","The Holy Kingdom of Eldorado did not have what anyone could honestly call a good reputation.","Originally, it had been founded upon the conviction that the Demon King had to be defeated, but that purpose had faded with time.","Recently, the demons had even become so obsessed with sports rather than fighting that they barely paid attention to the other nations.","If anything, they had become more interested in culture, while the Demon King had increasingly come to be regarded as little more than the king of the demons.","Normally, an organization that had lost its purpose should simply disband.","But Eldorado was an entire country.","Because it had been forcibly held together despite losing its original purpose, the water naturally became stagnant.","And stagnant water inevitably rotted.","[Now answer my question. How did you learn the truth?]","While Allfather had been muttering to himself, the Immortal King’s eerie voice interrupted him.","Allfather snapped his fingers.","A book appeared in his hand.","\"This.\"","It was the record left behind by Rice Kraone, the last scribe of the Balkan Kingdom.","Rustle—","Allfather kindly opened the book to its first page and showed it to him.","Despite having no eyeballs, the Immortal King’s gaze seemed to move along the page.","Then, seeing his native language for the first time in ages, the Immortal King let out a stunned breath.","He spoke in a tone of disbelief.","[I cannot believe it. I ordered him to flee to the Forest of Four Seasons.]","\"That’s where this was found.\"","[Impossible. The Forest of Four Seasons is a labyrinth from which no one can ever escape.]","\"That’s true as well. But I’m not the one who found it.\"","Allfather briefly summarized everything that had happened.","How Grylls had fallen into the Forest of Four Seasons.","How he was somehow able to use the gallery from inside it.","How, after enduring hardship after hardship there, he’d stumbled across the corpse and the books by chance.","The Immortal King listened silently before finally speaking.","[I cannot believe it.]","\"It’s all true. So, what do you want to do?\"","[What do you mean?]","Allfather casually flipped through the book, which he had now completely deciphered, and explained.","\"I’m asking whether you’d like to strike a blow against the Holy Kingdom. I’m not particularly fond of them either.\"","[...]","\"The previous Hero who died together with you was a friend of mine. And the reason she resorted to mutual destruction in the first place was because she couldn’t withstand the Holy Kingdom’s pressure...\"","Allfather paused.","\"In practical terms, they murdered her.\"","[Do as you please. But I have one condition.]","\"A condition?\"","Allfather raised an eyebrow.","The Immortal King stared directly at him before making his request in a voice filled with something close to resignation.","[Kill me.]","\"Later.\"","[Damn it.]","At the immediate refusal, the Immortal King muttered a quiet curse.","It was fairly mild as far as curses went, but considering that he had once been a king, it was remarkably strong language.","\"Any other requests?\"","[I want to know who found the records.]","\"I told you I obtained them through the gallery.\"","[Help me gain access to that gallery.]","\"Don’t be ridiculous. You clearly...\"","Allfather stopped mid-sentence.","An amusing thought had suddenly occurred to him.","Ordinary undead had no sense of self.","Their wills were so faint that they were closer to monsters than people.","But the Immortal King was an exception.","Even after losing his entire body, he had retained a perfectly intact sense of self.","In that case...","Couldn’t he access the gallery too?","[You’re making a perverted expression.]","\"Ah. My apologies. An interesting thought occurred to me.\"","[So, will you help me?]","\"Of course I will.\"","[Even though I could reveal your location?]","It was almost a threat.","And at the same time, a foolish question.","Allfather chuckled and gave him a perfectly reasonable answer.","\"Who would believe a story about the Immortal King who once plunged the entire continent into terror sitting inside someone’s refrigerator?\"","[...]","\"I’m absolutely not setting you free. I’m merely telling you to entertain yourself on the gallery.\"","The Immortal King spent a long while silently considering Allfather’s words.","At last, seemingly having reached a decision, he made another request in a calm voice.","[Please kill me.]","\"Later.\"","That request wasn’t getting granted anytime soon."]},{"title":"Chapter 98","paragraphs":["Firewood (1)","There is a word called \"bait.\"","Usually, it refers to bait used to lure fish.","Because of its characteristic of attracting fish, however, the word is often used with other meanings as well.","The same goes for the gallery. If you throw out a huge piece of bait, the fish will come swarming in.","The bigger the bait, the more fish gather around it, and every now and then, you even hook a big one.","[Upvote if you’re glad the Holy Kingdom is screwed lol]","[Even the Immortal King is pitiful.]","[So Eldorado was the real Demon King all along lol]","[Demon Kings aren’t born.]","[Wonder when we’ll get the Holy Kingdom’s response.]","’When is this going to die down?’","Evening had arrived.","I stared at the gallery, which was still blazing over the Immortal King controversy, and wondered about it.","I didn’t know whether it was because this had happened relatively recently or because the Holy Kingdom’s ugliness was simply that outrageous.","One thing was certain: there was no sign of the flames dying down anytime soon.","I think I was starting to understand what I had done.","’I just need to make a proper statement tomorrow.’","I closed the gallery. It was about time to head up to the river.","The outside world could deal with its own affairs. I just had to worry about surviving.","Pleasure without responsibility?","What am I supposed to do when I couldn’t take responsibility even if I wanted to?","Besides, I couldn’t exactly call it pleasure. I had revealed the information because I wanted to improve my own chances of survival, even if only a little.","I had no idea that the Immortal King or some hidden evil festering in the world would be involved.","’Though I still would’ve posted it even if I’d known.’","What did I know about this world, anyway?","I’d woken up in the Forest of Four Seasons before I even had a chance to learn anything about it.","Sure, I had the gallery, but a community forum wasn’t exactly the place to learn about the world.","’Will this cause problems if I ever get out?’","Even that depended on one condition.","The admin would have to reveal my address in real time.","Otherwise, there was no way people could find me.","’Ugh. Forget it. There’s no point thinking about this.’","I’d just watch and see what the Holy Kingdom had to say tomorrow.","I sighed inwardly as I arrived at the river.","There were exactly two fish caught in the trap.","Another feast today.","Delighted, I pulled up the fish trap.","Squirm. Squirm.","\"Hm?\"","Fish weren’t the only things caught inside.","An octopus of unknown origin was wriggling around in there.","Its body wasn’t glowing blue or anything, so it didn’t seem to be venomous. It looked like an ordinary octopus.","Nor did it look anywhere near as monstrous as the octopus I’d encountered on the sandy beach before.","’Is it because seawater is flowing backward into the river?’","Ever since that torrential downpour, all sorts of creatures had been getting caught.","Well, from my perspective, more things to eat was a good thing.","Besides, I’d never eaten octopus in this forest before, so trying it once didn’t sound bad.","’But were octopus legs always this thin? Maybe it’s a long-arm octopus?’","For now, I decided to carry the entire trap back with me. It was small, so I planned to eat it right away.","As for cooking it, I figured boiling it in water or stir-frying it would work.","Whether it was an octopus or a long-arm octopus, it was ultimately going to be my dinner.","That hadn’t changed.","Eventually, I returned to the cave and was just about to transfer the food from the trap into a container when—","Whip!","\"Huh?\"","The thing—whether it was an octopus or a long-arm octopus—wrapped itself around my arm.","It moved so quickly that I froze for a moment, and in that instant, another of its legs wrapped around somewhere else.","Clench!","\"Ghk! Kgh!\"","Right around my neck.","I couldn’t breathe.","I desperately tried to tear away the octopus leg that had begun strangling me.","But it was so absurdly strong that I could barely pry it loose.","Worse, I could feel something sticking to me. Its suckers must have latched onto my neck.","\"Ghhk...! Kgh...!\"","At this rate, I was obviously going to suffocate.","As my consciousness gradually began to fade, I groped around with my hand.","The dagger I’d left nearby for preparing food.","My hand closed around it.","Slice—slice—slice—slash!","I desperately hacked through the octopus’s legs, and before long, the pressure around my neck eased.","But the octopus apparently had no intention of giving up, because it tightened its remaining legs around me even harder.","My vision was starting to turn yellow.","I circulated the mana inside my body and continued cutting through the legs.","Crack! Riiip!","I severed every leg that had been tightly constricting my neck.","Finally, I grabbed its head with one hand and forcibly ripped it off me.","The octopus was still desperately trying to kill me, but all its legs had already been cut away.","\"Cough! Cough! Haaah... Ngh.\"","I coughed and glared at the octopus in my hand.","It had only one leg left.","Watching it flail around, still trying to cut off my breath with just that one pathetic limb, was almost laughable.","Bam!","I showed no mercy to animals that tried to kill me.","I carried out its execution immediately.","I slammed the octopus onto the cutting board and drove my dagger into its head.","Apparently I hit a vital spot, because the octopus rapidly turned white before going completely limp.","\"Ugh. Seriously.\"","Pop! Pop-pop!","I peeled the severed legs off my neck.","The suckers had attached themselves so firmly that it felt like I was peeling off duct tape.","\"Phew...\"","When I put the legs on the cutting board, they were still writhing.","They looked so grotesque that I wanted to get rid of them as quickly as possible.","’What kind of octopus tries to strangle someone?’","Considering it hadn’t sprayed any ink, maybe it really was a long-arm octopus rather than an octopus.","Either way, that had been dangerous.","Once again, I’d learned that I couldn’t let my guard down just because something was small.","’I’m going to make sure to chew you into tiny pieces.’","They were the same legs that had wrapped around my neck, but I didn’t care.","Such \"minor\" hygiene concerns weren’t a problem.","While I was at it, I could also write down a record of the long-arm octopus in my journal.","I’d gained quite a lot today.","Sizzle—sizzle—sizzle—sizzle.","Eating it alive didn’t really appeal to me, so I decided to cook it in a pan.","There was such a thing as stir-fried long-arm octopus, but I didn’t have any sauce for that.","It would probably be fine if I just tossed it in while cooking the fish.","Chew. Chew.","\"Mmm. Tastes good.\"","It had the distinctive fishy smell of marine life, but its rich, savory flavor completely covered it.","And I was eating it together with fish.","The umami of the fish flesh blended perfectly with it, delighting my taste buds.","\"Wonmo, you can have the head.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","I gave the head to Wonmo.","Naturally, I cut it into small pieces and cooked it thoroughly so he wouldn’t choke.","For the record, Namu-Ppareumbo adamantly refused.","Well, it was an herbivore, so that made sense.","I polished off another filling dinner.","There had been a crisis in the middle of it, but I seemed to have gotten through it safely enough.","’The smaller they are around here, the more dangerous they are.’","Until now, I’d mostly been threatened by enormous monsters.","But thinking about it now, being huge might actually be a disadvantage when it came to survival.","Namu-Ppareumbo, for example, was smaller than me, yet it was absurdly strong.","And especially that saber-toothed tiger that had possessed a dragon heart.","Its regeneration had been powerful, but because of its massive size, it had left plenty of openings.","The same was true of the orichalcum Protector. The smaller ones were more dangerous.","’...Let’s make an exception for crabs and crayfish.’","Those things were practically the definition of \"monsters,\" so it was better to treat them as exceptions.","After finishing all the cleanup, I went back into the cave to write in my journal.","Scratch, scratch—scratch, scratch—","The corpse was worth noting, but the most important thing was the long-arm octopus. I carefully wrote down everything I had learned about it.","After getting such a harsh lesson today, I probably wouldn’t fall victim to a similar attack again. Still, keeping a record was essential.","There was always the chance I could injure my head and lose my memory.","’I’m done with the journal, so it’s time to practice the internal energy cultivation method.’","I was gradually getting used to the cultivation method as well. All I had to do was close my eyes and concentrate a little, and I could vividly sense the mana inside my body.","I should start taking the inner cores tomorrow or the day after. I’d begin with just one.","After finishing all my training, I logged into the gallery.","I wanted to see whether it was still blazing over the Immortal King controversy.","’Nothing’s changed.’","There wasn’t much difference.","The gallery was still on fire.","It was impressive that the flames had lasted this long even though no one had thrown any additional firewood onto them.","Even the admin wasn’t trying to stop it. According to the rules, posts that encouraged conflict between nations were supposed to be prohibited.","’Maybe it’s because this technically isn’t a conflict between nations?’","The countries currently being mentioned were the Holy Kingdom, Eldorado, and the Balkan Kingdom.","The Balkan Kingdom had already fallen long ago. There couldn’t exactly be a conflict with it.","Mephisto, the nation of demons where the \"Demon King\" resided, was occasionally mentioned as well, but only rarely.","Most of the posts were criticizing or outright condemning Eldorado.","’I should ask the admin and the Heavenly Demon, just in case.’","It wasn’t that I was worried about Eldorado.","I simply felt indifferent toward it.","Just how terrible had its reputation been for everyone to seize this opportunity and start cursing it out?","But if posts like these kept springing up everywhere, the mods would have their hands full.","I wasn’t worried about Eldorado.","I was worried about the people who would have to deal with the mess.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you there by any chance?]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady is always waiting for a chance to converse with you.]","The Heavenly Demon was the first person I contacted.","The admin occasionally disappeared, so I planned to ask them afterward.","[Wild Grylls: It seems like the gallery is in chaos because of me right now. I was wondering if you were busy because of it...]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady understands what you mean. You need not worry too much. This sort of thing happened often even before this.]","[Wild Grylls: It happened often?]","[Heavenly Demon: Indeed. Whenever something happened in the world, the gallery tended to erupt like this. Occasionally, the trouble spills over into the real world, but such cases are exceedingly rare.]","[Wild Grylls: So if we just leave it alone, it’ll die down on its own.]","[Heavenly Demon: As long as the nation called the Holy Kingdom does not throw more firewood onto the flames.]","So in the end, I wouldn’t know how things would turn out until tomorrow.","I’d already suspected as much, so I didn’t think too deeply about it.","[Wild Grylls: Then what if the Holy Kingdom gives a terrible explanation?]","[Heavenly Demon: It will burn even more fiercely than it does now. That is when things will become busy.]","[Wild Grylls: I hope that doesn’t happen.]","[Heavenly Demon: Are you worried?]","[Wild Grylls: Of course. My posts might get buried.]","[Heavenly Demon: Hmm. A most serious matter indeed.]","The gallery’s posting rate was insane right now.","If I closed it for a moment and opened it again, another one or two pages of posts would already have appeared.","For someone like me who depended heavily on the gallery, this was a very serious situation.","At least direct person-to-person trading was possible. Otherwise, this would have been a real headache.","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Yes! I’m here! What is it?]","Fortunately, the admin seemed to be logged into the gallery.","I wondered what to say before deciding to simply ask about the current situation.","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady will seek out your posts and read them regardless, so do not worry. This Lady will always support you.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Wild Grylls: Admin, you’ve dealt with situations like this a lot, right?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: It happens all the time! And it’s a pain every time!]","I felt a little guilty since I was the one who had created this particular headache.","After receiving reassurance from the Heavenly Demon, I turned to the admin, Don’t Abandon the Hero.","They were probably the person suffering the biggest headache in the gallery right now.","I felt even more apologetic because they were the one who had given me privileges.","[Wild Grylls: Admin, are you there?]","[Wild Grylls: I didn’t know this would happen either. I’m sorry.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: You don’t need to apologize! I don’t think you posted it with that kind of intention!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. But what happens to me once this whole controversy dies down?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: It might be different if you’d acted maliciously, but you didn’t have any malicious intent, so I don’t think there’ll be a problem!]","[Wild Grylls: That’s a relief.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Besides, deleting it now might make the gallery explode even more!]","That was probably true.","I’d heard of something like that before.","Trying to hide something only made people more interested in it.","In the end, I wouldn’t know whether the controversy would die down until tomorrow.","[Wild Grylls: I’ve ended up making things difficult for you without meaning to. I’d like to apologize again.]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: It’s fine! If the Holy Kingdom did something wrong, then they did something wrong, and if they didn’t, then they didn’t!]","[Wild Grylls: Are you from the Holy Kingdom, Admin?]","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: Yes! It is a nation blessed by the gods, especially the Goddess!]","Patriotism practically overflowed from the answer.","If all those atrocities turned out to be true, wouldn’t that affection disappear?","[Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ll say it again, but you really don’t need to apologize! There must be some kind of misunderstanding!]","[Wild Grylls: Probably. I hope they explain themselves properly.]","That way, my posts wouldn’t get buried.","I finished my conversation with the admin and browsed through the gallery.","Most of it was about the Immortal King controversy, so there weren’t any interesting posts.","There were occasionally people who tried to take advantage of the lull to post about something else, but those posts were buried before long.","’I guess I’ll practice aura until bedtime.’","Since the gallery wasn’t entertaining either, I practiced controlling my aura.","The more time passed, the more aura came pouring out on its own, making it increasingly difficult to control, but I still had to practice.","I channeled mana into Cheonma’s sword, generating aura.","The aura shimmered around the blade like a heat haze.","My first task was to shape it into something sharp.","\"...\"","As expected, it wasn’t easy.","Apparently, this was the sort of thing that depended on talent.","I extinguished the aura and began maintaining my equipment.","’There really isn’t much to do without the gallery.’","Especially before bedtime.","Even training became harmful if you overdid it.","’I only smoke when things get rough. I guess I’ll just practice the internal energy cultivation method.’","Until I found a decent hobby, it looked like I’d have to fill my spare time with internal energy cultivation.","And so, that eventful day came to an end, and the next morning dawned.","Now that a new day had arrived, the controversy in the gallery should have cooled down somewhat.","Unless someone had thrown more firewood onto the flames, it should at least have lost some momentum.","[Eldorado Holy Kingdom: Here Is What Really Happened.]","I already have a bad feeling about this."]},{"title":"Chapter 99","paragraphs":["Firewood (2)","This world is a place where many different races and peoples live together.","As such, it is incredibly complex, and the differences between their respective cultures are so significant that conflicts have arisen since ancient times.","People are naturally inclined to discriminate against or look unfavorably upon those who are different from them.","Therefore, it could be said that disputes both large and small Arising from such differences are only natural.","Yet amid all these differences, there is one thing capable of uniting vast numbers of people.","Gods.","In other words, religion.","Religion has wielded enormous influence from the conflict-ridden days of antiquity all the way to the present.","Moreover, the existence of gods in this world is indisputable.","The proof lies in \"divine power.\"","It is sacred power granted by the gods, an energy said to be the purest form of mana.","Those capable of wielding divine power can exercise far greater strength than ordinary beings.","Of course, there is the requirement that they possess genuine faith, but considering the benefits, that is a reasonable price to pay.","Title) Where did all the gods go?","They say the gods used to descend into the world personally back in the day. Where are they all now?","ᄂ Probably went home.","ᄂ What home? Lmaoooo","ᄂ It happened so long ago that nobody knows. Even the elves and demons don’t know.","ᄂ I think they just taught humanity about magic and mana, and that was it?","ᄂ They’re probably somewhere. They wouldn’t be gods otherwise.","Countless gods existed, but if one had to name the most famous among them, it would undoubtedly be Ares.","The Goddess of War and Wisdom, and the younger sister of Aragon, the God of Magic.","There was also the Chief God, their father and a deity of higher standing than either of them, but his influence was smaller than Ares’s.","That was because, back when humanity was weak, Ares had protected mankind from the evils of the world.","For that reason, countless people worshiped Ares.","Even demons were no exception.","Considering that she was the Goddess of War, there was no reason demons wouldn’t worship her as well.","In this way, Ares and the other gods had left an enormous mark on human history, and their influence continued even now.","One example was Eldorado, a nation founded for the worship of the gods.","Bang!","\"How did this happen?! We were so certain we had concealed it perfectly!\"","A stern-looking old man slammed his hand down on the table and shouted.","His voice had weakened considerably with age, but it could not conceal the venom within it.","\"How could we have anticipated this either? For now, please calm yourself. The people are only demanding an explanation. They haven’t completely accepted the allegations as truth.\"","Another old man sitting across from him responded.","His luxuriant beard suited him remarkably well, but his snake-like eyes radiated a sinister air.","His voice sounded every bit as stubborn as the other old man’s.","\"Cardinal Morgan is correct. The people are still waiting for our answer.\"","An old man with a distinctive mustache spoke while gently tugging at it.","The slight upward tilt of his chin made him look exceedingly arrogant.","Each of them looked different, but they shared one thing in common.","They were all dressed in white clerical robes that exuded an air of holiness.","Yet the patterns decorating those robes, seemingly gilded in gold, almost seemed to expose their greed.","\"This is no time to fight among ourselves. The people outside are demanding an explanation as we speak. We must devise a solution immediately.\"","The voice was dignified and solemn.","At the same time, it carried subtle pressure.","The old men turned their gazes toward the head of the table.","The man sitting there had more wrinkles than any of the others.","Yet the sharpness in his eyes was no less intense than that of a young man.","Although that sharpness carried an ominous quality, the old man possessed an aura that made him seem unapproachable.","\"If any of you have a good idea, speak.\"","Louis II, the current Pope of the Holy Kingdom of Eldorado, spoke quietly.","Under the pressure of his command, the old men cleared their throats.","The old man who had slammed the table was the first to speak.","\"First, we deny everything without exception. What evidence do they have besides a post uploaded to the gallery?\"","\"Cardinal Howards is correct. Posts from the gallery are notorious for their lack of credibility.\"","Eldorado had been in chaos since morning.","The controversy surrounding the Immortal King that had begun in the gallery had now spilled over into the real world.","The Immortal King incident had occurred only thirty years ago.","Its scars still remained painfully vivid.","Those who had lost their parents.","Those who had lost their children.","Those who had lost their homes.","Those who had lost parts of their bodies.","Those who had lost everything.","They had gathered together and were now protesting in front of the Papal Palace.","Crash!!","The meeting was being conducted in secret.","Suddenly, a stained-glass window shattered, scattering shards everywhere.","The startled cardinals flinched.","Then furious shouts began pouring in from outside.","[Bring our son back! Bring our son back!]","[And you call yourselves clergy?! You claim to believe in the gods?!]","[If you have mouths, then speak!]","The voices came through the shattered window.","In truth, the room they were in was located far from the entrance of the Papal Palace.","They had even chosen a high floor for the meeting for safety, yet somehow a stone had still managed to reach them.","It was hardly surprising, considering that some of the protesters outside were former knights.","\"W-What are you doing?! Drag out whoever threw that stone!\"","\"W-We’re having difficulty identifying them...!\"","\"You useless fools!!\"","There was nothing the Holy Knight who had belatedly rushed in could do.","That was how fiercely the people’s anger was burning.","One might wonder how things could escalate this far over a single post on the gallery.","But this was a world with newspapers and a press.","And whenever the press caught wind of a sensational story, it was bound to pounce on it.","It didn’t matter even if the story had originated as mere controversy on the gallery.","[We believed in the gods, not you bastards!]","[If you have any conscience, the Pope should step down voluntarily!]","[How dare you disgrace Lady Ares!!]","More than anything, Eldorado’s already poor reputation had contributed greatly to the situation.","Eldorado had been founded as a nation devoted to worshiping the gods, and originally, it had enjoyed a pristine reputation.","Conveniently enough, it had been founded during an era when the demons of Mephisto were running rampant, allowing Eldorado to establish itself as a force of \"justice.\"","But as time passed, the demons became obsessed with something as trivial as playing ball, and the old antagonism between the two sides gradually faded.","And as that conflict faded, the atrocities Eldorado had committed over the years slowly began coming to light.","’How irritating.’","Louis II frowned and pressed his fingers firmly against his temples.","Seeing that, the other cardinals busied themselves watching Louis’s mood.","The current Pope, Louis, wielded more power than anyone else in Eldorado’s history.","One wrong word, and their heads could be at risk. Being a cardinal wouldn’t save them.","\"...Come to think of it, have any other nations issued statements?\"","\"Ah, yes! None so far.\"","\"None so far....\"","As mentioned earlier, Eldorado had committed no small number of atrocities.","One of those was pressuring neighboring nations while invoking the name of the gods.","It didn’t matter even if the nation in question was Alvenheim, the land of the elves.","Eldorado’s will was the will of the gods.","Anyone who defied the will of the gods became an enemy of the world.","Normally, Eldorado’s will should have followed the will of the gods, but the relationship had been completely reversed.","That alone showed just how immense the authority and power of religion had become.","And as always, stagnant water eventually rotted.","The stench of that corruption had grown stronger than any desire to follow the gods’ will, reaching a point where it could no longer be ignored.","\"So, do you have a solution?\"","\"Pardon?\"","\"I asked if you have a solution. If you intend to keep your mouths shut, then leave.\"","The moment they left, their heads would roll.","The cardinals could already foresee their futures.","How much hardship had they endured to rise to their current positions?","They absolutely could not give them up.","\"It will be difficult to simply deny everything outright. If, by any chance, a survivor of the Balkan Kingdom appears, matters will become even more complicated.\"","\"We can appeal to the public by saying we had no choice. The context surrounding the incident is what matters, isn’t it? The Immortal King was conducting experiments to turn his own people into undead first.\"","Desperate to avoid the Pope’s wrath, the cardinals racked their brains.","If anyone else were to hear the contents of this meeting, they would immediately realize that the records Grylls had uploaded to the gallery were true.","Just as stagnant water inevitably rotted, there was no trace left of the noble faith they had once possessed.","Instead, they were entirely preoccupied with concealing their own wrongdoing.","\"Good. Then that is what we’ll do.\"","\"Once the angry masses hear our side of the story, they will surely repent.\"","\"By the way, what are we going to do about that gallery?\"","The moment the mustached cardinal spoke, the atmosphere that had been on the verge of turning jovial immediately sank.","After all, the current crisis had originated in the gallery.","No one knew what sort of controversy might emerge from it next.","\"That’s simple.\"","Louis spoke with a vaguely unsettling smile.","When the cardinals turned toward him, Louis presented his solution.","\"Why don’t we take this opportunity to declare the gallery evil?\"","\"The gallery...?\"","\"Yes. We are those blessed by the gods. Our will is the will of the gods. Therefore, if we declare the gallery evil, it means the gods themselves have declared it evil as well.\"","As stated before, they had completely reversed the proper order of things.","Their desire to follow the will of the gods had been corrupted long ago.","But the desire for power was not something easily restrained.","\"That sounds excellent. We should take this opportunity to impose sweeping restrictions on the gallery as well. Hahaha.\"","\"There is nothing more dangerous than ignorant masses being exposed to false information.\"","\"Come to think of it, I hear indecent things are uploaded there as well. What is this world coming to?\"","And so, they began declaring the gallery evil.","Of course—","’I’m still going to use it.’","’I’ll just use it secretly.’","’It’s fine as long as I don’t get caught.’","Hypocrisy was practically a passive skill for them, so all they did was spout words that sounded respectable on the surface.","After the meeting concluded, a spokesperson appeared before the public.","In a situation like this, the Pope should have stepped forward personally.","The fact that he sent a spokesperson instead was enough to show his arrogance.","\"Descendants of the gods, hear me! This entire incident is nothing more than a misunderstanding! The wicked king of the Balkan Kingdom, the Immortal King, had long been conducting necromantic experiments upon his own people...!\"","Here Is What Really Happened.","The Immortal King had been conducting sinister experiments on his people.","The Holy Kingdom had discovered what was happening beforehand and had been forced to carry out the massacre.","Was it not far better for them to die as humans than to die as undead?","All of this had been done according to the will of the gods, and those who had lived through the incident were suffering from psychological trauma.","As the explanation continued, the crowd gradually began to calm down.","Of course, they didn’t exactly look convinced yet.","Still, at least the Holy Kingdom was offering an explanation.","Apparently, they had enough nerve to brazenly lie straight to everyone’s faces.","Trust in the Holy Kingdom had already hit rock bottom.","Now people were simply waiting to see whether there was an even deeper abyss beneath it.","\"Furthermore, His Holiness the Pope has declared the gallery to be a true evil, and those who believe the false information spread through the gallery will face severe punishment—!\"","\"You fucking bastards!!\"","\"I knew it! You’re saying that crap because there’s something you want to hide!!\"","\"What did you say about the gallery?! Are you that desperate to get your head chopped off like the Emperor of the Central Plains?!\"","\"Stop blaming the gallery for everything! We’re sick and tired of it!!!\"","Someone had once said that even rock bottom had a rock bottom beneath it.","Blaming the gallery whenever anything went wrong was already a routine they had been repeating for years.","Normally, people would have simply brushed it off with—","Ugh. Those bastards are at it again.","But the public’s anger had already exceeded its breaking point.","This time, even that wouldn’t work.","\"Everyone! Breaking news! The Mage King Kadir has issued a statement!\"","\"What? The Mage King?\"","\"Isn’t he a close friend of the previous Hero?\"","Amid the rapidly worsening chaos, someone delivered the news.","The spokesperson felt a terrible sense of foreboding upon hearing it.","But it was already too late.","\"The previous Hero did not die together with the Immortal King! He chose to die with the Immortal King! And he made that choice because of the Holy Kingdom’s pressure and coercion!\"","\"What does that even mean?\"","\"The previous Hero chose death? Are you saying he committed suicide?\"","\"Can you... even call that suicide? That’s more like...!\"","At exactly the right moment, Kadir tossed another piece of oil-soaked firewood onto the flames.","\"Bring out the Pope! Tell him to come out here and explain himself!\"","\"Bring my son back!\"","\"Give me back my father!\"","The inferno showed no sign of dying down anytime soon.","Meanwhile, at that very moment, in the Forest of Four Seasons—","\"Cough. Cough! Ugh. Did I put in too much firewood?\"","Grylls was adding firewood to prepare breakfast."]},{"title":"Chapter 100","paragraphs":["Firewood (3)","Title) Holy Kingdom of Eldorado: Here Is What Really Happened","Eldorado had known about the Immortal King’s plan for quite some time.","The Immortal King had transformed his citizens into undead in an instant, and what happened beforehand had merely been groundwork for that plan.","We believed that they could retain at least a minimum of human dignity by dying as humans rather than undead, and therefore we had no choice but to kill them.","Many people still suffer from psychological trauma because of what happened.","Furthermore, all of these lies originated from the gallery. Therefore, from this point forward, we will designate the gallery as evil.","Please do not dare question the will of the gods. We are doing our utmost as well.","That’s roughly what I heard? These bastards are trying to declare the gallery evil again, lmao.","ᄂ That’s the Holy Kingdom for you, lol.","ᄂ They would’ve been fine if they’d just left the gallery out of it, but they just had to ruin it, lol.","ᄂ But people don’t seem to be buying all that, do they?","ᄂ Yeah, the general reaction was basically, \"What the hell are you talking about?\" Probably because the Holy Kingdom’s reputation is already trash.","ᄂ They’re throwing more firewood onto the flames themselves, lol.","ᄂ If that was really what happened, they would’ve said so ages ago.","ᄂ Who the hell would believe them? Lmao.","ᄂ Serves them right after constantly throwing around \"the will of the gods\" and acting all high and mighty.","ᄂ Breaking news. Kadir released a statement. The previous Hero chose to commit suicide.","ᄂ ??? What the hell does that mean now?","ᄂ Didn’t the previous Hero die together with the Immortal King?","ᄂ Yeah, they died together, but apparently it was basically suicide.","ᄂ Whoa... I heard the previous Hero was an incredibly good person.","ᄂ Did the Holy Kingdom pressure him? People these days say the clergy barely have any genuine faith left.","ᄂ If that’s true, there might be a riot.","ᄂ I doubt it’ll go as far as a riot. What can anyone do if they keep denying everything to the bitter end?","ᄂ It’ll be a different story if witnesses start coming forward one by one.","ᄂ Forget all that. Upvote if you’re happy the Holy Kingdom is fucked, lmao.","ᄂ Starting with me, lol.","ᄂ This is honestly so satisfying! Those bastards call everything \"the will of the gods,\" lmao.","ᄂ The funniest part is that they tell believers the path is open to everyone, but if you’re not from the Holy Kingdom, you can’t even become a bishop, lol.","ᄂ Their discrimination against demons is especially fucking bad. They treat them like terrorists or something.","The bait I had thrown out without thinking.","The bait I had expected to die down after a single day.","It had gone beyond being discussed in the real world and transformed into a raging inferno.","The overwhelming majority of posts were cursing the Holy Kingdom.","There wasn’t a single good thing being said about it.","Title) What the hell did Eldorado ever do wrong, guys?","Did they pressure neighboring countries while claiming it was the will of the gods or something?","Did they falsely accuse innocent people of heresy and torture them to death or something?","Did clergymen enter the slums and kill people or something?","Did they admit they were too busy to pray or something?","Did they double taxes in regions where people didn’t pay enough offerings or something?","Did they declare sports to be a drug and then get Molotov cocktails thrown at them by fans or something?","Did they constantly attack the gallery only to get caught looking at porn themselves or something?","Did they pass a law preventing foreigners from rising above the rank of archbishop or something?","Did they call the common people pigs and dogs because \"they’ll forget soon enough\" or something?","Did they try to forcibly establish a federation to subjugate the Demon King, only to get chewed out by the Empire or something?","And on top of all that, did they fuck over the Balkan Kingdom or something?","During the Immortal King incident, did they turn refugees away because they claimed they were infected or something?","When a plague spread because of the undead, did they conduct experiments on humans or something?","Seriously, what has Eldorado ever done to deserve being mocked?","I just can’t understand it.","\"Wow.\"","So they were just fucking awful.","Rotten all the way through.","People said stagnant water eventually rotted, but this had gone beyond rotting and turned into petroleum.","No.","Petroleum was at least useful for something.","This was just garbage.","’Every country has a dark side, but this is a bit much.’","That post alone made me immediately understand why the Holy Kingdom’s reputation was so terrible.","Especially the part about people from other countries being unable to rise above the rank of archbishop.","That was basically an open declaration that they intended to keep all the good positions for themselves.","It was blatantly unfair.","’Can a religion really become this corrupt?’","I hate gods, but I don’t hate religion or the people who believe in it.","I’m wary of extremists, sure, but some of the people who helped me when I was struggling were religious themselves.","But these people...","They seemed less like religious believers and more like rotten politicians.","Unless enough time passed for those people to die off, or a rebellion broke out like someone had suggested, it would probably be difficult for anything to change.","’People are the same everywhere.’","Even in a different world, people apparently didn’t change much.","I watched as the gallery began filling with every imaginable joke and meme before quietly closing it.","It seemed like it would take quite a while before the information I actually wanted showed up.","If all else failed, I could just ask Allfather.","’Still, declaring the gallery evil? Seriously?’","What kind of ridiculous way of handling things was that?","At least the fact that they weren’t threatening to hunt me down suggested they still had some brains.","Not that they could catch me even if they wanted to.","I was in the Forest of Four Seasons.","It was impossible.","I just had to focus on what I needed to do.","\"Cough! Cough! Ugh.\"","I coughed from the acrid smoke.","The campfire had been too weak, so I’d added more firewood, only to overdo it.","I couldn’t exactly take the wood back out now, which left me in a bit of a predicament.","’I should start thinking about other cooking methods.’","Grilling directly over a fire, cooking food on a cast-iron pan over an open flame, and so on.","Those methods alone were enough to keep me fed, but they had a drawback.","The fish that made up my staple diet were simply too damn big.","Even excluding the head, merely flipping one over was a chore.","Because of that, parts would sometimes burn while others remained undercooked.","The results were inconsistent.","’Would an oven be better for something like this?’","If I had a masonry oven—an actual oven—I could minimize burnt or undercooked portions.","It would also have the advantage of letting me do other things while the food cooked.","Now that I had decided to live here for a long time, an oven was practically a necessity.","’I should try making one.’","Asking the entire gallery seemed unnecessary when there was one regular in particular who was perfect for the job.","Conveniently, I could also obtain materials from him, killing two birds with one stone.","[Wild Grylls: Hey. You there?]","[Passing Dwarf: Yeah. Why?]","[Wild Grylls: You’re actually awake for once? I figured you’d be lying around half-dead from drinking.]","[Passing Dwarf: I didn’t drink much yesterday. Anyway, why’d you call me?]","[Wild Grylls: Nothing major. I’m thinking of building an oven. I’ll buy the bricks from the auction house, but I wanted to get some tips from you.]","[Passing Dwarf: Just because I’m a dwarf doesn’t mean I know how to make everything ;; I specialize in metallurgy, you idiot.]","[Wild Grylls: Aren’t all dwarves supposed to be good with their hands?]","[Passing Dwarf: That’s separate from actually having expertise. I can get you a metal plate to use in the oven, though, so let me know.]","[Wild Grylls: Make it big enough to fit a whole fish easily. You know how big they are, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: I’ll make it lol. Give me a piece next time you cook one in the oven.]","[Wild Grylls: Lol. Oh, right. Give me the barricade too.]","[Passing Dwarf: Forgot about that. I’ll send it when I give you the metal plate.]","In that case, I should get everything ready before the dwarf sent it over.","I’d woken up at six this morning. I’d spent thirty minutes on the gallery.","I usually ate breakfast around seven or seven-thirty, so I could work on the oven until then.","If it proved too difficult to finish, I could just cook breakfast on the griddle like usual.","No problem there.","Splash! Splash!","There were three fish in the trap today.","It seemed like I caught three whenever I checked after waking up, and two at other times.","’There won’t be another long-arm octopus, right?’","Even if it wasn’t a long-arm octopus, I intended to immediately go on guard if I saw any other creature.","Fortunately, there was nothing inside besides the fish.","Humming to myself, I carried the trap full of fish back down.","Rustle!","Then I heard something moving through the bushes.","The moment I heard it, I immediately adjusted my grip on my weapon and went on alert.","After everything I’d been through, the reaction came naturally.","But all I continued to hear was rustling.","I gradually lowered my guard while staring in the direction the sound had come from.","’It’s coming from a little higher up rather than down below... A bird?’","But even if it was a bird, I couldn’t hear any wings flapping.","Puzzled, I returned to the cave.","Nothing else happened on the way back.","Splash! Splash!","Supply was gradually starting to exceed demand.","It looked like I needed to buy a larger steel drum.","Unless it rained again, if I didn’t have a container large enough to keep the fish alive, they would all end up rotting.","’This is a problem in its own way.’","The fish were too big.","Back when I was short on food, their enormous size had been a huge advantage.","But now that my food supply was relatively secure, I was gradually starting to see the drawbacks.","Even so, being able to eat my fill at every meal was too big an advantage to give up.","’It’s not like I can just stop collecting food, either.’","I had no idea when or how my food supply might run short, so it was better to keep stockpiling it just in case.","I watched the fish swimming comfortably inside the steel drum for a moment before moving on.","Breakfast was approaching, so I figured I should at least get some work done on the oven.","’But where should I put the oven?’","I suddenly ran into an unexpected problem.","Where would be the best place to install it?","If I built it inside the cave, I’d have to deal with the limited space and smoke.","If I built it outside, the weather would become a problem.","After thinking it over for a while, I decided to build it right against the cave entrance.","Of course, I didn’t forget to account for rain in the design.","’Once the oven is finished, I’ll put a waterproof tarp over it. I can angle the tarp so the rainwater runs toward the drainage ditch.’","If I wanted to put an entire fish inside, the oven would have to be quite large.","I opened the auction house and checked whether there were bricks of a suitable size.","Perhaps because bricks had been used since ancient times, there was quite a wide variety available.","’First, I need to level the ground.’","Apparently, even building a single oven required all sorts of preliminary work.","It looked like I’d have to settle for my usual breakfast today.","’I’ll just get the materials ready and call it there.’","A pile of bricks.","A waterproof tarp.","Poles to secure the tarp.","And so on.","I piled the necessary materials near the cave entrance and prepared breakfast.","Wonmo happened to wake up around then as well.","’I could put this metal plate inside the oven too.’","I had fish for breakfast as usual, then immediately began building the oven.","First, I leveled the ground as much as possible.","Then, taking the size of the fish into consideration, I began stacking the bricks one by one.","The important part was the chimney that would let the smoke escape.","I wasn’t trying to smoke the fish, so I made a proper passage for the smoke to vent through.","I designed it so the smoke could escape while minimizing the amount of rain that could get inside.","’And then... what did an oven look like again?’","Every now and then, I logged into the gallery to check what an oven’s structure was supposed to look like.","There were ovens available in the auction house, but they were expensive, and I had no idea whether any of them were large enough for what I wanted.","Besides, a rectangular shape with sharp corners suited my needs better than a round one.","It was easier to build too.","’Considering the size of the fish, I should make it pretty long.’","It didn’t need much height.","What it needed was depth.","Taking all of that into account, I even built a chimney at the very top.","Very nice.","’Perfect.’","I’d also bought the stone slab I installed inside from the auction house, so there was nothing to worry about there.","But I wasn’t completely finished yet.","I still needed the thing I’d asked the dwarf for.","He had said he would make it for me, but it seemed like I should measure the dimensions myself.","[Wild Grylls: (Photo of the entire oven) (Photo of the oven entrance being measured with a tape measure) This should be enough, right?]","[Passing Dwarf: You made it pretty neatly. Smear mud into the gaps between those bricks. That’ll keep the heat from leaking out and let the temperature rise better.]","[Wild Grylls: Nice tip. Thanks.]","Following the dwarf’s advice, I gathered some soil from the surrounding area and turned it into mud.","It felt a little dirty, but for the sake of the oven, I could put up with anything.","\"Kkyuu?\"","\"Daddy’s working.\"","Wonmo came over beside me, but I remained focused on building the oven.","Apparently curious about what I was doing, Wonmo plopped himself down and watched.","He was so adorable that I nearly scooped him up into a hug, but I somehow managed to restrain myself.","Only after I had finished applying all the mud was the job finally done.","Technically, I still needed to install the waterproof tarp before it was truly complete, but I could take my time with that.","\"Perfect. Absolutely perfect.\"","Looking at the completed oven brought a smile to my face.","Now I could post it on the gallery and show it off.","And when I opened the gallery—","[Eldorado Announces It Will Capture the Person Who Spread False Information Lmaooo]","A line I couldn’t simply ignore caught my eye.","For the record, it was a trending post.","Wondering what kind of idiots had said something like that, I opened it.","It could have just been bait or some baseless rumor, so I had to check.","Title) Eldorado Announces It Will Capture the Person Who Spread False Information Lmaooo","When they were asked how they planned to catch him, they said they’d do it through amicable discussions with the administrator.","But apparently the reporter uses the gallery too, because when they pointed out that Grylls is in the Forest of Four Seasons, Eldorado said it didn’t matter, lmao.","Even crazier, they apparently formed an entire tracking party just to capture Grylls, lmaooo.","What?","Are they going to supply me with survivors in the Forest of Four Seasons just for my sake?"]},{"title":"Chapter 101","paragraphs":["Firewood (4)","I was stunned by the shocking news, but only for a moment. I immediately left a comment.","The comment section was already a complete mess, but I couldn’t suppress my curiosity.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s that supposed to mean? Are they saying they’ll send survivors in there for me?","└ The man himself has arrived.","└ Grylls, you won’t have to be lonely anymore.","└ The Holy Kingdom is sending a search party just for you. Kekekeke.","└ The Holy Kingdom accomplishes what no one else could!","└ Wild Grylls: I can just dismiss that as bullshit, right? Damn it, they’re getting my hopes up for nothing.","└ Normally, you’d be terrified, but Grylls is actually looking forward to it. Kekekeke.","└ Considering he’s in the Forest of Four Seasons, that’s understandable. Kekeke.","└ But who exactly are they planning to send?","└ Rumor has it they’re sending people who oppose the current Pope’s regime.","└ So they’re just using this to eliminate their political enemies. Kek.","└ Do they even have the ability to find the head mod?","└ Absolutely not. Kekekeke. Unless the head mod openly gives them his location, it’s impossible.","└ Didn’t the head mod once tell them where the person planning to assassinate the emperor was?","└ Even then, the head mod only gave them the culprit’s location in real time. He didn’t reveal his own address.","└ And that head mod got his eyes gouged out for stalking someone. Kekekeke.","└ So they can send messages to the moderators?","└ Yeah, they can. Those bastards will definitely send one.","So it was all for show.","I had a rough idea of what they were trying to do.","I thought this sort of thing only happened on Earth, but since this world had the Gallery, events seemed to follow a similar pattern.","It was what people called a battle for public opinion. After all, the Gallery was practically the only place where public sentiment could be gauged.","’They just keep stepping on land mines.’","Naturally, public opinion toward the Holy Kingdom was as bad as it could possibly get.","There were occasionally people who defended or made excuses for it, but they were an exceedingly tiny minority.","All I had to do was sit back and enjoy the spectacle. The Holy Kingdom might declare the Gallery evil, but I wasn’t so sure that would work.","’Wasn’t the Emperor of the Central Plains beheaded after he tried to stop people from using the Gallery?’","It was a fairly famous incident—the assassination of the Emperor of the Central Plains.","It occasionally resurfaced as a hot topic, so I knew the story well.","The emperor tried to ban people from using the Gallery, only to be assassinated one day.","The imperial family officially announced that he had died of illness, while the people of the Central Plains assumed that he had fallen victim to an internal power struggle.","However, considering how ominously the Gallery users from the Central Plains had been behaving, most people on the Gallery didn’t believe either explanation.","’I’m sure they’ll handle it somehow.’","Whether Eldorado made another blunder or entered the Forest of Four Seasons was none of my concern.","The key was how the head mod—Don’tAbandonTheHero—would respond.","He could reveal my location in real time, and he could even impose penalties on them.","’The head mod told me not to worry, but judging from the Holy Kingdom’s behavior...’","Moreover, the head mod was presumed to be from the Holy Kingdom himself.","The fact that he was a devout apostle who worshiped the goddess Ares provided a clue to his origins.","Still, considering what a mess his country had become, hadn’t he probably lost whatever patriotism he once possessed?","The head mod worshiped his goddess. That didn’t necessarily mean he felt any loyalty toward Eldorado.","’I’ll have to wait and see how things unfold.’","It seemed the small ball I had set rolling had transformed into a massive meteor before crashing down.","Cleaning up the aftermath would take time. But if the Holy Kingdom continued stepping on land mines, the fire would never go out.","Until then, I could simply go about my business.","Title: I Made an Oven","Wild Grylls","(A photograph of a fairly well-made oven)","I made an oven out of bricks and clay. What do you think?","└ Heavenly Demon: That is quite a decent-looking oven. Are you planning to bake bread?","└ Wild Grylls: It’s meant for fish rather than bread. I think this will save me time.","└ Heavenly Demon: I wonder what oven-roasted fish tastes like.","└ Wild Grylls: Would you like me to give you some later?","└ Heavenly Demon: If you can spare a single piece.","└ SwordMaster: Weren’t you the one who said taking anything from him would be like squeezing blood from a stone? Kekekeke.","└ Heavenly Demon: I have realized that he is no stone.","└ SwordMaster: That excuse is pathetic. Kek.","└ Heavenly Demon: I can do something even more pathetic, if you wish.","└ SwordMaster: Ah. Come on, man...","└ Instantly subdued. Kekekeke.","└ Master, you know what to do if you think it’s unfair, right?","└ You merely need to turn blue as well.","└ SwordMaster: I’d rather die than become a junior mod.","└ Starlight Princess: Did you make that yourself? You did a wonderful job!","└ Wild Grylls: Thank you, hehe.","└ Starlight Princess: Now that you have an oven, you’ll be able to prepare many different dishes. Is there anything you have in mind?","└ Wild Grylls: I only have fish, though.","└ Starlight Princess: I could give you some flour. Would you like to try baking bread?","└ Wild Grylls: No, thank you. I don’t need to go that far.","Bread was a luxury.","Unless I grew wheat myself, it would be absurdly extravagant.","At most, I could use the oven to warm up smoked meat. That was essentially the extent of its usefulness.","As I had said earlier, the only reason I made the oven was to save time.","’Though even that will be difficult until the dwarf gives me the iron plate.’","He had said he would give it to me at lunchtime along with the barricade.","I could train until then.","This morning’s training would be swordsmanship practice.","Ding!","Just as I was about to close the Gallery, a notification sounded.","Gallery notifications appeared whenever someone commented on one of my posts or sent me a message.","If it had been a comment, I would have merely checked who had left it. This time, however, it was a message.","Thinking it might have come from the head mod, I immediately checked it.","[NecromancyIsLove: Are you the one who uploaded the final record of Rice Kraone?]","It was a username I had never seen before.","I raised an eyebrow as I read the message.","Come to think of it, if this person possessed authority similar to that of the head mod, there was no reason they would only be capable of messaging him.","They could send messages to me as well.","’The username is a little strange, though...’","At present, the Holy Kingdom was the only party likely to send me a message like this.","Curious about what kind of bullshit they would spout, I greeted them politely.","[Wild Grylls: If you’re asking whether I uploaded the book about the Immortal King, then yes.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Then you must also be the one who gave the book to Kadir.]","[Wild Grylls: Kadir? The Sorcerer King?]","Kadir, the Sorcerer King.","I had vaguely heard about him on the Gallery.","He was said to have gone beyond merely mastering every form of magic in the world and reached an understanding of the fundamental principles behind it.","He had joined the previous Hero in subjugating the Immortal King and had slain a dragon driven mad.","He was a truly legendary figure.","Some people said he had an eccentric side, though I didn’t know anything about that. In any case, he was famous.","’But the person I gave the book to was Allfather. No, before that...’","How did this person know that I had given the book to someone?","There were many things I didn’t understand, and the entire situation seemed suspicious.","Perhaps this user was merely fishing for information.","There was no need to answer carelessly.","[Wild Grylls: I’m afraid I don’t know what you mean.]","[NecromancyIsLove: There is no need to play dumb. We have already seen the book in Kadir’s hands.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you saying Allfather is Kadir?]","[NecromancyIsLove: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: Then who are you?]","[NecromancyIsLove: The Immortal King—no.]","NecromancyIsLove appeared to contemplate the matter for a moment before revealing his identity.","[NecromancyIsLove: We are Kazan Kraone III, the final king of the Kingdom of Balkan.]","[Wild Grylls: I heard the Immortal King was dead.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Our physical body has perished, but our soul remains. We are currently sealed inside Kadir’s refrigerator.]","[Wild Grylls: This is just role-playing, right?]","What kind of scam was he trying to—no, what kind of nonsense was he spouting?","The overwhelmingly powerful Immortal King had been sealed inside a refrigerator? Why didn’t he just say he was being aged in there like kimchi?","It seemed he had simply made a lucky guess about me giving the book to Allfather.","However, this user was apparently so committed to his role that he continued speaking without the slightest hesitation.","[NecromancyIsLove: Whether you believe us is your choice. That is not what matters to us.]","[Wild Grylls: Then what does?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We merely wished to express our gratitude. Whether you intended to or not, you vindicated our kingdom.]","It was rare for genuine emotion to come through in a message.","And right now, I could... not feel any sincerity at all.","I merely thought he had chosen an exceptionally strange role to play. Then again, there were plenty of strange people in the world.","Besides, I had heard that the Immortal King was undead. Could undead beings even use the Gallery?","Weren’t undead supposed to lack a sense of self?","Nothing about his story made any sense.","’It doesn’t matter even if Allfather really is Kadir.’","He was someone from a distant land who had nothing to do with me.","Even if I told anyone about this, no one would believe me.","He might as well have claimed that Heavenly Demon was the actual Heavenly Demon of the Central Plains.","It seemed best to humor him for now.","[NecromancyIsLove: Regrettably, that would be difficult, as we no longer possess a physical body.]","I knew it.","Not that I had expected anything from him.","I snorted and continued my conversation with NecromancyIsLove.","[Wild Grylls: Then tell me something that might help me. I’m curious how the person who wrote that book survived.]","[NecromancyIsLove: First, we shall tell you how our brother died.]","[Wild Grylls: You translated it?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We have not forgotten the kingdom from those impoverished yet joyful days. Nor could we forget its language.]","[Wild Grylls: I uploaded it because I wanted to obtain some information too, you know.]","[NecromancyIsLove: We see. Is there something you desire?]","[Wild Grylls: Come here and help me.]","Ah, yes. Of course.","What a unique character he was playing.","Still, it was fortunate that he claimed to know why the book’s owner had died.","Of course, there wasn’t the slightest shred of credibility to his story, so I intended to ask Allfather separately.","[NecromancyIsLove: Our brother, Rice Kraone, died from an infection.]","[Wild Grylls: An infection?]","[NecromancyIsLove: His wound gradually began to rot. Unable to endure the pain, he ultimately took his own life. That is what he wrote in his final entry.]","[Wild Grylls: What injured him?]","[NecromancyIsLove: He wrote that he was attacked by a group of gorilla-like apes.]","Gorillas...","Could they be the creatures living in that place?","I remembered hearing something resembling monkey cries when I traveled upriver.","It seemed Rice Kraone had encountered the creatures that lived there.","’That’s important information.’","I didn’t know how far he had explored, but it would probably be best to avoid that area if possible.","After all, I already suspected that there were several of those creatures rather than just one.","[Wild Grylls: Thank you for the useful information. That helped a little.]","[NecromancyIsLove: Ask us if there is anything else you wish to know. We shall take our leave now.]","[Wild Grylls: What are you going to do?]","[NecromancyIsLove: We intend to observe the world. Seeing it again after so long has left us with a peculiar feeling.]","He was just going to browse the Gallery. Did he really need to dress it up like that?","His commitment to the role was so unhinged that it nearly rivaled Heavenly Demon’s.","I ended the conversation there and immediately sent a message to another registered user.","[Wild Grylls: Allfather, may I ask you something?]","[Allfather: Go ahead.]","[Wild Grylls: A registered user told me earlier that you’re Kadir. You know, the Sorcerer King.]","[Allfather: Yes. That’s correct.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","Now I was the one caught off guard.","I had never expected him to admit it so readily.","[Allfather: Do you believe me?]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm... No?]","He had a point.","I accepted that answer immediately.","’I’ll just assume he’s another strange person.’","There was no reason to overcomplicate things.","***","Asella, the current Hero and head moderator of the Gallery, had found herself in a difficult situation.","It wasn’t because a search party was hot on her heels or because she had run out of money.","It was an extension of the enormous controversy that had spread beyond the Gallery and into the real world.","\"No message... has come at all.\"","Asella was waiting for a message from Eldorado, the Holy Kingdom.","Only registered users could send private messages.","Therefore, sending Asella a message would practically amount to admitting that they used the Gallery.","Fortunately, she hadn’t received any private messages so far...but that created a problem of its own.","’Does the Holy Kingdom... have no intention of resolving this?’","It would be a problem if a message arrived, but it would also be a problem if none came.","In the former case, they would be exposing their own guilt. In the latter, it would mean they had no intention of resolving the issue.","Either way, Asella couldn’t help but feel disappointed.","’If they do send me a message...’","Couldn’t she reveal that she was the Hero and gain an opportunity to clear up the misunderstanding?","The moment that thought occurred to her, Asella hurriedly shook her head.","As previously mentioned, she had a foolish side, but she wasn’t stupid.","Even if she cleared up the misunderstanding, Eldorado would undoubtedly attempt to exploit her position as the head moderator.","Among other things, they would pressure Grylls, the person who had released the information. In the worst-case scenario, they might even order her to permanently ban him.","That would be devastating for Grylls, whose chances of survival differed drastically depending on whether he had access to the Gallery.","’That... wouldn’t be right.’","The Gallery was a platform that everyone could use.","Even a nation had no right to regulate it recklessly. At least, that was what she believed.","However, the Holy Kingdom’s actions were completely at odds with Asella’s principles.","How could a nation blessed by the gods use those very blessings to commit such abuses?","’It would be better if...’","Asella closed the Gallery.","She could feel herself growing increasingly depressed.","’It would be better if they did nothing at all.’","Then, at least, she would be a little less disappointed."]},{"title":"Chapter 102","paragraphs":["Territory (1)","I set aside the rumor that Allfather was actually Kadir...and finished what I had to do.","The newbie(?) with the outrageous role-play had taken up some of my time, but it had only been ten minutes.","It hadn’t affected my overall schedule. It was no different from browsing the Gallery.","’Today is Day Thirteen. In two more days, it’ll be exactly half a month.’","Time seemed to pass slowly yet quickly at the same time.","It would have flown by if my daily routine had simply repeated itself, but I was currently going through all sorts of hardships.","’A little hardship is fine, but this is too much.’","Grumbling inwardly, I began my training.","After cultivating my internal energy, it was time for swordsmanship practice.","Two days from now, once I reached the half-month mark, I planned to consume the inner core.","I had already told Heavenly Demon about it, so she had given me a more in-depth explanation.","[Heavenly Demon: It seems you have laid a sufficient foundation. You truly possess extraordinary talent.]","[Wild Grylls: How long does it normally take to finish laying the foundation?]","[Heavenly Demon: The beginning is difficult in all things. The time required to sense the internal energy within one’s dantian differs from person to person. It takes between a week and half a month on average, yet you sensed it in only a single day. You can truly be called a genius.]","[Wild Grylls: You’re embarrassing me.]","[Heavenly Demon: This is not something to be embarrassed about, but something you should take pride in. This lady is also delighted to have the opportunity to teach someone as talented as you.]","Hmm. Now this was what a true adult looked like.","She didn’t envy the achievements of someone beneath her(?) and instead praised them sincerely.","This was why, even if I resented the heavens, I didn’t want to resent humanity.","There might be bad people in the world, but there were also kind people like Heavenly Demon.","Smiling happily, I sent Heavenly Demon another message.","[Wild Grylls: I wouldn’t have made it this far without you either, Heavenly Demon. The mnemonic chant you taught me has been especially helpful whenever I’ve been in danger.]","[Heavenly Demon: A carp living in a lake grows larger than one living in a pond. However, even a carp living in a lake gains nothing if it fails to survive.]","[Wild Grylls: You’re saying the Heavenly Demon Divine Art is the lake and I’m the carp, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: You understood immediately. How gratifying.]","The way she used poetic expressions confirmed that she was indeed fairly old.","She occasionally used strange expressions, but I could simply assume that the Gallery had corrupted her.","[Wild Grylls: When will you teach me the second mnemonic chant?]","[Heavenly Demon: You said you would consume the inner core soon, so I shall teach you then. If the first chant is about entrusting your body to the heavens, the second is about sensing the power of the heavens.]","[Wild Grylls: Entrusting myself to that power instead of controlling it?]","[Heavenly Demon: To control a power, you must first understand its true nature. Can you forcibly twist the course of a raging river?]","[Wild Grylls: That would be difficult.]","[Heavenly Demon: The heavens are no different. The closer you draw to them, the farther away they appear. This is a means of approaching the heavens, if only slightly.]","Her explanation was easy to understand.","I nodded as I listened to Heavenly Demon.","The eel I had eaten before.","I remembered all the side effects it had caused.","I had genuinely thought I was going to explode, but I had somehow managed to disperse its energy.","Perhaps consuming the inner core would proceed similarly.","It felt as though I had unintentionally studied the material in advance.","’That’s actually better.’","After receiving various pieces of fundamental knowledge from Heavenly Demon, I began circulating my internal energy.","As I gradually came to understand what the foundation entailed, the amount of time I spent cultivating also increased.","One might think the required time should decrease, but as Heavenly Demon had explained through her metaphor, the foundation was like a tree’s roots.","The deeper and wider the roots grew, the more water they required.","’The only way to increase its purity is to improve my lung capacity.’","That could only be achieved by continuously practicing my breathing.","My lung capacity would naturally increase while I cultivated my internal energy.","My goal was to breathe the same way I did while practicing my cultivation technique, even during my ordinary routine.","According to Heavenly Demon, this was less about laying a foundation and more about strengthening my roots.","In other words, I still had a very long way to go.","Nevertheless, it was entirely achievable if I put in the effort.","’Next is swordsmanship practice.’","Once I finished cultivating, it was time to practice swordsmanship.","I had been training step by step while following SwordMaster’s post, but there were parts where I had gotten stuck.","Other people claimed that merely reading the post was enough to turn anyone into a mass-produced(?) Swordmaster, but there was no one beside me to provide guidance.","Having a teacher was extremely important when learning something like martial arts. Since I was effectively trying to figure everything out from scratch, it was a little disheartening.","[SwordMaster: So, which part are you having trouble with?]","[Wild Grylls: It feels unstable. Like my sword keeps wavering?]","That was why I had decided to ask SwordMaster directly.","Previously, I could only ask questions by making a post, but now I could send private messages.","SwordMaster was just as excellent a teacher as Heavenly Demon, so I listened carefully.","[SwordMaster: I understand what you mean. However, that’s unavoidable as long as you wield your sword with one hand, Mr. Grylls. Naturally, using one hand is less stable than using both.]","[Wild Grylls: Is there no way to fix it?]","[SwordMaster: There are plenty of ways. One tip is to place the foot opposite your sword arm forward. Since you’re right-handed, Mr. Grylls, you should step forward with your left foot.]","[Wild Grylls: That’s what I’ve been doing.]","[SwordMaster: Were you doing it during training as well?]","[Wild Grylls: Oh.]","[SwordMaster: Here’s another tip: abandon the idea of cleaving your opponent in two. Stability is crucial when wielding a sword, but using it one-handed inevitably reduces stability while making you rely more heavily on brute force.]","[Wild Grylls: Are you saying I’ll eventually have to abandon my shield?]","[SwordMaster: That comes down to personal preference. You can compensate for the lack of cutting power with aura.]","[Wild Grylls: So practicing aura is ultimately my only path to survival.]","[SwordMaster: That’s right. If you work hard, your efforts will bear fruit someday. And one more tip—practice thrusting as much as possible!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you!]","[SwordMaster: Please hurry up, become a fine man, and marry me!]","[Wild Grylls: Teacher?]","Hearing a joke so completely at odds with her character left my mind reeling.","Come to think of it, I had been neglecting thrusts.","I had gained a great deal from this conversation.","Following SwordMaster’s advice, I began training my swordsmanship and aura.","The training focused on improving my lack of stability and compensating with aura for the weaknesses I couldn’t eliminate.","’I should practice thrusting too.’","In addition to practicing thrusts, I needed to gradually adjust my fighting style.","Until now, my strategy had been to wait for an opportunity, restrict my opponent’s mobility, and then slowly whittle away its stamina.","Since most of the monsters I encountered were enormous, the method had proven surprisingly effective.","However, it was only possible because I possessed the Heavenly Demon’s Sword, an absurdly overpowered item.","I also needed to consider how I would fight animals that weren’t particularly large.","’What would happen if a fight dragged on?’","That probably wouldn’t happen often, but who knew?","This was the Forest of Four Seasons.","I was probably vulnerable in prolonged battles. There weren’t exactly many opportunities to build endurance here.","My lung capacity had at least improved the more I practiced my cultivation technique, but I still couldn’t be certain.","There might be animals in the Forest of Four Seasons with greater lung capacity than mine.","\"...What are you doing?\"","\"Hoo.\"","When I asked Namu-Ppareumbo what it was doing, it exhaled deeply.","Rather than sighing, it seemed to be practicing its breathing.","The absurdity of it made me laugh.","Surely it wasn’t imitating the breathing method I had demonstrated before.","There was no way.","’I’d sooner believe that a gorilla had learned a breathing technique.’","A gorilla was an animal capable of literally tearing a person in half.","If an animal like that learned a breathing technique on top of its natural strength, it would be an unprecedented disaster.","Moreover, a breathing technique—or rather, an internal-energy cultivation technique—required a certain degree of intelligence.","Unless the Forest of Four Seasons had evolved its apes until they were as intelligent as humans, it would be difficult.","’Besides, no one would have taught them one in the first place.’","With that thought, I rose from my seat.","It was almost lunchtime.","Now that I had made the oven, I might as well use it. I could also collect the items from the dwarf.","\"Wonmo, let’s go.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","Wonmo happened to be awake, so I brought him along.","Naturally, I also carried Namu-Ppareumbo on my back.","I headed toward the river, eagerly wondering how many fish had been caught in the trap.","Splash! Splash!","\"Now that’s what I’m talking about.\"","There were two again.","I couldn’t have been happier.","I pulled in the trap while imagining the feast I would have for lunch.","Rustle!","As I was dragging the trap back, I heard something brush against the undergrowth.","The moment I heard it, I assumed a defensive stance just as I had that morning.","However, no other sound followed.","’Am I overreacting?’","Perhaps I had suffered so many attacks lately that I was beginning to hear things.","I rubbed my face before glancing at Wonmo.","Wonmo was staring fixedly at something—specifically, the upper branches of a tree.","\"Wonmo, was something there?\"","\"Kkyuu?\"","\"Never mind. Let’s go.\"","Worrying about it unnecessarily would only give me a headache.","Even if something launched a surprise attack, Namu-Ppareumbo was with me, so I felt somewhat reassured.","I placed the two fish caught in the trap inside the iron container and began preparing lunch.","[Passing Dwarf: Here’s the barricade and the tray you wanted. The tray is pretty heavy, so be careful.]","[Wild Grylls: Okay. I’ll give you some fish in a little while.]","[Passing Dwarf: My mouth is already watering. Kek.]","You too, huh?","Same here.","I installed the barricade I had received from the dwarf in the location I wanted.","Since my basic physical strength had increased tremendously, moving it wasn’t difficult.","Next was the appropriately sized steel tray.","I intended to place the fish on it before sliding it into the oven.","’He thoughtfully raised the edges so the oil wouldn’t spill.’","I repeatedly slid the tray into and out of the oven to test it.","Its weight was a slight drawback, but that was unavoidable.","Even so, it was excellent.","I could feel my quality of life gradually improving.","Crackle! Pop!","I lit a fire at the very bottom of the oven and slowly preheated it.","While the oven was heating, I prepared the fish. Using an oven didn’t change the preparation process itself.","However, I spread the fish open so it would cook evenly.","I didn’t forget to season it with salt either.","Slide—clunk!","Finally, all I had to do was place the fish inside the preheated oven.","The tray’s length and height fit perfectly.","The dwarf had given me an excellent gift.","’He said it would take around fifteen to twenty minutes, right?’","I could play with Wonmo until then.","It would also serve as training to improve Wonmo’s hunting skills.","Calling it training was a bit generous. All I had done was tie a rope to a branch and fasten a fish head to the other end.","It was more like playing with a cat.","The commonality was that they were both adorable.","This exercise might also help improve my reaction speed, even if only slightly.","\"Kkyuu! Kkyuuuu!\"","\"That’s it! Good job!\"","While the fish inside the oven cooked, Namu-Ppareumbo merely stared blankly at the trees.","Rustle!","Rustle! Swish!","Several beasts swiftly made their way through the trees.","Rather than traveling beneath them, they moved rapidly by lightly stepping from branch to branch.","At first glance, their bodies resembled those of humans. However, their long arms and the fur covering their entire bodies made it clear that they were not.","The beasts sped through the forest faster than any human could and eventually arrived in a particular area.","There, they found an ape lounging leisurely atop a tree.","Its overall appearance resembled a gorilla, but there was something unusual about its presence.","\"Ooh! Ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","The group of gorillas that had gone out to scout(?) began hooting as though they were reporting something.","The gorilla that had been lounging in the tree slowly rose.","Unlike its previously relaxed demeanor, its expression had turned deathly serious.","\"Ooh?\"","\"Ooh-ooh-ooh!\"","\"Ooh...!\"","A subtle breeze began to blow through the forest."]}]);
